TOMATO PATTERN BY: ANNIEGURUMI
Skill Level: Beginner to Intermediate
Materials:
Pillar Red Cotton Aran Yarn
Evergreen Cotton Aran Yarn (or scrap green yarn)
3.25mm Crochet Hook
2 amigurumi/safety eyes (6mm)
2 pink brads (9mm) or use scrap pink yarn to make blusher
Polyfill
Tapestry Needle
Black Crochet Thread (I used DMC Embroidery Thread)
Stitches: (US Crochet Terms)
MR: magic ring
ch: chain
sl st: slip stitch
sc: single crochet
inv dec: invisible decrease
BLO: back loop only
FO: Fasten Off
Tomato Body:
Using Pillar Red Yarn:
R1: 6sc in MR (6)
R2: 2 sc in each (12)
R3: (2sc in next, sc in next) repeat (18)
R4: (2sc in next, sc in next 2 stitches) repeat (24)
R5: (2sc in next, sc in next 3 stitches) repeat (30)
R6: (2sc in next, sc in next 4 stitches) repeat (36)
R7: (2sc in next, sc in next 5 stitches) repeat (42)
R8: (2sc in next, sc in next 6 stitches) repeat (48)
R9-15: sc around (7 rounds)
*add eyes between R12-13; 5 stitches apart
*glue brads around R14 & one stitch outside the
eyes.
!2
TOMATO PATTERN BY: ANNIEGURUMI
R16: (inv dec, sc in next 6 stitches) repeat (42)
R17: (inv dec, sc in next 5 stitches) repeat (36)
R18: (inv dec, sc in next 4 stitches) repeat (30) *start stuffing
R19: (inv dec, sc in next 3 stitches) repeat (24)
R20: (inv dec, sc in next 2 stitches) repeat (18)
*Stuff firmly
R21: (inv dec, sc in next) repeat (12)
R22: inv dec around (6) FO & sew in ends.
Green “petals”:
Using Evergreen Yarn:
R1: 6sc in MR (6)
R2: 2 sc in each (12)
R3: (2sc in next, sc in next) repeat (18)
!3
TOMATO PATTERN BY: ANNIEGURUMI
first picture: chains and starting BLO second pic: sc BLO
R4:
sc next 2 st, ch 7, sc BLO from the second ch from hook (6 total sc);
sc next 2, ch 6, sc BLO from the second ch from hook (total 5 sc);
sc next 2, ch 7, sc BLO from the second ch from hook (total 6 sc);
sc next 2, ch 6, sc BLO from the second ch from hook (total 5 sc);
sc next 2, ch 8, sc BLO from the second ch from hook (total 7 sc);
sc next 2, ch 6, sc BLO from the second ch from hook (total 5 sc);
sl st to first stitch.
FO leaving long tail for sewing later. Pinch the points to make it look more sharp. (6 petals)
!4
TOMATO PATTERN BY: ANNIEGURUMI
Stem:
Using Evergreen Yarn:
ch 5, sc BLO second ch from hook and every st across. (4sc total)
FO, leaving long tail for sewing.
Assembly:
Attach petals using several back
stitches to secure in place. Be sure to
leave some of the tips free so they
stand up a bit.
Sew the stem onto the top.
embroider a smile with black crochet
thread.
Weave in all ends.
Don’t forget to add a note that you
love the person “from my head
TOMATOES”! :)
If you enjoyed this pattern, please
check out my etsy shop and love
crochet. I always post my patterns
there and hope you like them.
Hope you enjoy my pattern! Thank
you very much for your support. :)
