Yarnstructions || Natascha Kuipers;https://www.lovecrafts.com/en-gb/p/3d-heart-crochet-pattern-by-yarnstructions;"abbreviations are stated in parentheses.
• Single crochet (sc) • Increase (inc) • Continuous rounds
• Magic circle (mc) • Decrease (dec)
Page 2 of 4
Measurements
When using the yarn and crochet hook as stated above the heart is about 3cm or 1 3/16”.
When using a different yarn than stated in the list of materials please use the recommended hook
size. This information can be found on the yarn label. I recommended going down 1 hook size for
amigurumi. As you want your stitches to be nice and tight.
They are only suggestions to get as close as possible to the identical result. Be sure to use yarn that
you enjoy to crochet with and a crochet hook that suits your grip type and thread tension. Please note
that the dimensions may differ from person to person and also when using different yarns and/or
hook.
Contact
Have remarks/questions about this pattern? Send an email to: contact@yarnstructions.com
Enjoy your project!
How to read this pattern?
Each pattern will differ just slightly from others in the way that the crochet instructions are written
down. In this pattern the following format of stitches is used:
2sc = crochet a single crochet in the first stitch and another single crochet in the next stitch.
2inc = crochet an increase in the first stitch and another increase in the next stitch.
Then, the round (and rows) are constructed as follows:
4. (2sc, inc) x 3 [12]
This means that round (or row) 4 is crocheted by 3 repeats of the stitches mentioned between
parentheses (...). The parentheses provide a condensed format to the instructions. If you would fully
write out this round it would say this:
4. 2sc, inc, 2sc, inc, 2sc, inc [12]
The number between square brackets [...] at the end of each instruction shows the total stitch count
in the round after that round is finished. In this example it tells that round 4 will have a total of 12
stitches. You can use this number to do regular checks if you are on the right track.
Page 3 of 4
Part 1
Crochet in continuous rounds.
1. 5sc in mc [5]
2. (inc) x 5, [10]
3. 10sc [10]
Fasten off and hide yarn tail.
Part 2
Crochet in continuous rounds.
1. 5sc in mc [5]
2. (inc) x 5, [10]
3. 10sc [10]
4. Hold part 1 against part 2 and do 1 sc through both parts,
this sc does not count towards the total, since we will not
crochet over this stitch again.
Continue crocheting around part 2: 9sc.
Now continue onto and around part 1: 9sc [18]
5. 3sc, dec, 7sc, dec, 4sc [16]
6. 3sc, dec, 6sc, dec, 3sc [14]
7. dec, 3sc, (dec) x 2, 3sc, dec [10]
Start to stuff firmly.
8. dec, 3sc, dec, 3sc [8]
Stuff firmly.
9. dec, 2sc, dec, 2sc [6]
Stuff more if possible. Fasten off and hide yarn tail.
Enjoy your project!
Enjoy! When you have finished your project or if you are still
working on it don’t forget to me on Instagram ""
(@Yarnstructions).
