AMIGURUMI PATTERN;https://www.lovecrafts.com/en-gb/p/alice-in-wonderland-amigurumi-crochet-pattern-by-monchou-designs;;"AMIGURUMI PATTERN
“Curiouser and curiouser...”
Alice is worked in worsted and light weight
yarns and has wired limbs to help her make
her way down the rabbit hole and through
Wonderland.
Finished Size: 7 inches tall
Notions:
Level: Advanced Beginner/Intermediate
Size E (3.5 mm) and size F (3.75mm) crochet
Skills: crochet, basic hand sewing, glueing
hook
Stitch markers
Sewing needle & thread (black and white)
Materials:
Craft glue
Skin: Patons Astra Light Yarn - Apricot (A) - 7 metres 2 x 6mm black safety eyes
Clothing and Hair: Worsted weights 4” dowel rod (approx 1/4” diameter)
Blue (B) - 10 metres Polyester stuffing
White (C) - 10 metres 16 gauge wire - found at hardware stores
Black (D) - 3 metres Wire cutters
Yellow (E) - 8 metres Scraps of pink or red and brown embroidery floss
Pattern Notes:
• This amigurumi pattern is crocheted in the round, beginning at the crown of the head and
ending at the shoe. The soles of the shoe and the arms are sewn on separately.
• Some sections are worked in rows and some sections are worked in rounds (either joined or
continuous) - please check the individual instructions for each section.
• A stitch marker is recommended to mark the start of each round.
• Maintain strong tension as you work to keep your stitches tight.
• After finishing off, hide yarn ends by pulling them to the inside of the doll.
Key: (US crochet terms) Hdc2tog: half double crochet 2 sts together
ch: chain BLO: crochet into the back loop only
sc: single crochet sl st: slip stitch
hdc: half double crochet Rep: repeat
sc2tog: single crochet 2 sts together Rnd: round
Instructions
Head: Starting with apricot yarn (A) and 3.5mm hook:
Rnd # Details Total # of sts
1 Beginning at top of head, make an adjustable ring, ch 1, sc 6 into the ring. Pull closed. (6)
2 Work 2 sc into each st. (12)
*insert a stitch marker to keep track of the row starting spot, move marker up after each rnd
3 *(2sc into next st, sc into next st), rep from * to end of rnd. (18)
4 *(sc into next 5 sts, 2sc into next st), rep from * to end of rnd. (21)
5-8 Sc in each st around. (21)
9 Sc into next 4 sts, sc2tog, sc into next 9 sts, sc2tog, sc into next 4 sts. (19)
10 Sc into each st around. (19)
Using a needle and black thread embroider
eyelashes between rounds 7 and 8, between
stitches 10 and 11, and the other between
stitches 12 and 13. After embroidering the
lashes, insert safety eyes.
2
11 Sc into next 3 sts, sc2tog, sc into next 4 sts, sc2tog, sc into next 4 sts, sc2tog, sc into (16)
next 2 sts.
12 Sc into first st. * (sc2tog, sc into next st), rep from * to end of rnd. (11)
Pause and insert stuffing firmly into head.
13 Sc2tog 3 times, sc into next st, sc2tog two times. (6)
14-15 Sc into each st. (6)
Switch to blue yarn (B)
16 Using 3.75mm hook for this rnd only: sl st into each st around. (6)
17 Switch back to 3.5mm hook: 2sc BLO into each st. (12)
18 *(sc into next st, 2 sc into next st) rep from * to end of round. (18)
If you’re not at the middle of the back of the doll, sc to the centre back. Continue to
move your stitch marker down to keep track of where your round ends.
19 *(sc into next 5 sts, 2 sc into next st) rep from * to end of rnd. (21)
20-23 Sc into each st around. (21)
Pause and insert the dowel through the neck into the head.
Place stuffing in the body around the dowel so that it rests in the centre of the body.
24 *(sc into next st, sc2tog) rep from * to end of rnd. (14)
25-26 Sc into each st. (14)
27 Sc BLO into each st. (14)
28 Sc into each st. (14)
29 Sc into next 3 sts, 2sc into next st, sc into next 2 sts, 2 sc into next st, sc into next 3 sts, (18)
2sc into next st, sc into next 2 sts, 2sc into next st.
30-32 Sc into each st around. (18)
Now you’ll divide the torso and just be working on one leg.
Make sure you’re at the centre back to begin the next rnd.
33 Sc into next 9 sts, skip 9 sts, sc 1 into next st. This is the first st of rnd 34. (9)
3
Switch to white yarn (C)
34-44 Sc into each st, loosely adding stuffing as you go. (9)
45 Sc2tog, then sc into each st to the end of round. (8)
46-49 Sc into each st. (8)
50 Sc2tog, sc into each st to the end of round. (7)
Make sure you’re at the centre of the back of the leg.
51 Sc into next 3 sts, 3 hdc in next st, sc in next 3 sts. (9)
52 Sc into next 4 sts, 3 hdc in next st, sc in next 4 sts. (11)
Switch to black yarn (D)
53 Sl st into each st around. (11)
54 Sc into next 5 sts, 3 hdc in next st, sc in next 5 sts, fasten off. (13)
33 Second leg: Using blue yarn (B): Join yarn at 16th st of rnd 32 with a sc,
and sc into next 8 sts around the opening. (9)
Switch to white yarn (C)
Repeat rnds 34-54
Finish loosely stuffing both legs.
Inserting the wire:
The wire makes your doll posable and also gives it the stiffness it
needs to stand. Cut a 10 inch length of wire, and twist one end to
make a half-inch loop. This prevents a sharp end from poking out
through the end of the shoe.
4
Gently insert the sharp end of the wire up the leg through the
opening at the bottom. As you get to the top of the leg, spread the
doll’s legs (as if she’s doing the splits) and continue pushing the
wire, very gently as it’s going through the stuffing and you’re trying
not to shift it, and out through the bottom of the other leg.
Bend the legs into place, and make a loop at the other end of the
wire and bend both wire loops to a 90 degree angle so that the
ends rest inside the feet. Leave the remaining area at the bottom
of the foot unstuffed, as this will help the doll to stand.
Bottom of shoe (make 2) - Using black yarn (D):
Row # Details Total # of sts
1 Make an adjustable ring, ch 1, sc 5 into the ring, pull closed, sl st into first st, ch 1, (5)
turn.
2 Sc BLO into next 2 sts, ch 1, turn. (2)
3-4 Sc into next 2 sts, ch 1, turn. (2)
5 Sc2tog, fasten off.
Position the sole at the bottom of the shoe with
the adjustable ring portion as the heel and the
pointed end as the toe, with the right side of the
adjustable ring facing outward. Stitch in place
using a needle and thread.
5
Collar Trim - using blue yarn (B)
Row # Details
1
Starting in st 4 of rnd 16 (the rnd of blue sl sts on the neck), insert hook the
1
front loop and make 2sc, then work 2sc into each st around, ending at st 3 at
the front, ch 1, turn. (12)
2
*(sc into next st, 2sc into next st) rep from * to end of row, fasten off. (18)
2
Arms (make two) - starting with blue yarn (B):
Rnd # Details Total # of sts
Ch 7 and join with a sl st to make a circle.
1 Sc into each st. (7)
2 Work 2sc into each st. (14)
3 Sc into each st around. (14)
4 Sc into next 3 sts, skip over next 2 sts, sc into next 2 sts, skip over next 2 sts, sc into (10)
next 5 sts.
5 Skip over first 2 sts, sc into next 3 sts, skip over next 2 sts, sc into next 3 sts. (6)
Switch to apricot yarn (A)
6 Sc BLO into each st around. (6)
7-13 Sc into each st around. (6)
Tip: for assistance with the hands see this video:
https://youtu.be/rko-34B_XUs
Sl st into first st. Ch 3, sl st into second ch from hook, sl st into next
14
ch, sc into same st that you made the ch from, sl st into next st. This
creates the thumb.
6
Ch 4. Sl st into second ch from hook and next 2 chs. Insert hook into
the same st you made the ch in, and then insert it through to the
sixth st on the round, coming in from the back. Pull yarn through to
make a sl st. (Index finger)
Ch 4. Sl st into second ch from hook and next 2 chs. Insert hook into
same st you made the ch in, through the back of the corresponding
st on the other side (the 5th st on the rnd). pull yarn through into a sl
st. (Middle finger)
Ch 4. Sl st into second ch from hook and next 2 chs. Insert hook into
the next st and then insert it through to the corresponding st behind,
coming in from the back. Pull yarn through to make a sl st. (Ring
finger)
Ch 3. Sl st into second ch from hook, sl st into next ch. Sl st into
same st you began the ch from, then sl st into the post directly
below that st in the previous rnd. (Baby finger)
Fasten off.
Sleeve Trim
Using blue yarn (B), insert hook into the front loop of st 6 in rnd 6 (the
BLO rnd), sc into the front loop of each st around, join to first st in
rnd and fasten off. (6)
