Attaching arms to body:
Cut an 8-inch length of wire. Using the wire cutters to grip one
end, twist the end into a small loop, and insert that end into one
of the arms. The end of the wire should rest at the wrist and not
go all the way into the hand, where it could poke out. Gently
add stuffing around the wire to the upper arm, being careful not
to overstuff. Very little stuffing is needed in the arms.
Next, insert the other end of the wire through the shoulder area and through the body, coming out
on the other side in the corresponding st. Twist the remaining end of the wire into a loop and then
insert into the remaining arm. Using a needle and thread stitch the arms to the body.
8
Shoe Straps:
Using a piece of black yarn and a yarn needle, make a stitch across each
foot as shown.
Apron - Using white yarn (C)
Row # Total # of sts
1 Ch 45, fasten off. (45)
2 Find stitch 20 on the chain, and sc into it and the next 5 sts, ch 1, turn. (6)
3 *(2 sc into next st, sc into next st), rep from * to end of row, ch 1, turn. (9)
4-5 Sc into each st, ch 1, turn. (9)
6 *(2 sc into next st, sc into next 2 sts), rep from * to end of rnd, ch 1, turn. (12)
7-9 Sc into each st, ch 1, turn. (12)
10 *(2 sc into next st, sc into next 3 sts), rep from * to end of rnd, ch 1, turn. (15)
11-12 Sc into each st, ch 1, turn. Fasten off after row 12. (15)
Apron Bib - Using white yarn (C)
Row # Total # of sts
1 Insert your hook and make a sc in the top loop of st 21 of the ch (1 st in from where
you started the apron portion), sc into next 3 sts, ch 1, turn. (4)
2 2sc into next st, sc into next 2 sts, 2sc into next st, ch 1, turn. (6)
3 Sc into each st, ch 1, turn. (6)
4 2sc into next st, sc into next 4 sts, 2sc into next st, ch 1, turn. (8)
5-6 Sc into each st, ch 1, turn. (8)
7 Sc into next 3 sts, ch 1, turn. (3)
8 Sc2tog, sc into next st, ch 1, turn. (2)
9 Sc into each st, ch 1, turn. (2)
10 Sc2tog, ch 1, turn. (1)
11 Sc, ch 13, fasten off.
9
Next, insert your hook into the first st at the other end of row 6 and make a
sc, and then sc into the next 2 sts, ch 1, turn.
Repeat the steps above for rows 8-11, but don’t fasten off after making the
chain.
Starting in the 2nd stitch from your hook, sl st into each ch,
working back toward the bib of the apron. Continue to sl st
down the side edge of the bib, the edges of the apron skirt and
back up the other side to the other chain at the top of the bib.
Continue to sl st into each ch. When you get to the end of the
chain, continue to sl st around into the loops on the ‘bottom’ of
the chain, making a row of slip stitches on both sides of it.
Continue to slip stitch along the neckline of the bib, and up the
remaining chain to where you started, and fasten off.
Place the apron on the doll and tie the chains in a bow at the waist. Bring
the top ties over the shoulders and cross them in the back and then tie or
sew them to the waist tie as shown.
Hair Cap - Using yellow yarn (E)
Rnd # Total # of sts
1 Make an adjustable ring, ch 1, and sc 6 into the ring. Pull closed. (6)
2 2sc into each st around. (12)
3 *(2 sc into next st, sc into next st), rep from * to end of rnd. (18)
4 *(sc into next 5 sts, 2sc into next st), rep from * to end of rnd. (21)
5-7 Sc in each st around, fasten off after rnd 7. (21)
10
Position the hair cap on the head as shown and stitch in place.
Ear (make 2)
Using apricot yarn (A) make an adjustable ring. Ch 1, sc 2 into ring. Pull
tail to close ring and fasten off.
Position the ear on the side of the head, slightly overlapping the hair
cap. Stitch in place using a needle and thread.
Hair (make 2 sets) - Using yellow yarn (E)
Row # Total # of sts
1 Ch 15, and then starting in 2nd ch from hook, 2sc into next 4 sts, sc into (18)
next 10 sts, do not fasten off.
2 Repeat row 1. (18)
3-4 Ch 17, and then starting 2nd ch from hook, 2sc into next 4 sts, sc into next (20)
12 sts, do not fasten off.
5-6 Repeat row 1. (18)
7-8 Ch 11, and then starting 2nd ch from hook, 2sc into next 3 sts, sc into next
4 sts. Fasten off after row 8. (13)
11
Attaching the Hair to the Head:
Lay each piece along the top of the head as shown, with the top edges
of the two hairpieces meeting to form the centre part. The longer
strands of hair go at the front of the head, and the shorter strands go at
the back. Secure with pins and then use a needle and thread to stitch
them in palace.
Next, use the needle and thread to stitch down the hair strands on the
head. It isn’t necessary to stitch along the entire length of every piece,
rather just here and there enough to hold it in place on the hair cap.
Hair Ribbon:
Using black yarn (D), ch 40, fasten off and weave in ends. Tie in place
with a bow as shown.
Face:
Eyebrows: Cut two pieces of brown embroidery floss about 1/4 inch in
length. Glue them in place above the eyes using craft glue.
Nose: using a piece of apricot yarn and a yarn needle, make a few
stitches centred below the eyes as shown.
Mouth/lips: Cut two pieces of pink or red embroidery floss about 5/8
inch long and glue in place.
