Beaver Amigurumi
This sheep is pretty easy to make. The pattern uses single crochets. Perfect as
a little gift or just as a decoration!
Stitches
Decrease
For the decreases, I recommend the ‘one front loop, one back loop’ method.
Sheep
Pick up the front loop of the first stitch, and the back loop of the second stitch,
so you now have three loops on your needle, like in the picture. Yarn over and
pull through all three loops. This gives the most invisible decrease.
Increase
For the increases, just crochet two single crochets in the same stitch.
Materials needed Colour change (if you want to use it)
● Crochet needle: size 2 If you want a smooth colour change, loop in the new colour as such:
● Grey yarn and black yarn: when you reach the place where you want to change colour, pull a loop of the
Sport / 5 ply. I recommend new colour through the loop already on your needle. then pick up the next
100% mercerized cotton. In the stitch, yarn over with your new color and pull through(so you now have two
pictures, I’ve used Catania. the loops of the same colour on your needle). then yarn over again and finish the
cotton gives it a smooth look, stitch.
but you could also use a more
woolly yarn for a fluffy look.
● An embroidery needle
● polyfill
