1st photo on the left above: Eyes have been attached and the head has been firmly filled.
As for the 2nd photo on the right above: I will explain how to start embroidering his eye brows & nose.
I’ve got a little amount of Natura Just Cotton in Blue Paradise colour in my yarn box which I’ve used to embroider the facial parts of the bunny.
Having said that you can of course use any brand of cotton in any colour, or you can even use a piece of aran yarn for that matter. It’s totally up to
you.
I’ve cut a 60 cm long cotton piece & threaded onto yarn needle, inserted into the bunny’s head from the bottom open end and left a little yarn tail
out for fastening later once the eye brows & the nose are embroidered.
Page Four
Copyright © Tatie Soft Toys 2017
So, you’ve now inserted the yarn needle inside the bunny’s head. Bring the needle out from the second hole next to his right eye as you can see in
the photo left above. Count 4 holes up from where you inserted the needle and, make his eye brow tilted to the right as you see in the photo left
above. His right eye brow is done.
When you inserted the needle to finish his right eye brow, bring the needle out between his two eyes to embroider his nose. Use 5 holes to make his
nose, finish his nose by going in and out of the 5 holes four times, then insert the needle in the 3rd hole of the 5 holes that are used to make the
nose. And then c ount down 5 holes & insert the needle into the 5th hole to embroider his mouth.
When you insert the needle to finish his mouth, bring the needle up to embroider his left eye brow, as you see in the photo left above. And then, once
his left eye brow is done bring the needle out of the open end of his head. You now have two little yarn tails coming out of the open end of his head.
Grab those two yarn ends and make two knots to secure his facial parts and cut the excessive yarn ends with your trimming scissors.
His head is done as you see in the photo left below.
