Hat Step Seven
Colour Silver Blue
H at is crocheted in joined rounds. I prefer to use a smaller hook to crochet slip st & ch one stitches to join the rounds as I get smaller & less visible
joining stitches.
I am using 3.50m m hook to crochet the hat and 2.00mm hook to crochet the joining stitches which are sl st & ch 1.
After sl st, ch 1, change your hook to 3.50mm & work first sc st into the same st as sl st. Then carry on crocheting and after the last sc of the round
change your hook to 2.00mm to crochet the sl st & ch 1
Sl st and ch one stitches are not included in the stitch numbers that are given in the brackets.
1: 6 sc into magic ring, sl st, ch 1 [6 sts]
2: *inc* rep 6 ti mes, sl st, ch 1 [12 sts]
3: *sc, inc* rep 6 times, sl st, ch 1 [18 sts]
4: Back Loops O nly sc around, sl st, ch 1 [18 sts]
5-8: Sc around ( 4 rounds in total ), remember to finish with sl st and ch 1 [18 sts]
9: *inc* rep 18 t imes, sl st, ch 1 [36 sts]
10: Sc around [3 6 sts] slip st into first sc to finish.
Put a little bit of stuffing into the hat. Leave a long enough yarn tail for sewing.
