Neck Warmer Step Eight
Colour Beige
Neck warmer is crocheted with 4.00mm hook. Chain stitch and double crochet stitches are used.
Leave a tiny yarn tail, chain 35, turn the back side of the chain where you will see stitches look like the runner stitches which we are going to use to
crochet our dc sts. Why use back sts of the chain? Because, once the neck warmer is completed top and the bottom edges will look the same, you’ll
get *v* shapes stitches both on the top and bottom edges of the neck warmer which make your work nice & tidy.
Double crochet into the 4th back st of the chain from the hook. Dc all the way to the end of the ch. [32 dc sts]
Leave little yarn tail to sew the button on.
Get a little button in either silver blue or beige and sew the button on the 31st dc st. Fasten off by making two knots with the two yarn tails you have. I
had a little beige button in my button jar, so I used beige. Wrap the neck warmer around his neck. I like the button at the back of his neck.
Back side of the chain and back stitch is pointed out with the pink yarn needle.
Neck warmer from the front Neck warmer from the back
