Amigurumi Christmas Tree
ABOUT THE PATTERN
This simple tree is the perfect project for those last minute Christmas gifts. Made with simple
stitches and cool techniques, this little Christmas tree is bound to be your new holiday trinket
staple!
ABOUT THE AUTHOR
Shannen is the owner and designer behind Sweet N’ Cute Creations. Just recently, she released
her very first book, Huggable Amigurumi, which features 18 adorably cute animals. She has
been featured in other publications such as Zoomigurumi 2, Animals-At-Work, Inside Crochet
Magazine, Mollie Makes, and We Love Amigurumi.
To order her book, head on over to bit.ly/huggableamigurumi or head on over to your local
bookstores or craft stores.
USAGE
This is a free pattern from Sweet N’ Cute Creations. This pattern should not be sold for profit or
plagiarised. Any products made from this pattern may be sold provided that it be credited to
this pattern.
MATERIALS STITCHES/TECHNIQUES USED
Lilies and Cream in Light Lime magic ring
4 Ply High Bulk Acrylic Yarn in Brown and chain (ch)
Yellow Gold single crochet (sc)
crochet hook F slip stitch (ss)
tapestry needle half double crochet (hdc)
stitch markers - to mark the start of every double crochet (dc)
row! front loop only (flo)
fiberfill stuffing back loop only (blo)
PATTERN
TREE - USING THE GREEN AND F HOOK,
create a magic ring
rnd 1: make 5 sc [5]
rnd 2: sc all around [5]
rnd 3: inc 5 8mes [10]
rnd 4: through FLO, (3hdc in next st, sl st in st aBer) 5 8mes;
through BLO of the same row, sc all around [10]
rnd 5: (sc in next st, inc in st aBer) 5 8mes [15]
rnd 6: sc all around [15]
rnd 7: through FLO, (3hdc in next st, sk, sl st in st aBer) 5 8mes;
through BLO of the same row, (sc in each of the next 2 st, inc in st aBer) 5 8mes [20]
rnd 8: sc all around [20]
rnd 9: (sc in each of the next 3 st, inc in st aBer) 5 8mes [25]
rnd 10: through FLO, (3dc in next st, sl st in st aBer) 8 8mes, sl st in next st;
through BLO of the same row, sc all around [25]
rnd 11: sc all around [25]
rnd 12: (sc in each of the next 4 st, inc in st aBer) 5 8mes [30]
rnd 13: through BLO (sc in each of the next 3 st, dec) 6 8mes [24]
rnd 14: (sc in each of the next 2 st, dec) 6 8mes [18]
rnd 15: (sc in next st, dec) 6 8mes [12]
rnd 16: (sc next st, dec) 4 8mes [8]
fasten off leaving a long tail for sewing
CROCHETING THROUGH BOTH THE FRONT AND BACK LOOPS IN ONE ROW CREATES THE EFFECT ABOVE. IT
MAKES FOR THE RUFFLES WITHOUT HAVING TO SEW IT!
TRUNK - USING BROWN AND F HOOK,
CREATE A MAGIC RING
rnd 1: make 4 sc [4]
rnd 2: inc 4 8mes [8]
rnd 3: through BLO, sc all around [8]
rnd 4-5: sc all around [8]
fasten off leaving a long tail for sewing
STAR - USING YELLOW GOLD AND F HOOK,
CREATE A MAGIC RING:
make an (hdc, ch, hdc, ss) 5 8mes in the magic ring; then fasten off leaving a 5 inch tail for sewing
ASSEMBLY
1. Sew the star to the tip of the tree
2. stuff the tree and the trunk
3. weave in the ends of the tree, tighten, and fasten
4. sew the trunk onto the bottom of the tree
5. et voila, your little tree is finished!";Lovecrafts
