Easter Egg Bunny
With Easter right around the corner, these little trinkets are the perfect whips that will make your
easter egg fun hunt the best in the land! Make these cuties in different colors for added fun!
Don’t forget to tag me on instagram or post it to my Facebook wall so we can all see the adorable
easter egg bunnies that you have made!
MATERIALS
✴mercerized cotton thread:
★for the egg: any multi-colored one
★for the bunny: one cream as main color, any pastel color for the contrasting color
✴steel hook 6 (1.6mm)
✴stitch market
✴tapestry needle
✴fiberfill stuffing
PATTERN
Bunny Ears
Ch 10, hdc in 3st from hook and in each ch until the start of the foundation ch
Using the other side of the foundation ch, make 2 hdc in the first st, and hdc in each of the st until
you reach the end of the foundation chain. Slst to the first hdc of the round.
Fasten off leaving a long tail for sewing the ears to the egg
Egg
Rnd 1: magic ring, make 5 sc [5]
Rnd 2: inc 5 times [10]
Rnd 3: (sc in next st, inc in st after), repeat 5 times [15]
Rnd 4: sc all around [20]
Rnd 5: (sc in each of the next 2 st, inc in st after), repeat 5 times [20]
Rnd 6: sc all around [20]
Rnd 7: (sc in each of the next 3 st, inc in st after), repeat 5 times [25]
Rnd 8-12: sc all around [25]
---- if you’re making it into a bunny, sew on the ears by this portion. The ears must start from the
3rd round all the way to 7 round in a diagonal manner as seen in the photo —
Rnd 13: (sc in each of the next 3 st, dec) repeat 5
times [20]
--- start stuffing here ---
Rnd 14: (sc in each of the next 2 st, dec), repeat
5 times [15]
Rnd 15: (sc in next st, dec), repeat 5 times [10]
Rnd 16: sc in every other st [5]
Fully stuff the egg
Fasten off and weave in all ends";Lovecrafts
