http://sewing.about.com/od/bowsandribbonshowtos/ss/tiebow.htm
c.sew on the straps to the dress
please refer to the picture
9. sew the feet [booties] to the main part of the french maid outfit - just where the
skirt “drapes”
10.place the outfit on the minion
11. after placing the outfit on, sew on the arms to their respective spaces from the outfit
a. for the right arm, sew the ends together to create a flat top and directly sew it on
to the body
b. for the left arm, just sew it as is
12.position the lace headband on the minion’s head. for additional placement, sew it to
the goggles as well.
13.this is optional: get a small duster or props to complete the look for your minion
8
4
this part is completely optional
you may choose to make one, buy one, or simply not use
one....it’s all up to your creativity
since rice husks are not available in all countries, i will sub-
duster
stitute [in this pattern] some of the materials
materials:
- feathers or any rice husk/feather like material - can be
fuzzy yarn too!
- scissors
- cotton bud
- double sided tape
- normal scotch tape
- masking tape or washi tape -- this is for decorative pur-
poses
9
method:
1. gather all your materials
2.cover the upper half of your cotton buds with double sided tape
3.one by one, place either the feathers or fuzzy yarn, or rice husk to the taped area
a. make sure to m bunch this up to create a more full duster
4. after, tape the bottom part of this bunch using scotch tape
5. after the scotch tape, place washi tape or masking tape to mask the ends of the feather,
rice husk or yarn -- i skipped this step for mine
6. cut the bottom tip of your cotton buds [the one without anything taped on it] you’ll
roughly end up with 3/4 of the original cotton bud
7.your duster is done :D
8. to attach it to your minion, simply sew it to the hand
a. when sewing this, it’s easier to go through the tape once - going through the tape
with your sewing needle once will NOT break your tape!
