Amigurumi Kitty Cat;https://www.lovecrafts.com/en-gb/p/amigurumi-kitty-cat-machine-knitting-pattern-by-welsh-handcrafted;"ABBREVIATIONS
T = tension dial number
K = number of rows to Knit
C1 = colour 1 for body
C2 = colour 2 for tip of tail
BODY
§ Bring every second needle of 56 (45, 39) into work position
§ Cast on with waste yarn, then add ravel cord
§ Thread machine with C1, leave 15 cm / 6 inch tail
§ T 1 (3, 6), K 3 (2, 2)
§ Bring out of work needles forward so there are 3 in work and 1 out of work to end, take heel from
adjoining needle and add to empty needle
§ T 1.2 (4, 8), K 7 (6, 5)
§ Bring remaining needles into work, take heel from adjoining needle and add to empty needle
§ T 2.2 (5, 9), K 58 (46, 40)
§ T 6 (9, 10), K 1
§ Loop through loop bind off
§ Weave starting tail through stitches attached to ravel cord
§ Remove ravel cord and waste yarn
§ Pull yarn to close up bottom end, then mattress stitch sides together
§ Add filling with more at the bottom than the top
§ Close up the top by weaving just under the bind off stitches
§ If you want to make the ears more defined you can add some stitches on an angle at the base of
the ear.
§ Take a length of yarn and tie around neck area several times pulling it tightly and tie off
§ Use ball head pins to determine the position of the eyes and nose
§ Use the black yarn to embroider the eyes and white for nose, be sure not to pull the yarn too tight
TAIL
§ T 1.2 (4, 7)
§ Bring every second needle of 6 (5, 4) needles into work
§ Thread machine with C2
§ K 1
§ Hang claw weight
§ Press one part button
§ Bring remaining needles into work
