Mary’s Amiland 4
Little Cat The Ami
Assembling
Start working on the face.
Pin the ears to the head and then pin the spots where the eyes will be
placed to gather a pre-view of the face. This first phase aims to find the
right position of each item, it does not have to be perfect. You will
adjust the items as you sew them on.
More instructions as to where place each item are provided below.
Embroider the eyes, the nose and the whiskers.
#1 #2 Eyes: make a small line a stitch wide between rounds
6 and 7 from the top of the head, and go over it a few
times (see photo #1); add a straight line at the bottom
and on the top of the eye to smooth the shape (see
photo #2); move 6 stitches away and make the other
eye (see photo #3). Do not cut the yarn yet as it will be
used to shape the face later.
#3 #4
Nose: take a thin pink yarn and draw the outline of the
nose using backstitches, then fill the nose in using
satin stitches. Add satin stitches until not filled it in
full. Add a satin stitches to the top (see photos #4-5);
Shape the face: with the black yarn of the eyes make a
#5 #6
small invisible stitch in each eye. After you have made
the first stitch, pull until the spot becomes indented,
then make the second stitch in the other eye, pull the
yarn again, and fasten it off (see photos #6-7);
Whiskers: take out one thread of the back yarn and
#7 #8
embroider three whiskers on each side (see photo #8).
2013-16 ©MarysAmiland
Mary’s Amiland 5
Little Cat The Ami
Now find the right position of the ears. Place them close to the top centre of the head.
Check that both ears are at the same
distance from the eyes, approx
three/four stitches away. When you
are happy with the position of the
ears, sew them in place.
Next pin the head onto the body ensuring it is centred with respect to the face. Sew it up with neat
stitches and add some fibrefill between the head and the body before completely sewing it to avoid the
head leaning forwards.
Pin the arms and the legs to the body to find the rigth position and then sew them in place.
Tip: with the same yarn of the belly
put some small stitches so to hide the
colour change.
Finally sew the tail onto bottom-back of the body with hidden stitches.
Congratulations, you have completed Little Cat The Ami! 11
2013-16 ©MarysAmiland
