Assembly
Assembling Gladoscan be difficult. Not only is
embroidery needed, but if the right order of assembly is
not carried out some parts will not overlap each other
correctly. This is why I will explain in detail how it all
goes together.
We’ll start by sewing on the Center Device and the Side
Square onto the potato. Leave a little gap between Fig. 8
them for the next step. (Fig. 7)
Finished items made from this pattern may be sold provided credit is given to “MevvSan” with a link to my website
www.mevvsan.etsy.com. Rewriting, redistribution or resale of this pattern in any format is strictly prohibited. ™ & © 2009-
2015 Mevlinn Gusick.
Page 5
Using black yarn, begin to embroider the hooks that will
hold the device to the potato. There are three groups,
with two hooks per group. I pass the black yarn though
the same spot twice and move onto the next hook.
When you have gone around the entire circle, and
finished the hooks, pass the black yarn through a few
times to make the black wire that will connect the Circle
Device and Side Square together. If you did not sew
these two pieces down first then your embroidery will
Fig. 9
not overlap these pieces realistically. (Fig. 8)
Center Details
Now let’s embroider the center black details. Taking
your 4 ply worsted yarn pull it apart, so that you now
have 2plys to embroider with. You could use black
thread instead but I find this works well enough. It stops
the lines from becoming super chunky. Embroider
around both the yellow circle and the dark grey circle.
Finish off by embroidering the slanted lines that goes
diagonal from top right to the bottom right of the circle.
(Fig. 9) Fig. 10
Finish up the embroidery by making two red spots on
the side square and one more on the top right of the
Circle Device, right next to the black diagonal line
created earlier. (Figs. 10-11)
Sew on the wires next to the Circle Device’s edges as
shown in the photos. (Figs. 12-13) Afterwards sew on
the nails, one next to the Side Square’s left edge and
the other on the Potato’s top right.
Fig. 11
For last bit of embroidery. Take your red triangle clips
and sew in their ends, the ones made after Binding Off.
Take the black yarn on the wire and use it to sew the
wire to the back of the clip. Take your Light Grey yarn
and embroider the tip of the clips, making the metal
part on the ends. Finally, take the clips and sew them
to the black nails. (Figs. 14-15) Congratulations, You are
Finished!
