Pattern:
Cup/Frap
rnd 1: ch2, 5 sc in 2nd ch from hook
rnd 2: 2sc in each of the sts around
rnd 3: *sc in next st, 2 sc in next* repeat from * to * til end
rnd 4: *sc in each of the next 2 sts, 2sc in next* repeat from * to * til end
rnd 5: *sc in each of the next 3 sts, 2sc in next* repeat from * to * til end
rnd 6: using back loops, sc in each of the sts around
rnd 7-8: sc in each st around
rnd 9: *sc in each of the next 4 sts, 2sc in next* repeat from * to * til end
rnd 10-11: sc in each st around
rnd 12: *sc in each of the next 5 sts, 2sc in next* repeat from * to * til end
rnd 13-16: sc in each st around
rnd 17: *sc in each of the next 6 sts, 2sc in next* repeat from * to * til end
rnd 18-21: sc in each st around
rnd 22: *sc2tog in next 2 sts, sc in each of the next 6 sts* repeat from *
to * til end
rnd 23: sc in each st across
rnd 24: slst all around
“Whip Cream”
rnd 1: ch2, 5 sc in 2nd ch from hook
rnd 2: 2sc in each of the sts around
rnd 3: *sc in next st, 2 sc in next* repeat from * to * til end
rnd 4: *sc in each of the next 2 sts, 2sc in next* repeat from * to * til end
rnd 5: *sc in each of the next 3 sts, 2sc in next* repeat from * to * til end
rnd 6: *sc in each of the next 4 sts, 2sc in next* repeat from * to * til end
rnd 7: *sc in each of the next 5 sts, 2sc in next* repeat from * to * til end
rnd 8: *sc in each of the next 6 sts, 2sc in next* repeat from * to * til end
Sweet N Cute Creations Amigurumi Starbucks Frappucino
Amigurumi Starbucks
Frappucino
rnd 9: *sc in each of the next 7 sts, 2sc in next* repeat from * to * til end
rnd 10-12: sc all around
rnd 13: *sc2tog in next 2 sts, sc in each of the next 7 sts* repeat from *
to * til end, sl st to end
Swirl:
chain approximately 70 inches of white yarn
Assembly:
stuff cup/frap and whip cream firmly. Stitch the frap to the whip cream (whip cream
should cover rnds 22-24 of the frap). Print the logo of starbucks on felt paper, cut the
logo to form a circle. Using craft glue, glue the felt with the logo to the middle of the
frappucino, and the swirls to the whip cream base. Cut a starbucks straw to your desired
length and once again attach using craft glue. Make sure everything has been placed
properly and firmly. ENJOY!
