This is FREE crochet pattern.;https://www.lovecrafts.com/en-gb/p/amigurumi-unicorn-keychain-crochet-pattern-by-ljubomir-kostin;"Abbreviations:
Yarn: St. George Tango Rnd—round
Crochet hook: 2mm mr—magic ring
Embroidery needle sc—single crochet
Fiberfill stuffing inc—increase
Stitch marker, scissors dec—decrease
Horn
Rnd. 1. 4 sc in mr (4)
Rnd. 2. (1 sc, inc) x 2 (6)
Rnd. 3 – 4. 6 sc (6)
Rnd. 5. (2 sc, inc) x 3 (8)
Rnd. 6 – 7. 8 sc (8)
Finish off and cut the yarn
Hands (make 2)
Rnd. 1. 6 sc in mr
Rnd. 2. inc x 6 (12)
Rnd. 3 – 5. 12 sc (12)
Rnd. 6. (dec, 4 sc) x 2 (10)
Rnd. 7. (dec, 3 sc) x 2 (8)
Rnd. 8 – 18. 8 sc (8)
Finish off and cut the yarn . Leave a tail
for sewing.
Ears (make 2)
Chain 2
In the 2nd chain from the hook do:
Row 1. inc, ch 1, turn (2)
Row 2. inc x 2, ch 1, turn (4)
Row 3. inc, 2 sc, inc, ch1, turn (6)
Row 4. dec, 2 sc, dec (4)
Finish off and leave a tail for sewing the ears to the
head.
Head and Body
Rnd. 1. 6 sc in mr (6)
Rnd. 2. inc x 6 (12)
Rnd. 3. (1 sc, inc) x 6 (18)
Rnd. 4. (2 sc, inc) x 6 (24)
Rnd. 5. 24 sc (24)
Rnd. 6. (3 sc, inc) x 6 (30)
Rnd. 7. 30 sc (30)
Rnd. 8. 13 sc, 4 sc into the horn, 13 sc (30)
Rnd. 9. (4 sc, inc) x 6 (36)
Rnd. 10. 36 sc (36)
Rnd. 11. (5 sc, inc) x 6 (42)
Rnd. 12. 42 sc (42)
Body
Rnd. 13. 6 sc, skip next 30 sc and attach the yarn in
31st sc, do 6 sc (12)
Rnd. 14. (2 sc, inc) x 4 (16)
Rnd. 15. 16 sc (16)
Rnd. 16. (3 sc, inc) x 4 (20)
Rnd. 17. (4 sc, inc) x 4 (24)
Rnd. 18. (2 sc, inc) x 8 (32)
Rnd. 19 – 26. 32 sc (32)
Rnd. 27. (dec, 6 sc) x 4 (28)
Rnd. 28. 28 sc (28)
Rnd. 29. (dec, 5 sc) x 4 (24)
Rnd. 30. 24 sc (24)
Flatten the body and do couple of more stitches (for me
it’s 8 sc). Then close the body with 12 sc by doing:
Rnd. 31. ch 1, 12 sc (12)
Continue working on the first leg.
Left leg
Rnd. 32. ch 1, 4 sc in FLO and 4 sc in FLO on the other
side. (8)
Put the running stitch marker in the last sc.
Rnd. 33 – 42. 8 sc (8)
Rnd. 43. (1 sc, inc) x 4 (12)
Rnd. 44. (5 sc, inc) x 2 (14)
Rnd. 45 – 47. 14 sc (14)
Rnd. 48. (dec, 5 sc) x 2 (12)
Rnd. 49. dec x 6 (6)
Finish off and cut the yarn.
Right leg
Leave 4 sc between the legs. Do 1 slip stitch to join the
yarn. Then in the same way as for the left leg do:
Rnd. 32. 4 sc in FLO and 4 sc in FLO on the other side.
Put the running stitch marker in the last sc. (8)
Rnd. 33 – 42. 8 sc (8)
Rnd. 43. (1 sc, inc) x 4 (12)
Rnd. 44. (5 sc, inc) x 2 (14)
Rnd. 45 – 47. 14 sc (14)
Rnd. 48. (dec, 5 sc) x 2 (12)
Rnd. 49. dec x 6 (6)
Closing the Head and Snout
Go back to the Rnd. 12 of the head where the head was
left open and continue Rnd. 13 by doing:
Rnd. 13. 1 slip stitch to join the yarn, 1 sc in the same
stitch, then do 29 sc around. (30)
Mark the last sc with running stitch marker.
Rnd. 14. (13 sc, dec) x 2 (28)
Rnd. 15. (dec, 5 sc) x 4 (24)
Rnd. 16 – 17. 24 sc (24)
Change the color for the snout
Rnd. 18. 24 sc (24)
Rnd. 19. (dec, 2 sc) x 6 (18)
Rnd. 20. (dec, 7 sc) x 2 (16)
Rnd. 21. dec x 8 (8)
Finish off and close the hole.
Mane
Join the yarn on the body, between Rnd. 15. and 16,
and start making the curls.
Chain 20 and starting from 2nd chain from the hook
do inc 19 times, skip 2 rounds on the body and join the
yarn with 1 slip stitch.
Then, repeat the same thing:
Ch 20, from the second chain do inc 19 times.
Make 10 curls.
Tail
Join the yarn between Rnd. 29. and 30, and start
making the curls in the same way as the mane.
Chain 20, from the second chain do inc 19 times,
skip 2 rounds on the body and join the yarn with 1
slip stitch. Repeat the same thing for the second
curl.
Assembly
Embroider the eyes between Rnd. 11 and 12.
Sew the ears on Rnd. 6 and 7.
Sew the hands between Rnd. 16 and 17.
Congratulations! The unicorn is ready!
