Angelica The AngelFish;https://www.lovecrafts.com/en-gb/p/angelica-the-angelfish-crochet-pattern-by-lisa-kingsley;"Abbreviations Used:
Sc - single crochet
Hdc - half double crochet
2sc - increase (2 single crochet stitches in one stitch)
Sc2tog - decrease (turning 2 stitches into one stitch)
*to* - repeat the directions inside the stars as directed
St - stitch
Ch1 - chain 1
MR - magic ring
Supplies Needed:
Red Heart Super Saver - Carrot (50 grams) used for the fish body and fins
Bernat super value - Black (small amount) used for the dots, stripes, head and small fins
White felt - cut into small circles approximately 1"" in diameter - used under the safety eyes
1 pair of black 12 mm safety eyes
4 mm crochet hook
Polyester stuffing
Stitch marker
Tapestry needle (used for sewing your pieces together)
T-Pins - used to hold your pieces together before sewing
Head and Body:
With black yarn
Round 1) MR - 4 sc in the loop (4 st)
Round 2) *sc in the next st, 2sc in the next st* repeat *to* all around (6 st)
Round 3) *sc in the next 2 st, 2sc in the next st* repeat *to* all around (8 st)
Round 4) *sc in the next 3 st, 2sc in the next st* repeat *to* all around (10 st)
Round 5) *sc in the next 4 st, 2sc in the next st* repeat *to* all around (12 st)
Round 6) *sc in the next 2 st, 2sc in the next st* repeat *to* all around (16 st)
Round 7) *sc in the next 3 st, 2sc in the next st* repeat *to* all around (20 st)
Round 8) *sc in the next 3 st, 2sc in the next st* repeat *to* all around (25 st)
Round 9) *sc in the next 4 st, 2sc in the next st* repeat *to* all around (30 st)
Round 10) *sc in the next 5 st, 2sc in the next st* repeat *to* all around (35 st)
Round 11) *sc in the next 4 st, 2sc in the next st* repeat *to* all around (42 st)
Round 12) *sc in the next 6 st, 2sc in the next st* repeat *to* all around (48 st)
Round 13) sc in each st around (48 st) start stuffing and continue as work progresses
Change to orange *see note below regarding the safety eyes*
Round 14) *sc in the next 11 st, 2sc in the next st* repeat *to* all around (52 st)
Rounds 15 and 16) sc in each st around (52 st)
Round 17) *sc in the next 11 st, sc2tog* repeat *to* all around (48 st)
Rounds 18 to 21) sc in each st around (total of 4 rounds) (48 st)
Round 22) *sc in the next 10 st, sc2tog* repeat *to* all around (44 st)
Rounds 23 to 32) sc in each st around (total of 10 rounds) (44 st)
Round 33) sc2tog, *sc in the next 6 st, sc2tog* repeat *to* all around, sc in the last 2 stitches
(38 st)
Round 34) *sc in the next 4 st, sc2tog* repeat *to* all around, sc2tog in the last 2 stitches (31
st)
Round 35) *sc in the next 3 st, sc2tog* repeat *to* all around, sc in the last st (25 st)
Round 36) *sc in the next 3 st, sc2tog* repeat *to* all around (20 st)
Round 37) *sc in the next 2 st, sc2tog* repeat *to* all around (15 st)
Round 38) *sc in the next st, sc2tog* repeat *to* all around (10 st)
Round 39) *sc2tog* repeat *to* all around
Fasten off and hide your end inside the fish. If you are using safety eyes, cut your one inch
circles of white felt, cut a slit in the centre, this is where you will insert the post of the eye, insert
the eye post between rows 8 and 9 of the head - one on each side of the head.
Upper and Lower orange Fins. Worked in the round. Carrot yarn. Do not stuff. (Make 2)
Round 1) Chain 18 - starting in the second chain from hook, sc in the next 16 st, 3sc in the last
chain (this will allow you to work under the foundation chain) sc in the next 15 st, 3sc in the last
st (37 st)
Round 2) 2sc in the next st, sc in the next 15 st, sc2tog, sc in the next 17 st, 2sc in the next 2 st
(39 st)
Round 3) sc in the next 15 st, sc2tog, sc2tog, sc in the next 15 st, 2sc in the next 3 st, sc in the
next 2 st (40 st)
Round 4) sc in the next 15 st, sc2tog, sc in the next 16 st, 2sc in the next 3 st, sc in the next 4
st (42 st)
Round 5) sc in the next 11 st, sc2tog, sc2tog, sc2tog, sc in the next 18 st, leave the remaining
stitches unworked. Flatten and sc across, closing the hole.
Fasten off leaving a long length of yarn. Sew one to the top of the fish and sew the other one to
the bottom of the fish.
Tail fin. Worked in the round. Do not stuff. (Make 2)
Round 1) MR - 4 sc in the loop
Round 2) *sc in the next st, 2sc in the next st* repeat *to* all around (6 st)
Round 3) *sc in the next 2 st, 2sc in the next st* repeat *to* all around (8 st)
Round 4) *sc in the next 3 st, 2sc in the next st* repeat *to* all around (10 st)
Round 5) *sc in the next 4 st, 2sc in the next st* repeat *to* all around (12 st)
Round 6) *sc in the next 5 st, 2sc in the next st* repeat *to*all around (14 st)
Round 7) *sc in the next 5 st, sc2tog* repeat *to* all around (12 st)
Round 8) *sc in the next 4 st, sc2tog* repeat *to* all around (10 st)
Round 9) *sc in the next 3 st, sc2tog* repeat *to* all around (8 st)
Fasten off first fin only. Once you have completed the second one, do not fasten off, instead join
to the other fin with a sl st in the last st worked on the first tail fin. Continue to work as follows:
Round 10) sc in the same st as you joined, sc in the next 2 st, sc2tog, sc in the next 2 st,
sc2tog, sc in the next 2 st, sc2tog, sc in the next st, sc2tog (12 st)
Rounds 11 and 12) so in each st around (12 st)
Fasten off leaving a long tail. Sew to the back of the body.
Bottom fins. Made with Black yarn. Worked in the round. Do not stuff. (Make 2)
Round 1) MR - 4 sc in the loop
Round 2) *sc in the next st, 2sc in the next st* repeat *to* all around (6 st)
Round 3) *sc in the next 2 st, 2sc in the next st* repeat *to* all around (8 st)
Round 4) *sc in the next 3 st, 2sc in the next st* repeat *to* all around (10 st)
Round 5) *sc in the next 4 st, 2sc in the next st* repeat *to* all around (12 st)
Round 6) *sc in the next 5 st, 2sc in the next st* repeat *to*all around (14 st)
Round 7) *sc in the next 5 st, sc2tog* repeat *to* all around (12 st)
Round 8) *sc in the next 4 st, sc2tog* repeat *to* all around (10 st)
Round 9) *sc in the next 3 st, sc2tog* repeat *to* all around (8 st)
Round 10) sc in each st around (8 st)
Round 11) flatten and sc across, closing the hole.
Fasten off leaving a long length of yarn. Sew one on each side of the fish towards the bottom
where the black and orange meet (see photo below for placement).
Stripes. Made with black yarn. (Make 6)
Chain 30. Starting in the second ch from hook, sl st in the next 7 st, sc in the next 3 st, hdc in
the next 9 st, dc in the next 3 st, sl st in the last 7 st. Fasten off leaving a long length of yarn.
Sew 3 on each side of the fish. See photo for placement.
Spots. Made with black yarn. Worked in the round. (Make 4)
Round 1) MR - 6 sc in the loop (6 st)
Round 2) 3sc in the next st, sl st in the next 2 st, 3sc in the next st, sl st in the next 2 stitches.
Fasten off leaving a long length of yarn. Sew one on each tail fin.
Assembly:
1) cut out your felt pieces and insert your safety eyes as instructed above
2) Centre one of the large orange fins along the top of the fish (see photo for placement)
3) Centre the second large orange fin along the bottom of the fish (see photo for placement
and direction)
4) Sew a black spot on each tail fin (total of 4)
5) Sew the tail to the back of the fish (hiding the hole - if you have one :)
6) Sew the small black fins to the bottom of the fish, on either side of the large orange fin, at
the front of the fish
7) Sew 3 long stripes on each side of the fish. See photo for placement.
