The hair is worked directly onto the head using needle and backstitch, and
then formed into plaits.
1. Cut ORANGE yarn into strips of about 55–58 cm [22-23 in]long,
until you have about 22 bundles of 4 strands each.
2. Using pins, mark out a straight line down the middle of the head
from the front (forehead) to the back (base of hairline).
This photo from
another doll
using same
technique
3. Take one bundle of 4 strands of yarn and fold it in half to find the
middle of the bundle.
Using a needle threaded with another long piece of ORANGE yarn,
attach the middle of the bundle to the head at the forehead using
a backstitch.
4. Continue attaching strands of yarn to the head, along the middle
line marked by the pins, using backstitch, until you reach the base
of the head. There should essentially be a head of hair with a part
down the middle.
