With Color B:
Ch 13
1. sc in 2nd ch and across= 12
2. Ch 2, turn, work 5 dc in the same st, sl st in next 3 st,
(6 dc in next st, work a sl st in the next 3 st) x 2
F/O and leave a long tail for sewing
Sweet Oddity Art 8
Gills(Make 6):
With Color C: (Make one gill in each rainbow color)
Ch 13
1. sl st in 2nd ch from hook, sl in next ch, Ch 4 off that stitch
Sl st in 2nd ch from hook and sl st in next 2 chains, sl st in the original starting st that you made
the ch 4 from.
2. sl st in next ch, Ch 4, sl st in 2nd chain from hook and sl st in next 2 chains, sl st in the original
st that you made the ch 4 from
3. Repeat row 2: 2 more times
Sweet Oddity Art 9
Gills Continued:
4. sl st in next ch, Ch 5, sl st in 2nd chain from hook and next 3 chains, sl st in the original starting
st that you made the ch 5 from.
5. Repeat row 4: 3 more times
6. sl st in next ch, Ch 6, sl st in 2nd chain from hook and next 4 chains, sl st in the original starting
st that you made the ch 6 from.
7. Repeat row 6: 2 more times
Now you will turn the first side you made and start working on the opposite side of the chain:
1. sl st in next ch, Ch 6, sl st in 2nd chain from hook and next 4 chains, sl st in the original
starting st that you made the ch 6 from.
2. Repeat row 1: 2 more times
3. sl st in next ch, Ch 5, sl st in 2nd chain from hook and next 3 chains, sl st in the original starting
st that you made the ch 5 from
4. Repeat row 3: 3 more times
Sweet Oddity Art 10
Gills Continued:
5. sl st in next ch, Ch 4, sl st in 2nd chain from hook and next 2 chains, sl st in the original starting
st that you made the ch 4 from
5. Repeat row 5: 3 more times
Sl st in next st to F/O
Leave a long tail for sewing
Sweet Oddity Art 11
Assembly
Head and Body:
1. Pin the arms onto the side of the body in a forward angle. There are no particular
rounds I place these on. I try to judge by what I think looks best.
2. Sew the arms onto the body.
Sweet Oddity Art 12
Legs:
1. Turn the body upside down with the nose facing away from you. Pin the legs on the bottom
of the body approximately between rounds 54 and 55.
2. Sew the legs onto the body.
Sweet Oddity Art 13
Nostrils:
1. Mark 4 spots on the face approximately between rounds 19 and 20.
You will want the each nostril pin 2 holes apart. The set of nostril pins approximately 5
holes apart from each other.
2. Thread your needle with a long strand of dark pink yarn. Insert the needle into a hole
on the side of the head. Bring the needle up to a pin and insert into the hole of the next
pin. Repeat this about 2 more times. Repeat for the 2nd nostril. Weave in the tail ends.
Sweet Oddity Art 14
Tail:
1. Pin the tail gills onto the sides of the tail. Sew them onto the tail.
2. Pin the tail onto the back of the body. You may need to add more stuffing as you sew.
Sew the tail onto the body.
Sweet Oddity Art 15
Gills:
1. Bring the tail end you left off with on the gills down to the bottom of the gill.
2. Pin the gills onto the side of the head, one at a time. In a row going down the side of
the head.
3. Sew the gills onto the head.
Sweet Oddity Art 16
Sweet Oddity Art 17
Eyebrows:
1. Thread your needle with a long strand of black thread. Insert the needle into a hole
approximately 3 rounds above the eye. Insert the needle into another hole 2 stitches
away. Repeat for the 2nd eyebrow. Weave in the tail ends.
You now have your finished axoltol! Thank you for your purchase! If you have any questions or
concerns please email me at sweetoddityart@gmail.com or etsy convo me. I will get back to
you asap. Please share your finished axolotl with me as often as you want! I love seeing them!
Sweet Oddity Art 18
Helpful Tips:
Exact Colors and Brand of Yarn Used:
1. Pink: I love this yarn Soft Pink
2. Dark Pink: I love this yarn Dark Pink
3. Red: I love this yarn Red
4. Purple: I love this yarn Lilac
5. Blue: Red Heart Royal Blue
6. Green: Red Heart Spring Green
7. Yellow: Red Heart Daffodil
8. Orange: I love this yarn Coral
You can use different eye and nose sizes. You might have to adjust the placements if you
change the sizes.
You can use different hook sizes and weights of yarn. It will just change the size of your axolotl
and you might need to adjust eye and nose placement.
How you stuff matters! The type of stuffing you use, how you stuff, all this matters on how your
axolotl turns out. I prefer Polyfil stuffing but you can use other types.
I painted my own eyes for this doll but you can find some great ones at glasseyesonline.com or
suncatchercrafteyes.com
