Baby Elephants;https://www.lovecrafts.com/en-gb/p/baby-elephants-crochet-pattern-by-melissas-crochet-patterns;"Abbreviations used…
● Ch - chain
● Sl - slip stitch
● Sc - single crochet
● St - stitch
● Sts - stitches
● Rpt - repeat
● Inc - increase, 2 sc in the same space
● Dec - decrease or sc2tog (single crochet 2 together)
Note : All pieces are made in a continuous spiral. Most pieces begin with a magic
ring, but you can also use a ch 2 to start.
Trunk, Head, and Body (one piece)
● Starting at the trunk
Rnd 1 ~ Using a magic ring, place 4 sc into the magic ring (4 sc)
Rnds 2-6 ~ sc around (4 sc)
Rnd 7 ~ sc, inc / rpt (6 sc)
Rnd 8 ~ sc in 2, inc / rpt (8 sc)
Rnd 9 ~ sc, inc / rpt around (12 sc)
Rnd 10 ~ sc, inc / rpt around (18 sc)
Rnd 11 ~ sc in 8, inc / rpt (20 sc)
Rnds 12-15 ~ sc around (20 sc)
Rnd 16 ~ sc in 2, dec / rpt around (15 sc)
● Insert safety eyes in desired place
● Stuff head
Rnd 17 ~ sc in 3, dec / rpt around (12 sc)
Rnd 18 ~ sc around (12 sc)
Rnd 19 ~ sc, inc / rpt around (18 sc)
Rnd 20 ~ sc in 2, inc / rpt around (24 sc)
Rnds 21-26 ~ sc around (24 sc)
Rnd 27 ~ sc in 2, dec / rpt around (18 sc)
Rnd 28 ~ sc, dec / rpt around (12 sc)
● Stuff body
Rnd 29 ~ dec around (6 sc)
● Fasten off, leaving a tail for sewing.
● Using your yarn needle, sew the remaining hole closed.
Legs (make 4)
Rnd 1 ~ Using a magic ring, place 4 sc into the magic ring (4 sc)
Rnd 2 ~ inc around (8 sc)
Rnds 3-4 ~ sc around (8 sc)
● Sl in next st
● Fasten off, leaving a tail for sewing.
● Stuff legs
● Using your yarn needle, sew legs onto the bottom of the elephant’s body.
Tail
Leaving a beginning tail, ch 4, sc in the 2nd ch from the hook and in next 2 ch sts
(3 sc)
● Fasten off, leaving a tail.
● With another piece of yarn (not the beginning or end tail) sew the tail into
place. The side with the tails will be the end of the elephant’s tail.
Tail Cont.
Cut a 4-5 inch piece of yarn. Fold in half. With your crochet hook, pull the piece of
yarn through the center of the end of the tail (in between the beginning and end
tails) about half way through, pull the two ends of the piece of yarn through the
loop. Pull tightly to keep in place. Trim all yarn ends to the same length.
Ears (make 2)
Row 1 ~ Leaving a long beginning tail for sewing, chain 5, sc in the 2nd ch from the
hook and across (4 sc) ch 1, turn
Row 2 ~ inc, sc in 2, inc (6 sc) ch 1, turn
Row 3 ~ sc across (6 sc) ch 1, turn
Row 4 ~ dec, sc in 2, dec (4 sc)
● Fasten off, leaving a tail.
● Weave in the end tail.
● With your yarn needle and beginning tail, sew onto the elephant’s head.
Ball
Rnd 1 ~ Using a magic ring, place 6 sc into the magic ring (6 sc)
Rnd 2 ~ inc around (12 sc)
Rnd 3 ~ sc, inc / rpt around (18 sc)
Rnds 4-7 ~ sc around (18 sc)
Rnd 8 ~ sc, dec / rpt around (12 sc)
● Stuff ball
Rnd 9 ~ dec around (6 sc)
● Fasten off, leaving a tail for sewing.
● With your yarn needle, sew the remaining hole closed.
