Baby Wolf Amigurumi Pattern;https://www.lovecrafts.com/en-gb/p/baby-wolf-amigurumi-crochet-pattern-by-amanda-maciel;;"Baby Wolf Amigurumi Pattern
by adorably kawaii
This cute little wolf has jointed arms, legs, and tail! I hope you enjoy this
pattern. Look over the pattern carefully before starting.
Materials: Tools:
• Worsted weight yarn in gray and • G/4.25mm hook
white. (I used Craft Smart) • Yarn needle
• Black embroidery thread • Embroidery needle
• Pair of 15mm safety eyes
• Five 15mm safety eyes (or doll joints)
• Stuffing
Size:
1
Approximately 8”(20cm) tall when standing and 5”(12.7cm) wide from ear to ear.
The tail is about 4.5”(11cm) long and 2.5”(6.3cm) wide. Results will vary
depending on your tension and your yarn & hook choice.
Note on Gauge/ Tension :
It's important to make sure the hook size you're using is the appropriate size for
your yarn as well as for your tension. Tension varies from person to person and
from day to day. It can change slightly throughout the project and result in larger
or smaller stitches and rows which can affect proportions and the overall size.
Abbreviation s :
Ch - Chain Sl st - Slip stitch
Sc - Single crochet St(s) -–Stitch(es)
2 sc - 2 single crochet increase R# - Round/Row #
Sc2tog - 2 single crochet decrease Rep - Repeat
Sk - Skip
Magic Ring:
A few inches from the end of the yarn, wrap two loops over your finger. While the
loops still on your finger, insert the hook from right to left into the loops and pull
the working yarn through.
2
Carefully take the loops off your fingers and chain one. This doesn't count as the
first stitch.
Insert the hook into the two loops again and pull up a loop. Yarn over and draw
through both loops. This counts as the first single crochet stitch. Continue for
the rest of the stitches. Then pull the yarn tail to close the hole.
Color Change s :
When you get to the last stitch in the current color, insert hook into the next
stitch, yarn over, and draw up a loop.
3
Yarn over with the new color and draw through both loops on the hook.
Color Change i n the Middle o f S c2tog :
Pick up the first loop with your current color and then pick up the next loop with
your new color.
