Crochet Pattern BAT by Strickglück 2
Materials:
- Crochet hook Size 3 mm and optional 2 mm
- Polyacrylic yarn for this hooks. I had Schachenmayr Bravo 50g/133m (orange und
violet – about 35 g, a little brown and white)
- Polyester fiber
- Hot glue gin (optional)
Purple bat is about 14 cm (5,5 inch) tall, about 27 cm (10,6 inch) wide, orange bat
is about 12 cm (4,7 inch) tall and 25 cm (9,8 inch) wide.
Techniques used:
 The bat is worked in continuous rounds; do not join and do not turn at the ends of
rounds.
 Place a stitch marker to indicate the beginning of rounds and move marker as each
round is worked.
 Decreases are following to do:
https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tZ575_ZklWk
Please watch this video to learn the method.
Stitches used:
Ch = chain
st = stitch
sc = single crochet
hdc = half double crochet
dc = double crochet
tr = treble crochet
sl st = slip stitch
inc = increase = 2 sc in the next st
dec = decrease = 2 st together
*……..* X times = repeat the combination of stitches from * to * X times
Crochet Pattern BAT by Strickglück 3
Body (purple or orange):
Rnd 1: ch 6,
than 4 sc starting from the second chain from hook, 3 sc in the last ch, on the other side of
chain 3 sc, 3 sc in the last ch (13 sc)
Rnd 2: inc, 3 sc, *inc* repeat 3 times, 4 sc, *inc* 2 times (19 sc)
Rnd 3: 8sc, inc, 8sc, inc, 1sc (21 sc)
Rnd 4: 8sc, *inc* 2 times, 9sc, *inc* 2 times (25 sc)
Rnd 5: Sc in each st around (25 sc)
Rnd 6: 8sc, inc, 2sc, inc, 9sc, inc, 2sc, inc (29 sc)
Rnd 7: 11sc, inc, 14sc, inc, 2sc (31 sc)
Rnd 8-9: 2 rounds Sc in each st around (31 sc)
Rnd 10: 13sc, inc, 14sc, inc, 2sc (33 sc)
Rnd 11: *13sc, inc, 1sc, inc* 2 times, 1sc (37 sc)
Rnd 12-13: 2 rounds Sc in each st around (37 sc)
Rnd 14: 16sc, inc, 17sc, inc, 2sc (39 sc)
Rnd 15: 16sc, inc, 1sc, inc, 17sc, inc, 1sc, inc (43 sc)
Rnd 16: Sc in each st around (43 sc)
Rnd 17: 19sc, inc, 20sc, inc, 2sc (45 sc)
Rnd 18-21: 4 rounds Sc in each st around (45 sc)
Rnd 22: *3sc, dec* 9 times (36 sc)
Rnd 23: Sc in each st around (36 sc)
