BEAR;https://www.lovecrafts.com/en-gb/p/bear-amigurumi-crochet-pattern-by-lori-van-den-bosch;"Abbreviations and Stitches
Ch - Chain
Sc - Single Crochet
Inc - Increase
Dec - Decrease
Head
E/9-3.5mmHook
ChocolateBrown(BigTwist)
Working in rounds
1. Ch 2, 4sc into the 2nd ch from hook (4)
2. (Sc, inc) around (6)
3. (Sc, inc) around (9)
4. Sc around (9)
*Insert 8mm safety nose into the center of the 1st round with the last stitch of round 4
above the top of the nose.
5. Sc around (9)
6. Inc around (18)
7. (Sc, inc) around (27)
8. Sc, inc, (sc in next 2, inc) 8 times, sc (36)
9. (Sc in next 3, inc) around (45)
10.(Sc in next 3, dec) around (36)
11. Sc, dec, (sc in next 2, dec) 8 times, sc (27)
12 - 13. Sc around (27)
*Insert eyes between rounds 6 and 7, centered with the nose, with 5 stitches
separating them.
14. (Sc, dec) around (18)
15. (Sc, dec) around (12)
*Start to stuff head
16 - 17. Sc around (12)
*Sl St into the next stitch and finish off, leaving a long tail for attaching. Stuff firmly.
Body
E/9-3.5mmHook
ChocolateBrown(BigTwist)
*The body is worked from butt to front.
Working in rounds
1. Ch 2, 6sc into 2nd ch from hook (6)
2. Inc around (12)
3. Sc in next 2, inc in next 2, sc in next 4, inc in next 2, sc in next 2 (16)
4. Sc in next 2, inc in next 4, sc in next 4, inc in next 4, sc in next 2 (24)
5. Sc in next 4, inc in next 5, sc in next 7, dec 2 times, sc in next 4 (27)
6. Sc in n next 7, dec 2 times, sc in next 16 (25)
7 - 9. Sc around (25)
10. (Sc in next 3, dec) around (20)
11. Sc around (20)
12. Inc, sc in next 10, inc, sc in next 8 (22)
13. Sc around (22)
14. Sc in next 4, inc, sc in next 5, inc, sc in next 11 (24)
15. Sc in next 4, inc in next 2, sc in next 5, inc in next 2, sc in next 11 (28)
16. Sc around (28)
17. Sc in next 6, dec 2 times, sc in next 3, dec 2 times, sc in next 11 (24)
18. (Sc in next 2, dec) around (18)
19. (Sc, dec) around (12)
*Stuff body firmly
-The end will be an invisible finish used for CLOSED pieces. The steps are broken down
in steps a through c.
Invisible Finish - Closed
(this method is for CLOSED pieces)
Step a: Cut the yarn and pull up on the hook, drawing your yarn out from your last stitch.
Step b: Thread the yarn onto a dull yarn needle and insert the needle through the next 2
FRONT LOOPS ONLY. Pull yarn through. Repeat to complete the round. Pull the yarn tight to
close.
Step c: Weave through the last round to secure the end and pull tight again. Hide the loose end
through the middle of the invisible finish and inside of your finished piece.
*The body vertically is narrow and horizontally will be more round. The pointed
beginning rounds of the body is the butt and the flatter invisible finish side is the front of
the bear. The pointed butt is more pointe at the top.
Side view of the body
Feet
E/9-3.5mmHook
ChocolateBrown(BigTwist)
Make 4
Working in rounds
1. Magic circle, 8sc into circle (8)
2. Inc around (16)
3. Sc in next 6, inc in next 4, sc in next 6 (20)
4. Sc in next 8, dec 2 times, sc in next 8 (18)
5. Dec, sc in next 4, dec 4 times, sc in next 4 (13)
6. Sc in next 3, dec 3 times, sc in next 2, dec (9)
*Stuff foot
7 - 8. Sc around (9)
9. (Sc in next 2, inc) around (12)
10 - 11. Sc around (12)
*Sl St into the next stitch and finish off, leaving a long tail for attaching. Stuff firmly.
Ears
E/9-3.5mmHook
ChocolateBrown(BigTwist)
Make 2
Working in rounds
1. Ch 2, 5sc into 2nd ch from hook (5)
2. Inc around (10)
3. (Sc, inc) around (15)
4. (Sc, dec) around (10)
5. (Sc in next 3, dec) around (8)
*Sl St into the next stitch and finish off, leaving a long tail.
*Flatten the ear. Pinch the opening closed and use the tail to add a few stitches through
the pinched end of the ear to keep the shape. Keep the long tail for attaching.
Tail
E/9-3.5mmHook
ChocolateBrown(BigTwist)
Working in rounds
1. Ch 2, 4sc into circle (4)
2. Inc around (8)
3. Dec around (4)
*Sl St into the next stitch and finish off, leaving a long tail for attaching.
Assembly
Connecting the rear legs
- The rear legs are connected to the bottom of the body, below the point of the butt. Make
sure the legs are stuffed firmly. The back of the legs will be connected between the 3rd
and 4th round from the butt. The front of the legs will be connected between the 7th and
8th round from the butt. The space between the legs should be as close as you can
manage.
Connecting the front legs
- The front legs are connected to the bottom of the body, centered with the back legs.
Make sure the legs are stuffed firmly. The front of the legs will be connected between
the 4th and 5th round from the front. The back of the legs will be connected between the
8th and 9th round from the front. The space between the legs should be as close as you
can manage.
Connecting the ears to the head
- The ears are connected centered on the top of the head between the 10th and 11th
round from the nose, with 8 stitches between the ears.
Connecting the head to the body
- The head is connected to the front of the body, centered with the legs. The bottom of the
neck will be connected just below the beginning round on the front of the body. The top
of the neck will be connected between the 3rd and 4th round from the front of the body.
Make sure the head and neck is stuffed firmly.
Connecting the tail to the body
- The tail is connected just above the beginning round of the butt.
The Bear is done!
