Cute Bear Pumpkin Bun;https://www.lovecrafts.com/en-gb/p/bear-free-crochet-pattern-pumpkin-halloween-crochet-pattern-crochet-pattern-by-kathy-leung;"Abbreviations (US Terms)
MR = Magic Ring
Rnd = Round
Ch = Chain
SC = Single Crochet
HDC = Half Double Crochet
DC = Double Crochet
INC = Increase (2 Single Crochets in the same stitch)
Slst = Slip Stitch
St = Stitch
Tip: Ch(s) are not counted as a stitch unless otherwise stated.
Materials:
Yarn: Milk Cotton Yarn
Yarn weight: 2 Fine / Sport
Amount of yarn needed: approx 35 meters
Crochet Hook: 2.0mm(US B)
Stuffing
Stitch marker
Sewing needle
Plastic eyes 4 mm
Finished size: approx.10 cm
Head
R1: With orange yarn, Ch 25. Starting in 3rd ch from hook: 23 HDC, Ch 2, turn.
R2–R28: BLO 23 HDC, Ch 2, turn. Fasten off, leaving a long tail for sewing.
Sew R1 and R28 together to form a tube. Thread the yarn tail through one edge, pull tight to
close. Stuff lightly, then thread the yarn tail through the opposite side, pull tight to form a
pumpkin shape.
Use yarn to divide the pumpkin into 7 segments.
Ear (make 2)
R1: With orange yarn, 6 SC in MR [6]
R2: 6 INC [12]
R3–R4: 12 SC [12]
R5: 6 DEC [6]. Fasten off, leaving a long tail for sewing.
Sew ears symmetrically onto both sides of the head.
Nose
With white yarn, 6 SC in MR, sl st to join. Fasten off, leaving a long tail for
sewing.
Embroider the nose with dark brown yarn.
Sew the finished nose piece to the center front of the bear head, between
the eyes.
Pumpkin Stem
R1: With green yarn, 5 SC in MR [6]
R2–R3: 5 SC [5]
Fasten off, leaving a long tail for sewing.
Sew the stem to the top center of the pumpkin.
