Stitch Guidance:
Slip Stitch (sl st): Insert hook in st indicated, yarn over and draw through all loops.
UK Double Crochet/US Single Crochet (dc/sc): Insert hook in st indicated and draw up a loop
(two loops on hook), yarn over, draw through both loops on hook.
UK Double Crochet/US Single Crochet 2 sts together (dc2tog/sc2tog): Insert hook in the
st indicated and draw up a loop (two loops on hook), Insert hook in the next st, yarn over, draw
through three loops on hook.
Cluster st = yarn over, insert hook into next st, pull up a loop (three loops on hook), yarn
over, yarn over, insert hook into same st, pull up a loop (five loops on hook), yarn over, pull yarn
through all five loops on hook.
Pattern Guidance:
Invisible join:
The last st of your work (where relevant) should be finished off using the invisible join method:
 After the last stitch is completed do not join; cut your yarn and pull the tail all the way
through the stitch
 Then using a hook or a yarn needle thread insert under the loops of the stitch you wish to
join to. Pull yarn through gently.
 Then, insert your hook or needle into
the centre of the last stitch. Pull yarn
through gently and weave in ends as
usual.
