BOTANICAL;https://www.lovecrafts.com/en-gb/p/botanical-buddies-free-toy-knitting-pattern-for-kids-in-paintbox-yarns-simply-dk;"ABBREVIATIONS
● Use the knitted cast on unless otherwise instructed. cm centimeters
● Work all pieces flat (back and forth) on the single pointed foll following
needles, not in the round. g grams
● To work stockinette stitch (st st), which is also known g st garter stitch
as stocking stitch, knit the right side rows and purl the in inches
wrong side rows. k knit
● To work reverse stockinette stitch (rev st st), knit the k2tog knit two stitches together (decrease by 1)
wrong side rows and purl the right side rows. kfb knit into front and back (increase by 1)
● To work garter stitch (g st) knit the right side and wrong LH left hand
side rows. mm millimeters
● The ""wrap and turn"" creates short rows to shape the oz ounces
pieces. On the wrapped stitches, pick up the wraps as p purl
you encounter them on following rows to prevent holes p2tog purl two stitches together (decrease by 1)
forming at the point of the wrap and turn. patt pattern
● Use mattress stitch and yarn tails for seaming unless psso pass the slipped stitch over (decrease by 1)
otherwise instructed. rem remaining
● To mark stitches, use lockable stitch markers, or thread a rep repeat
piece of waste yarn through the stitch to be marked and rev reverse
tie in a loose knot so that it can be removed later. RH right hand
sl1 slip 1 stitch purl-wise
ssk slip the next stitch knit-wise, slip the next stitch purl-wise,
knit through the front of the two slipped sts (decrease by 1)
st st stockinette (stocking) stitch
st/s stitch/es
tog together
w&t wrap and turn: work to stitch to be wrapped, on a knit row
bring yarn to the front and slip the next stitch onto the right hand
needle, return the yarn to the back, slip the stitch back to the left
hand needle and turn; on a purl row take yarn to the back and slip
the next stitch onto the right hand needle, return the yarn to the
front, slip the stitch back to the left hand needle and turn.
