TO MAKE UP PLANT POTS
Note: This is optional, but the toys photographed used a plastic
plant pot to line the knitted pot - this keeps the sides smooth
and flat, and also allows you to add a weight inside the pot so
that your plant will stand up unsupported (otherwise it may be
top heavy and topple over). You can use plastic or biodegrade-
able plant pots for this purpose. For “ballast”, add 31/2oz/100g
of dried rice in a plastic food bag inside the base of each pot
(or alternatively you could also use sand or gravel). Note that
you do not have to use the plant pots to line the knitted pot,
you can simply stuff the knitted pot to make a squishy toy if you
prefer. Instructions are included for both options below.
To begin making up
Start to make up the knitted plant pot for each toy in the same
way. Start by gathering the cast on sts tog at the bottom of
the pot, and sew the side edges of the pot tog up to the start
of the yarn C soil or yarn G moss at the top of the pot, leaving
a gap in the top.
If you are using a plastic plant pot liner for the pots with
eyes (i.e. Bella Blue Columns Cacti, Beth Bonsai Tree, Simon
Spider Plant and Victor Venus Fly Trap)
You will need to make holes in the sides of the plastic plant
pot for the toy safety eye stalks to fit through. To mark the
position of the eyes on the plastic pot, stretch the knitted pot
piece over the plastic plant pot liner. At the stitch markers,
push pins through the knitting into the plastic pot to mark
the eye positions. Remove the pins and knitted pot piece,
and use an awl or knitting needle to puncture holes in the
plastic pot at the marked positions. Check the holes are large
enough for the toy safety eye stalks to fit through and make
larger if necessary. Place the knitted pot over the plastic pot
again, lining up the eye positions with the holes in the plastic
pot. Push the eye stalks through both the knitted and plastic
pots, remove the stitch markers, and add the washers on
the eye stalks on the inside of the plastic pot. Add the dried
rice or other weight inside the base of the plastic pot and
place a layer of toy filling on top. Then sew the side edges
of the soil/moss tog along the top of the knitted pot. Sew
both cheeks onto the front of the knitted pot below the eye
positions, covering 2 of the increase stitches from pot row 24,
using a running back stitch around the outer edge in yarn I.
If you are using a plastic plant pot liner for the pots without
eyes (i.e. Barry Ball Cactus and Sally Saguaro Cactus)
Place the knitted pot over the plastic plant pot liner. Add
the dried rice or other weight inside the base of the plastic
pot and place a layer of toy filling on top. Then sew the side
edges of the soil/moss tog along the top of the knitted pot.
If you are not using a plastic plant pot liner
For the pots with eyes (i.e. Bella Blue Columns Cacti, Beth
Bonsai Tree, Simon Spider Plant and Victor Venus Fly Trap),
insert the toy safety eyes at the marked sts and remove
markers. For all the toys add toy filling to the pot, then sew
the side edges of the soil/moss tog along the top. For the
pots with eyes, sew the 2 cheeks onto the front of the pot
below the eyes using a running back stitch around the outer
edge in yarn I.
