More instructions where to place each item are
provided below.
The eyes are placed with the pupils towards the top, at round 5 from the top head, 4 stitches apart.
When you are happy with the position of the eyes, sew them in place with invisible stitches (find
instructions in Basic Stitches in the appendix) Fill them with fibrefill before completely sewing the eyes.
Next find the right position of the mouth. Place it slighly below the eyes in the centre.
2016 ©MarysAmiland
Mary’s Amiland 6
Bubble The Ami
When you are happy with the position of the
mouth sew it in place making small stitches in
the middle, leaving loose the outer border.
Now place the arms with the thumb along the body on the inner side, 13 rounds from the top of the
head. When you are happy with the position of arms sew them in place.
Note: ensure that the arms are placed at the
same level.
Place the curls with the ends overlapped on the top of the head.
Sew them together with
firm stitches so to avoid
them coming off if pulled.
Weave ends in.
Finally place the antennae on the top of the head, just behind the curls, a few stitches apart. Sew them
in place.
Congratulations, you have completed Bubble The Ami!
2016 ©MarysAmiland
