PATTERN NOTES & TIPS
As with all amigurumi patterns, stitches should
be worked tightly to achieve the desired shape.
Each round is worked in a spiral and does not
need to be joined unless otherwise specified.
The stem may be reinforced by adding wire.
This is especially encouraged if your stitches
tend to be looser.
You may crochet the pattern using yarn-over or
yarn-under stitches. The project in the photo
was crocheted using yarn-under stitches.
Pattern is written in US terms.
