F/O and leave a tail. (the tail does not need to be long)
Sweet Oddity Art 3
Body: Arms(Make 2):
Starting with Color B: With Color A:
1. Make 6 sc into a magic ring= 6 1. Make 6 sc into a magic ring= 6
2. Increase in each st around= 12 2. Increase in each st around= 12
3. (sc, inc) x 6= 18 3-6. Sc in each st around
4. (inc, 2 sc) x 6= 24 Stop stuffing the arms
5. (3 sc, inc) x 6= 30 7. 5 sc, dec, 5 sc= 11
6. 2 sc, inc, (4 sc, inc) x 5, 2 sc= 36 8. Sc in each st around
7-8. sc in each st around 9. 4 sc, dec, 3 sc, dec= 9
Change to Color C: 10. Sc in each st around
9-11. sc in each st around 11. 7 sc, dec= 8
Change to Color D: 12-16. Sc in each st around
12-13. sc in each st around F/O and leave a long tail for sewing
14. (5 sc, dec) x 4, 8 sc= 32 !Tip! If you fold the arms in half
Change to Color A: and sc closed, you will have an
15. (4 sc, dec) x 3, 14 sc= 29 easier time when sewing them.
16. (dec, 7 sc) x 2, dec, 9 sc= 26
17. 3 sc, dec, 16 sc, dec, 3 sc= 24
Start stuffing the body
Change to Color E:
18. sc in each st around
19. 8 sc, dec, 4 sc, dec, 8 sc= 22
20. sc in each st around
Change to Color F:
21. dec, 8 sc, dec, 10 sc= 20
22. sc in each st around
23. (dec, 8 sc) x 2= 18
F/O and leave a long tail for sewing
Stinger:
With Color B:
1. Make 4 sc into a magic ring= 4
2. sc in each st around
3. (inc, sc) x 2= 6
4. sc in each st around
5. (inc, 2 sc) x 2= 8
6-7. sc in each st around
Start stuffing the stinger
8. (inc, 3 sc) x 2= 10
9-10. sc in each st around
F/O and leave a long tail for sewing
Sweet Oddity Art 4
Legs(Make 2):
Starting with Color B:
Ch 6
1. inc in 2nd chain from hook, 3 sc, 4 sc in the last chain, working on the opposite side of the
chain: 3 sc, inc= 14
*For help with working on the opposite side of the chain refer to page 18*
2. Inc3, 4 sc, inc3, 2 sc, inc3, 5 sc= 20
3. inc x 3, 5 sc, inc3, 4 sc, inc3, 6 sc= 27
Change to Color A:
4. sc, inc x 3, 8 sc, inc3, 6 sc, inc3, 7 sc= 34
5-7. sc in each st around
8. 17 sc, dec x 6, 5 sc= 28
Stuff the legs as you work
9. 16 sc, dec x 4, 4 sc= 24
10. 15 sc, dec x 4, sc= 20
11. 12 sc, dec x 4= 16
Stop stuffing the legs
12. (dec, 6 sc) x 2= 14
13. sc in each st around
14. (dec, 5 sc) x 2= 12
15. sc in each st around
16. (dec, 4 sc) x 2= 10
17. sc in each st around
F/O and leave a long tail for sewing
Antennaes(Make 2):
Starting with Color B:
1. Make 6 sc into a magic ring= 6
2. Increase in each st around= 12
3-4. sc in each st around
5. Dec x 6= 6
Change to Color A:
Do not stuff the antennaes from here on
6-12. sc in each st around
F/O and leave a long tail for sewing
Sweet Oddity Art 5
Wings(Make 4):
With Color G:
1. Make 6 sc into a magic ring= 6
2. (inc3, sc) x 3= 12
3. sc, (inc3, 3 sc) x 2, inc3, 2 sc= 18
4. 2 sc, (inc3, 5 sc) x 2, inc3, 3 sc= 24
5. 3 sc, (inc3, 7 sc) x 2, inc3, 4 sc= 30
Do not F/O the 3rd and 4th wings. Place the wings together with the back sides of each of them
facing each other. Start crocheting the wings together with the next round:
6. 4 sc, (inc3, 9 sc) x 2, inc3, 5 sc= 36
F/O and leave a long tail for sewing
*I originally was going to use one gray wing and one blue but decided to change my mind which
is why the 3rd picture is different.*
Sweet Oddity Art 6
Crown:
With Color F:
Ch 12, join with a sl st to the 1st chain to make a ring. Make sure not to get your chain twisted
when making a ring.
1-2. sc in each st around
3. (Ch 3, sl st in the 2nd chain from hook, sc in the next chain, sc in the next st on the crown)
Repeat around
(You will have 6 crown points total)
F/O and leave a long tail for sewing
Sweet Oddity Art 7
Assembly
Head and Body:
1. Cut a long strand of white embroidery thread. Insert the needle into a hole on the
side of the head. Bring the needle up to a corner on the bottom of the eye. Insert the
needle into a hole around to the top of the eye. Make sure you do not pull the thread
too tightly. Repeat on the 2nd eye and weave in the tails.
2. Sew the head to the body. You may need to add stuffing when you get to the last few
stitches to close.
Sweet Oddity Art 8
Sweet Oddity Art 9
Antennae:
1. Optional: Cut a piece of pipe cleaner in half. Fold the half in half again and twist.
Insert the pipe cleaner into the lower half of the antenannae. Cut any excess off.
You can choose to stuff them instead.
2. Pin the antennaes onto the head approximately between rounds 6 and 8.
3. Sew the antennaes onto the head.
Sweet Oddity Art 10
Arms:
1. Pin the arms to the side of the body approximately between rounds 21 and 22.
2. Sew the arms onto the body in a forward facing angle.
Sweet Oddity Art 11
Legs:
1. Turn the body upside down with the front of the face facing away from you.
Pin the legs onto the bottom of the body approximately between rounds 4 and 5.
2. Sew the legs onto the body.
Sweet Oddity Art 12
Crown and Stinger:
1. Pin the crown onto the head in between the antennaes. Sew the crown onto the
head.
2. Pin the stinger onto the back of the body approximately between rounds 6 and 8.
Sew the stinger onto the back of the body.
Sweet Oddity Art 13
Wings:
1. Bring the tail of the yarn to a corner on the wings. Any corner will work.
2. Pin the wings onto the back of the body approximately between rounds 15 and 16.
3. Sew the wings onto the back of the body only at the one corner and 3 stitches on
each side. Make sure they are sturdy before you weave in the yarn tail.
Sweet Oddity Art 14
Cheeks and Eyebrows:
1. Thread your needle with a long strand of black thread. Insert the needle into a spot
on the side of the head and bring the needle up about 4 rounds above the eye.
Insert the needle one round down about 1 stitch away from the first spot to
Embroider your eyebrow. Repeat for the 2nd eyebrow.
2. Embroider a small smile using the same technique.
3. With some actual blush make some cheeks next to the eyes.
4. Optional: With a fabric marker, add some black freckles to the cheeks. You can also
do this with the french knot if wanted. Here is a tutorial on how to do the french knot.
https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pjI5yo656U4
Sweet Oddity Art 15
You now have your finished Bumble the Bee! Thank you for your purchase! If you have any
questions or concerns please email me at sweetoddityart@gmail.com or etsy convo me. I will
get back to you asap. Please share your finished bee with me as often as you want! I love seeing
them!
Sweet Oddity Art 16
Helpful Tips:
Exact Colors and Brand of Yarn Used:
1. Yellow: I love this yarn Buttercup
2. Purple: Red Heart Lavender
3. Blue: Red Heart Aqua
4. Green: I love this yarn Menthe
5. Orange: I love this yarn Coral
6. Pink: Red Heart Bubblegum
7. Blue: Red Heart Light Blue
You can use different eye and nose sizes. You might have to adjust the placements if you
change the sizes.
You can use different hook sizes and weights of yarn. It will just change the size of your bee and
you might need to adjust eye and nose placement.
How you stuff matters! The type of stuffing you use, how you stuff, all this matters on how your
bee turns out. I prefer Polyfil stuffing but you can use other types.
If you can not find the oval noses, triangle noses work great! They make it so cute! You can
embroider the nose as well! The first picture is of an embroidered nose with purple yarn. The
2nd picture nose is an 18 mm nose. This picture was from a tester named Dawn and Elizabeth.
Sweet Oddity Art 17
Additional Information
How to work on the opposite side of the chain:
This is an example picture!
1. Work the indicated amount of stitches across the first side of your chain
2. Turn the chain around and work the indicated amount on the opposite side of the chain
