Notes:
• This pattern is worked using an amigurumi style of crochet.
• It is worked in continuous rounds meaning you will not join at the end of a round with a slip stitch and chain one at
the beginning of the next round.
• A stitch marker will be helpful in marking the start of each round to help with keeping count.
• When decreasing stitches I use the invisible decrease method which uses the front loops of the stitches instead of
both loops. I think it helps to decrease the gaps between stitches on the decrease.
