Bunny Crème Egg Cover
Body.
MR 6 (6).
Rnd 1: Inc in every st (12).
Rnd 2: [DC, inc] rep 6 times (18).
Rnds 3 - 4: DC in every st (18).
Rnd 5: DC, [inc, DC 2] rep 5 times, inc, DC (24).
Rnds 6 - 12: DC in every st (24).
Rnd 13: DC, [dec, DC 2] rep 5 times, dec, DC (18).
Fasten off.
Ears.
Make 2.
MR 6 (6)
Rnd 1: [DC, inc] rep 3 times (9)
Rnd 2: [DC 2, inc] rep 3 times (12)
Rnds 3 - 8: DC in every st (12)
Rnd 9: [DC 2, dec] rep 3 times (9)
Rnd 10: DC in every st (9)
Fasten off leaving a tail to attach the ears.
Assembly.
To attach ears to the top of the head, using the tail, oversew the rows ends and starting from the MR and working out-
wards for 4 rounds sew the ears to the top of the body.
Nose.
Using pink, work a stitch twice over 2 stitches, 7 rows up from the bottom edge in the centre of the body.
Eyes.
Using black, work a stitch twice on either side of the nose, starting 1 stitch away from the nose and working it over 2
rows.
If you wish to make a stuffed bunny, work the body the same way and do not fasten it off.
Rnd 14: [DC, dec] rep 6 times (12)
Stuff body.
Rnd 15: [Dec] rep 6 times.
Fasten off leaving a tail. Close the hole by picking up the front loops of the 6 sts and pull closed using the tail.
Finish the bunny in the same way for the crème egg cover.
