BUNNY FENG | CATNAP CROCHET
This pattern uses US terminology.
All decreases in this pattern use the invisible decrease method, which I’d highly
recommend using. Unless stated otherwise, everything is crocheted in continuous
rounds, in a spiral. No need to close each row with a slip stitch. Crochet with tight
stitches, using a smaller hook to avoid holes.
Notes
This pattern is property of @catnapcrochet. You may not alter, copy, sell, or redistribute this
pattern or any part of it.
If you decide to post any photos of your creations made with this pattern, I would love for
you to tag me (@catnapcrochet) on TikTok/Instagram/YouTube) so I can see and share!
DISCLAIMER
: If you find any mistakes, or have any questions, please feel free to reach out
to me via email or dm (crochetcatnap@gmail.com). I am happy to help with whatever
questions you may have, and I will be updating this pattern as necessary if I find any
corrections need to be made! Thank you for your patience.
TIP
: If you find any of the directions unclear, try copy & pasting them into Chat GPT and it
can help explain the instructions more in depth. Otherwise feel free to reach out to me.
BUNNY FENG | CATNAP CROCHET
Arms
MAKE 2
using 1 strand of DK Peach yarn, 2mm hook
R1: MC 6sc (6)
R2: (2sc, 1inc) x2 (8)
R3: 8sc (8)
R4: color change to light pink, BLO 8ss (8)
(keep stitches looser slightly)
R5-8: 8sc (8)
R9: fold to close with 4ss
f/o, leaving enough yarn for sewing later
Legs
MAKE 2
using 1 strand of DK Grey yarn, 2mm hook
R1: MC, 6sc (6)
R2: 6inc (12)
R3: BLO 12sc (12)
R4: 12sc (12)
R5: color change to black, BLO 12ss (keep stitches looser) (12)
R6-7: 12sc (12)
Cut yarn & f/o, leaving enough yarn for sewing later
Repeat for second leg, but instead of f/o connect the two legs with a single
crochet, then continue the pattern on the next page…
BUNNY FENG | CATNAP CROCHET
Torso & Head
using 1 strand of DK black yarn, 2mm hook
R8: connect 2 legs as stated on the previous page, 24sc (24)
R9-12: 24sc (24)
R13: color change to light grey, BLO 24ss (24)
R14: 24sc (24)
R15: (2sc, 1dec) x6 (18)
R16-18: 18sc (18)
R19: color change to peach, BLO 18ss (18)
R20: 18sc (18)
R21: (2sc, 1inc) x6 (24)
R22: (3sc, 1inc) x6 (30)
R23: (4sc, 1inc) x6 (36)
R24: (5sc, 1inc) x6 (42)
R25: (6sc, 1inc) x6 (48)
R26-32: 48sc, add eyes around R29, about 8 stitches apart (48)
R33: (6sc, 1dec) x6 (42)
R34: (5sc, 1dec) x6 (36)
R35: (4sc, 1dec) x6 (30)
R36: (3sc, 1dec) x6 (24)
R37: (2sc, 1dec) x6, add stuffing (18)
R38: (1sc, 1dec) x6 (12)
R39: 6dec (6)
Sew closed, f/o and weave in ends
BUNNY FENG | CATNAP CROCHET
Jacket
using 1 strand of DK Light Pink yarn, 2mm hook
R1: ch10. Start in 2nd from hook. 8HDC back (8)
R2: ch1, turn, 8HDC (8)
R3: ch1, turn, 1HDC, ch6, then HDC into the 7th stitch
along, & one HDC into the next st (this creates the arm
hole) (8)
R4-8: ch1, turn 8HDC (8)
R9: Repeat steps in R3 to create the second armhole (8)
R10-12: ch1, turn, 8HDC (8)
f/o & weave in ends
Hood
using 1 strand of DK Light Pink yarn, 2mm hook, working in HDC
R1: MC, 8HDC (8)
R2: 8HDC-inc (16)
R3: (1HDC, 1HDC-inc) x8 (24)
R4: (2HDC, 1HDC-inc) x8 (32)
R5: (3HDC, 1HDC-inc) x8 (40)
R6-7: 40sc (40)
R8: (now working in rows), ch2, turn, 39HDC
R9-11: ch2, turn, 39HDC back.
cut yarn & f/o, leaving enough yarn for sewing later
BUNNY FENG | CATNAP CROCHET
Skirt
1 strand of DK Dark Pink yarn, 2mm hook
Turn doll upside down. Make a slip knot and
pull it through one of the FLO loops on the
back of the torso at R13. Start working
along this row around doing (1sc, 1inc) until
you make it back around to your starting
slip knot. Then do 4 rounds of HDC all
around to create the skirt.
Bunny Ears
MAKE 2
using 1 strand of DK Dark Pink yarn, 2mm hook
R1: (keep initial yarn tail long for sewing to the hoodie later)
ch16, turn, in 2nd from hook 1sc, then 14HDC
R2: ch1, turn, start in 2nd from hook, 14HDC back, end with a
ss
f/o & weave in ends
Bangs
using 1 strand of DK Black yarn, 2mm hook
Ch14. Turn work, in 2nd from hook, make 1ss. Make a ss into the
next ch, then ch12, turn, start in 3rd from hook, 10HDC. Ss to the
next skipped unworked st back on the ch.
Make 4 picot stitches along chain (1 picot = ch4, sc into 4th ch
from hook, ss to next skipped st on ch).
Finally make another ch12, turn, start in 3rd from hook, 10HDC. End with ss to ch, f/o
& leave enough yarn for sewing later
BUNNY FENG | CATNAP CROCHET
Assembling
& Extras
Nose: sew in the center of the face a few times over with
some peach yarn to create the nose
Face (optional): Sew some white yarn around the eyes for
the eye details. Sew some eyelashes and eyebrows using
black yarn. Add blush to cheeks
Sewing the body parts: I sewed the body parts as I went along:
- Sew the arms just under where the neck starts, one on either opposite side.
- Place the jacket around the body, with the arms through the armholes
- Sew the hoodie to the neck, just under where the head starts, positioning the neck in
the space in the hood which was left specifically for the neck in R8-11 of making the
hoodie. Sew the hoodie on so it can’t be removed off the plushie’s head
- Sew the bangs to the forehead, just under the top of the hoodie
- Sew the bunny ears to the top of the hoodie, one on either side
- Sew some pink yarn on the shoes in an ‘X’ shape to resemble shoelaces
- Sew some grey yarn in front of the neck and create a small bow
- Sew some white yarn to make 3 parallel lines along each of her sleeves
- Cut some white felt into a bunny head shape and glue/sew to the back of the jacket
BUNNY FENG | CATNAP CROCHET
