Chick Crème Egg Cover
Body.
MR 6 (6).
Rnd 1: Inc in every st (12).
Rnd 2: [DC, inc] rep 6 times (18).
Rnds 3 - 4: DC in every st (18).
Rnd 5: DC, [inc, DC 2] rep 5 times, inc, DC (24).
Rnds 6 - 12: DC in every st (24).
Rnd 13: DC, [dec, DC 2] rep 5 times, dec, DC (18).
Fasten off.
Wings.
Make 2.
MR 6 (6).
Rnd 1: Inc in every st (12).
Rnd 2: DC 3, (2 HTR, CH1, 2HTR), DC 8 (16).
Fasten off with a long tail to attach to the body.
Assembly.
To attach the wings to the body, using the tail, line the wings up with the last row of the body and sew on either side of
the body leaving the pointed end of the wing unsewn.
Beak.
Using pink, work a stitch twice over 2 stitches, 6 rows up from the bottom edge in the centre of the body.
Eyes.
Using black, work a stitch twice on either side of the beak, starting 1 stitch away from the beak and working it over 2
rows.
If you wish to make a stuffed chick, work the body the same way and do not fasten it off.
Rnd 14: [DC, dec] rep 6 times (12)
Stuff body.
Rnd 15: [Dec] rep 6 times.
Fasten off leaving a tail. Close the hole by picking up the front loops of the 6 sts and pull closed using the tail.
Finish the chick in the same way for the crème egg cover.
