Lisa Kingsley Designs;https://www.lovecrafts.com/en-gb/p/christmas-bauble-pillow-or-hanger-crochet-pattern-by-lisa-kingsley;"Abbreviations Used:
Sc - single crochet
2sc - increase (2 single crochet stitches in one stitch)
Sc2tog - decrease (turning 2 stitches into one stitch)
Hdc - half double crochet
Dc - double crochet
Page ␀1 of ␀4
Lisa Kingsley Designs
Sl st - slip stitch
*to* - repeat the directions inside the stars as directed
St - stitch
Ch1 - chain 1
MR - magic ring
Supplies Needed:
Red Heart Super Saver: Turqua
Red Heart Super Saver: Black
Red Heart Super Saver: White
Red Heart Super Saver: Blue Suede
Red Heart Super Saver: Grey
4 mm crochet hook
1 pair of 12 mm black safety eyes
Polyester stuffing
T-Pins used to hold your pieces together before sewing
Stitch markers
Bauble Panel - Made with Turqua (Make 2)
Round 1) MR - 6 sc in the loop (6 st)
Round 2) 2sc in each st around (12 st)
Round 3) *sc in the next st, 2sc in the next st* repeat *to* all around (18 st)
Round 4) *sc in the next 2 st, 2sc in the next st* repeat *to* all around (24 st)
Round 5) *sc in the next 3 st, 2sc in the next st* repeat *to* all around (30 st)
Round 6) *sc in the next 4 st, 2sc in the next st* repeat *to* all around (36 st)
Round 7) *sc in the next 5 st, 2sc in the next st* repeat *to* all around (42 st)
Round 8) *sc in the next 6 st, 2sc in the next st* repeat *to* all around (48 st)
Round 9) *sc in the next 7 st, 2sc in the next st* repeat *to* all around (54 st)
Round 10) *sc in the next 8 st, 2sc in the next st* repeat *to* all around (60 st)
Round 11) *sc in the next 9 st, 2sc in the next st* repeat *to* all around (66 st)
Round 12) *sc in the next 10 st, 2sc in the next st* repeat *to* all around (72 st)
Round 13) *sc in the next 11 st, 2sc in the next st* repeat *to* all around (78 st)
Round 14) *sc in the next 12 st, 2sc in the next st* repeat *to* all around (84 st)
Round 15) *sc in the next 13 st, 2sc in the next st* repeat *to* all around (90 st)
Round 16) *sc in the next 14 st, 2sc in the next st* repeat *to* all around (96 st)
Round 17) *sc in the next 15 st, 2sc in the next st* repeat *to* all around (102 st)
Round 18) *sc in the next 16 st, 2sc in the next st* repeat *to* all around (108 st)
Round 19) *sc in the next 17 st, 2sc in the next st* repeat *to* all around (114 st)
Round 20) *sc in the next 18 st, 2sc in the next st* repeat *to* all around (120 st)
The next section is worked in rows - you will be forming the bottom of the bauble:
Row 1) sc2tog, then sc in the next 6 st, ch1 and turn
Row 2) sc2tog, then sc in the next 4 st, ch1 and turn
Row 3) sc2tog, then sc in the next 3 st, ch1 and turn
Row 4) sc2tog, then sc in the next 2 st, ch1 and turn
Row 5) sc2tog, sc in the next st, ch1 and turn
Row 6) sc2tog
Page ␀2 of ␀4
Lisa Kingsley Designs
Fasten off the first panel only. Once you have the second panel complete, set it aside for now
and do not fasten off.
Nose - Made with Blue Suede
Round 1) Chain 6 - starting in the second chain from hook, sc in the next 4 st, 3 sc in the last
chain, working under the foundation chain, sc in the next 3 st, 3 sc in the last stitch (13 st)
Round 2) *sc in the next 3 st, 2sc* repeat two more times, then sc in the last st (16 st)
Fasten off leaving a long tail. Using a length of white yarn, stitch the highlight on the upper right
side of the nose.
* Once you have the eyes attached to the Present, sew the nose just below them.
Eyes - Made with White yarn (Make 2)
Round 1) Chain 2 - 8 hdc into the second chain from hook (8 st)
Round 2) 2sc in each st around (16 st)
Round 3) 2 hdc into the next st, 2sc into the next st, sl st in the next 2 st, leave the remaining
stitches unworked
Fasten off leaving a long tail. Insert safety eyes - (do not attach the backs yet) into the eye ovals
between rounds 1 and 2 (FYI the hdc stitches from round 3 are the top of the eyes). Place the
ovals onto the front of one of the Bauble panels - (use the magic ring or circle as a guide) and
insert the backs through the present panel as well. Once you are satisfied with the eye
placement attach the backs of the safety eyes.
* Once you have the eyes and nose sewn on, using black yarn, stitch the eyebrows and smile
onto the Bauble. (See photo for placement).
* Once you have the face sewn on fold the panel in half lengthwise to find the centre at the top
of the Bauble - mark the centre stitch with a stitch marker (see photo below).
Top of the Bauble - Made with Grey yarn
Row 1) Using grey yarn, join at the 6th stitch to the right of the stitch marker, sc in the same
stitch and then sc in the next 11 st. (12 st) Ch1 and turn
Rows 2 to 5) sc in each st across (total of 4 rows) Ch1 and turn
Fasten off after row 5 and weave in your ends.
Repeat the above steps for the second panel.
Assembly:
* Place the top panel on top of the second panel (wrong sides facing) and using the yarn you left
earlier, sc in each st around joining the 2 pieces together. When you get to the grey area, fasten
off the blue yarn and join the grey yarn, sc in each st, except for the corners do 3 sc. Once you
have completed the grey area, rejoin the blue yarn and continue to work your way all of the way
around. Do not forget the stuff the piece before closing :)
Hanger - Make this only if you are going to hang your pillow - Made with Grey yarn
Chain 25, join with a sl st to form a ring. Fasten off leaving a long tail. Sew to the back of the top
of the Bauble.
Page ␀3 of ␀4
Lisa Kingsley Designs
Ribbon - Made with Blue Suede.
Chain 75 - fasten off. Wrap around the base of the grey area of the Bauble and tie into a bow.
