CHRISTMAS PUDDING
Christmas Pudding measures about 12cm across
Short and sweet, cute enough to eat! This Christmas Pudding is great for those looking to make
some Holiday treats for loved ones. It won’t take you very long to make and really puts me in the
Christmas spirit. :)
Please do not alter, use images or claim this pattern as your own. Copyright ©anniegurumi 2020.
For requests to use this copyright-protected work in any matter, email:
asst.anniegurumi@gmail.com
Please be sure to tag me on social media (@anniegurumi) and Paintbox Yarns
(@paintboxyarns). Please use #anniegurumi so I can see your Christmas Pudding. Thank you for
enjoying my pattern.
!1
CHRISTMAS PUDDING BY: ANNIEGURUMI
Skill Level: Intermediate Beginner Stitches: (US Crochet Terms)
Materials: MR: magic ring
Paintbox Yarns One Ball in Each Colour: Paper White, ch: chain
Grass Green, Pillar Red and Soft Fudge sc: single crochet
Crochet Hook: 3.25mm inc: single crochet increase
Amigurumi Eyes: 2 count (9mm) hdc: half double crochet
Brads: 2 count in red (5mm) st: stitches
Tapestry Needle, Glue, Stuffing sl st: slip stitch
bb: back bump
FO: fasten off
Body [Make one]
Using Brown Yarn:
R1: MR 6 R21: (sc 8, dec) x6
R22: (sc 7, dec) x6 [52]
R2: inc around [12]
R23: (sc 6, dec) x6 [48]
R3: (sc, inc) x6 [18]
R4: (sc 2, inc) x6 [24] R24: (sc 5, dec) x6 [42]
R25: (sc 4, dec) x6 [36]
R5: (sc 3, inc) x6 [30]
R6: (sc 4, inc) x6 [36] Stuff semi firmly as you go
R26: (sc 3, dec) x6
R7: (sc 5, inc) x6 [42]
R27: (sc 2, dec) x6
R8: (sc 6, inc) x6 [48]
R9: (sc 7, inc) x6 [52] R28: (sc, dec) x6
R29: dec around
R10: (sc 8, inc) x6 [60]
R11-20: sc around [10 rounds] FO. Weave in all ends.
Squish the body by pressing the top and
Embroider a smile on R13, add eyes
bottom so it is more of a tall pancake
between R14-15, 3-4 stitches above smile.
Add red brads between R13-14 next to eyes. shape.
Secure with glue.
!2
CHRISTMAS PUDDING BY: ANNIEGURUMI
Leaves [Make three or more]
Using Green Yarn:
ch 7, sl st in 2nd ch from hook through bb, (sl st through bb,
ch 2, sl st in same bb), sl st in next 2 back bumps, ch 3, sl st
in same bb, sl st in next bb, 3 sl st in next bb.
working on other side of the ch:
sl st in next 2 st, ch 3, sl st in current st, sl st in next, ch 2, sl
st in same, sl st in last.
FO leaving long tail for sewing.
Berries [Make three or more]
Using Red Yarn:
R1: MR 4
Clean FO and leave a long tail for sewing.
Icing [Make one]
Using White Yarn:
R1: MR 6 [6]
R2: inc around [12]
R3: (sc, inc) x6 [18]
R4: (sc 2, inc) x6 [24]
R5: (sc 3, inc) x6 [30]
R6: (sc 4, inc) x6 [36]
R7: (sc 5, inc) x6 [42]
R8-9: sc,hdc in next 2 st, sc in next 3st, hdc,
sc, hdc, sc, hdc in next 2 st, sc in next 2 st, hdc
in next 3 st, sc in next 4 st, hdc in next 5 st, sc
in next 6 st, hdc in 8 st, sc in last 2 st. [2
rounds]
FO leaving long tail for sewing.
!3
CHRISTMAS PUDDING BY: ANNIEGURUMI
Assembly:
Sew Leaves onto the top of the icing, then the berries. Place Icing onto the top of the head
(around R21-29). Weave in all ends. Please use picture for reference.
Congratulations! You did it :) Hope you enjoyed this pattern and have a wonderful Christmas!
Feel free to sell the final product in small quantities but please include the following in your listing:
“Christmas Pudding designed by ©anniegurumi. http://anniegurumi.com”
Find more patterns here: Etsy , Love Crochet :) Thank you again from the bottom of my heart.
<3
