CHRISTMAS TREE DOLL;https://www.lovecrafts.com/en-gb/p/christmas-tree-amigurumi-crochet-free-crochet-patterns-crochet-pattern-cute-crochet-pattern-by-kathy-leung;"Abbreviations
MR = Magic Ring
Rnd = Round
SC = Single Crochet
HDC = Half Double Crochet
DC = Double Crochet
INC = Increase (2 Single Crochets in the same stitch)
DC INC = Increase Double Crochet (2 Double Crochets in the same stitch)
DEC= Decrease SC (Crochet 2 Single Crochets together)
CH = Chain
ST / STS = Stitch / Stitches
SL ST = Slip Stitch
SK = Skip
FLO = Front Loops Only
BLO = Back Loops Only
FO = Fasten Off
Head
Use Nude yarn.
Rnd 1: 6 SC in magic ring [6]
Rnd 2: 6 INC [12]
Rnd 3: (INC, SC) x6 [18]
Rnd 4: (2 SC, INC) x6 [24]
Rnd 5: (3 SC, INC) x6 [30]
Rnd 6: (2 SC, INC, 2 SC) x6 [36]
Rnd 7: (5 SC, INC) x6 [42]
Rnd 8-14: 42 SC [42], 7 rounds
Rnd 15: (5 SC, DEC) x6 [36]
Rnd 16: (2 SC, DEC, 2 SC) x6 [30]
Rnd 17: (3 SC, DEC) x6 [24]
Rnd 18: (2 SC, DEC) x6 [18]
Rnd 19: (DEC, SC) x6 [12]
Rnd 20: 6 DEC [6]
Stuff the head firmly.
Fasten off
Head Covering
Use Green yarn.
Rnd 1: 6 SC in magic ring [6]
Rnd 2: 6 INC [12]
Rnd 3: 12 SC [12]
Rnd 4: (INC, SC) x6 [18]
Rnd 5: BLO 18 SC [18]
Rnd 6: (2 SC, INC) x6 [24]
Rnd 7: 24 SC [24]
Rnd 8: (3 SC, INC) x6 [30]
Rnd 9: 30 SC [30]
Rnd 10: (2 SC, INC, 2 SC) x6 [36]
Rnd 11: BLO 36 SC [36]
Rnd 12: (5 SC, INC) x6 [42]
Rnd 13: 42 SC [42]
Rnd 14: BLO 42 SC [42]
Rnd 15: 42 SC [42]
Rnd 16: 32 SC, SK 10 [32] Ch 1, Turn
Rnd 17: BLO 32 SC [32] Ch 1, Turn
Rnd 18-19: 32 SC [32] Ch 1, Turn
Rnd 20: BLO 32 SC [32] Ch 1, Turn
Rnd 21-24: 32 SC [32] Ch 1, Turn
Rnd 25: 32 SC, Ch 10 [32]
Rnd 26: (5 SC, DEC) x6 [36]
Rnd 27: (2 SC, DEC, 2 SC) x6 [30]
Rnd 28: (3 SC, DEC) x6 [24]
Rnd 29: (2 SC, DEC) x6 [18]
Rnd 30: (SC, DEC) x6 [12]
Rnd31: 6 DEC [6]
Fasten off
Leaf
Use Green yarn.
Crochet on the FLO of Head Covering: *SC, SK 1, [5 HDC], SL ST*,
repeat between *’s to the end of round.
Tip: 5 HDC are worked on the same stitch.
Star
Use Yellow yarn.
Rnd 1: 10 SC in magic ring
Rnd 2: * [Ch 4, start in second chain from the hook, SL ST, SC, HDC],
SK 1, SL ST *, repeat between *’s 5 times
Cut the yarn, leaving a long tail for sewing.
Small Bang (make 2)
Use Brown yarn.
Rnd 1: 6 SC in magic ring [6]
Cut the yarn, leaving a long tail for sewing.
Large Bang
Use Brown yarn.
Rnd 1: 8 SC in magic ring [8]
Cut the yarn, leaving a long tail for sewing.
Red Rope
Use Red yarn: Ch 40
