CHRISTMAS TREE
Christmas Tree measures about 10 cm tall
Happy Holidays! I hope this quick and easy pattern for my Christmas Tree finds you well :) Add
some pom poms or jingles for a festive treat.
Please be sure to tag me on social media (@anniegurumi) and use #anniegurumi so I can see
your Christmas Tree. Thank you for enjoying my pattern. Please come by instagram and say hi, I
am very active there. :)
1
CHRISTMAS TREE PATTERN BY: ANNIEGURUMI
Skill Level: Intermediate
Materials:
Hobium Yarns - La Mia Cottony in Green
Crochet Hook 3.25mm
Tapestry Needle
Stitches: (US Crochet Terms)
MR: magic ring
ch: chain
sc: single crochet
inc: increase
sl st: slip stitch
BLO: back loop only
FL: Front Loop
FO: fasten off
Tree:
starting from top to bottom (BLO rows are indicated); then tree is worked bottom up.
R1: 6sc in MR (6)
R2: sc around
R3: BLO (inc, sc in next) repeat (9)
R4: sc around
R5: BLO (inc, sc in next 2 stitches) repeat (12)
R6: sc around
R7: BLO (inc, sc in next 3 stitches) repeat (15)
R8: sc around
R9: BLO (inc, sc in next 4 stitches) repeat (18)
R10: sc around
R11: BLO (inc, sc in next 5 stitches) repeat (21)
R12: sc around
R13: BLO (inc, sc in next 6 stitches) repeat (24)
R14: sc aroundc
R15: BLO (inc, sc in next 7 stitches) repeat (27)
R16: sc around
2
CHRISTMAS TREE PATTERN BY: ANNIEGURUMI
R17: BLO (inc, sc in next 8 stitches) repeat (30)
R18: sc around
R19: BLO (inc, sc in next 9 stitches) repeat (33)
R20: sc around
R21: BLO (inc, sc in next 10 stitches) repeat (36)
R22: (inc, sc in next 11 stitches) repeat (39)
R23: BLO sc around and sl st to next st. DO NOT FASTEN OFF
-ch 4, sc in the first FL (front loop) on the left of your chain, ch 5, sc in next FL.
(ch5, sc in next FL)* repeat for every FL in the same manner till you reach the very last FL stitch
at the top of the tree. ch 4 and sl st into the centre top of tree. FO and weave in all ends.
3
CHRISTMAS TREE PATTERN BY: ANNIEGURUMI
Glue pom poms or sew in mini jingle bells for a festive treat! :) Makes an adorable little hat for
your favourite amigurumi.
*Please be careful for children under 3 years of age. Pom poms and jingles can be a choking
hazard.
