AMIGURUMI PATTERN;https://www.lovecrafts.com/en-gb/p/cornish-pixie-amigurumi-crochet-pattern-by-monchou-designs;;"AMIGURUMI PATTERN
Worked in worsted weight yarns, this
mischievous menace has wired limbs and
works up in just 3-4 hours, ready to play pranks
and cause all sorts of magical havoc.
Yarns::
Notions:
Worsted or Light Worsted Weight Yarns:
Size E (3.5 mm) crochet hook
(A) Blue - 10 metres
Stitch marker
(B) White - 6 metres
Sewing needle & thread
2 x 8mm black safety eyes
Polyester stuffing
Finished Size: 5 inches tall
16 gauge wire - found at hardware stores
Level: Advanced Beginner
Wire cutters
Skills: crochet, basic hand sewing Scraps of light blue and white embroidery floss
Completion time: 3-4 hours Clear-drying craft glue
• This amigurumi pattern is crocheted in the round, beginning at the foot and finishing at
the crown of the head.
• A stitch marker is recommended to mark the start of each round.
• Amigurumi requires that you maintain strong tension as you work to keep your stitches
tight and give the doll form.
• After finishing off, hide yarn ends by pulling them to the inside of the doll.
• In some photos parts from a different doll are shown because the dark blue yarn is
sometimes harder to see in photos.
Key: (US crochet terms)
tc: treble crochet
ch: chain
sl st: slip stitch
sc: single crochet
rep: repeat
hdc: half double crochet
rnd: round
dc: double crochet
sc2tog: single crochet 2 sts together
Instructions
Body: Using blue yarn (A)
Rnd # Details Total # of sts
1 Make an adjustable ring, ch 1, sc 6 into the ring. Pull closed. (6)
2 Work 2sc into each st to end of rnd. (12)
*insert a stitch marker to keep track of the row starting spot, move marker up after each rnd
3 *(sc into next st, 2sc into next st) rep from * to end of rnd. (18)
4 Sc BLO into each st to end of rnd. (18)
5 Sc into each st to end of rnd. (18)
6 Sc into next 2 sts, sc2tog 7 times, sc into next two sts. (11)
7-12 Sc into each st to end of rnd, fasten off. (11)
Repeat rnds 1-12 for second leg, do not fasten off.
Sc into next 3 sts until you are at the side of the leg, then sc into st 8 on
13
the other leg to join them (this will be the middle of the inner leg)
2
Continue to sc around both legs to make one round. (22)
Cut a 7-inch piece of wire. Bend it in half and then twist each end into
a loop and bend at a 90 degree angle to create a skeleton for the legs
and feet. Insert into the legs of the doll, and loosely add stuffing into
the legs. There’s no need to stuff the feet, your doll will stand better
without it.
14 Sc into next 9 sts, sc2tog, sc into next 9 sts, sc2tog. (20)
15 *(sc into next 3 sts, sc2tog), rep from * to end of rnd. (16)
16-17 Sc into each st to end of rnd. (16)
18 *(sc into next 6 sts, sc2tog), rep from * to end of rnd. (14)
19 *(sc into next 5 sts, sc2tog), rep from * to end of rnd. (12)
20-21 Sc into each st to end of rnd. (12)
Finish stuffing the body.
22 Sc2tog 6 times. (6)
23 2sc into each st to end of rnd. (12)
24 2sc into each st to end of rnd. (24)
25 *(sc into next 11 sts, 2sc into next st) rep from * to end of rnd. (26)
26-29 Sc into each st to end of rnd. (26)
3
Pause and insert eyes between rows 28 & 29, 3 sts apart, centred in the
front of the face.
30 Sc2tog 13 times. (13)
Begin firmly stuffing the head.
31 Sc2tog 6 times, sc into next st. (7)
Finish stuffing the head.
32 Sc2tog until the opening is closed, fasten off.
Arms (make two) - using blue yarn (A):
Rnd # Details Total # of sts
1 Ch 6 and join with a sl st to make a circle, sc into each st to end of rnd. (6)
2-7 Sc into each st to end of rnd. (6)
8 Sc2tog, sc into each st to end of rnd. (5)
Sl st into first st. Ch 3, sl st into second ch from hook, sl st into next
9
ch.
Next, insert hook into the next st, and then continue through st 5,
coming in from the back, and pulling yarn back through and making a
sl st.
Ch 3. Sl st into second ch from hook and into next ch. Again, insert
hook into next st, and continue through and insert into st 4 on the
round, coming in from the back. Pull the yarn through to make a sl
st.
4
Ch 3. Sl st into second ch from hook and the next ch. Insert hook
into the post directly below, (rnd 8), make a sl st and fasten off.
Attaching arms to body:
Cut a 6-inch length of wire. Twist one end into a small loop, and
insert that end into one of the arms. The loop should rest at the
wrist, and not push all the way into the hand or it will poke through.
Next, insert the other end of the wire through the shoulder area and through the body, coming
out on the other side in the corresponding st. Twist the remaining end of the wire into a loop
and then insert it into the remaining arm. Pin both arms in place on the body. Using a needle
and thread, stitch the arms to the body.
Ears (make 2) - Using blue yarn (A)
Rnd # Total # of sts
1 Make an adjustable ring, ch 1, sc 4 into the ring. Pull closed. (4)
2 *(2sc into next st, sc into next st), rep from * to end of rnd. (6)
3 *(2sc into next st, sc into next st), rep from * to end of rnd. (9)
4 *(2sc into next st, sc into next 2 sts), rep from * to end of rnd. (12)
5 Sc into each st to end of rnd, fasten off. (12)
Use a needle and thread to stitch the two edges of the ear together so it lays flat,
and bend it into a bit of a crescent.
5
Pin ears to the head and stitch in place as shown.
Antennae (make 2) - using blue yarn (A)
Rnd # Total # of sts
1 Make an adjustable ring, ch 1, sc 6 into the ring, pull closed. (6)
2-3 Sc into each st to end of rnd. (6)
4 Sc2tog 3 times. (3)
5 Sc into each st to end of rnd, fasten off. (3)
Position antennae on the top of the head as shown, stitch or glue in
place.
Lower Wings (make 2) - Using white yarn (B)
Row # Total # of sts
1 Ch 9. Sc into 2nd ch from hook, hdc into next ch, dc into next 3 chs, tc into next (8)
3 chs, fasten off.
Upper Wings (make 2) - Using white yarn (B)
Row # Total # of sts
1 Ch 12. Sc into 2nd ch from hook, hdc into next 2 chs, dc into next 3 chs, tc into (11)
next 5 chs, fasten off.
6
Stitch or glue the wings on the back as shown, first
placing the lower wings, with the tips pointing
downward, and then adding the upper wings with
the tips pointing upward.
Face:
Use a length of blue yarn and a yarn needle to make a few
small stitches for a nose.
Glue a small piece of light blue embroidery floss to the face for
the mouth and two shorter pieces over the eyes for eyebrows.
Using white embroidery floss, make two small stitches at the
bottom of the mouth as teeth.
Congratluations, your pixie is complete!
