Gauge: 5cm x 5cm = 11 sts over 12 rows
Finished size = approximately 10.5cm high x 6.5cm wide (15cm circumference at widest)
©Sam Pratt @EmmieGeorge and EmmieGeorgeDesigns
Head and Body (worked in one piece)
Work in rounds and slip stitch in top of first stitch at the end of each round.
With white yarn
Rnd 1: DC 6 in MR (6sts).
Rnd 2: DC 2 in each DC (12sts).
Rnd 3: (DC 1, DC2 in same stitch) x 6 (18sts).
Rnd 4: (DC 2, DC2 in same stitch) x 6 (24sts).
Rnds 5-9: DC 1 in each stitch to end (24sts).
Add safety eyes between Rnds 6 & 7. Stuff head.
Rnd 10: (DC 2, DC2tog) x 6 (18sts).
Rnd 11: DC 1 in each stitch to end (18sts)
Rnd 12: (Armhole row) DC 3, ch3, miss next 3 stitches, DC 6, ch3, miss next 3
stitches, DC 3 (12sts & 6ch)
Rnd 13: DC 3, (working in back loop of chain) DC 1 in each of the next 3 chain,
DC 6, (working in back loop of chain) DC 1 in each of the next 3 chain, DC 3
(18sts).
Rnds 14-15: DC 1 in each stitch to end (18sts).
Rnd 16: (DC, DC2tog) x 6 (12sts).
Rnds 17-18: DC 1 in each stitch to end (12sts).
Rnd 19: (DC2tog) x 6 (6sts).
Rnds 20-21: DC 1 in each stitch to end (6sts).
Stuff body.
Rnd 22: (DC 1, DC2 in same stitch) x 2 (4sts).
Rnds 23: DC 1 in each stitch. (4sts).
Fasten off.
Arms (x 2).
With white yarn, join to edge of armhole space.
Rnd 1: (work along top, then bottom) DC 3, DC2 in each of the next 3sts (9sts).
Rnds 2-4: DC 1 in each stitch to end. Slst in first stitch (9sts).
Rnd 5: DC, (DC2tog) x 3 (6sts).
Rnd6: (DC2tog, DC) x2 (4sts).
Fasten off.
Repeat for second arm.
©Sam Pratt @EmmieGeorge and EmmieGeorgeDesigns
Make up
Sew through Row 10 and pull tightly to shape head/body.
To make a loop, attach yarn to Rnd 1 of head, chain 10, slst in starting point.
Fasten off.
