pg. 3
Happy Face Keyring | © Created by CraftyChick 2021
Using your black thread embroider on your happy face, I
use pins to mark out where I like things to go first to help
make things symmetrical.
Start by threading your needle and taking through the
bottom of the eye where you want to start, take the
needle up (through the inside of your keyring), to the top
of that same eye and bring it back down, (on the outside)
now take the needle over to the top of the other eye
(through the inside) and bring it down to the bottom of
the eye. (on the outside)
Take the needle to the start of the mouth, and following the pins embroider
the smile on in the same way. If you are happy with the placement of the face, take the
needle back to where you started on the first eye (through the inside). Tie the two
ends together with a granny knot, nice and close to the surface of the keyring, now
take each thread out through the side of the face. Cut your leftover threads.
Tie off the yarn at the bottom of your key ring where you started.
You are done!
