To keep track of the beginning of the rounds, use a stitch marker. Here you can watch a video
on how to use a scrap piece of yarn as a stitch marker
(click on the link or scan QR code): https://youtu.be/Vs--AuI9l-c
Crocheting through the back and front loops
Each stitch looks like a V with the top of the V pointing in the direction of the hook and the bottom
of the V pointing away from the hook. Each side of the V is one of the loops. When you form regular
stitches, you insert the hook through both loops. With the hook in loops of the stitch, you can see
one loop closer to you (the front loop) and one loop farther from you (the back loop). For front loop
crochet, insert your hook through the front loop only and complete the stitch as you normally would.
For back loop crochet, insert your hook through the back loop only and complete the stitch as you
normally would.
Here you can watch the video about crocheting through the back and front loops
(click on the link or sсan QR code): https://youtu.be/STZeF6zOmLc
