Fold the blue part
in half and using
the tail end sew
together as shown
in the picture.
Written by Veronika Cromwell, Blue Star Crochet Company
LEGS
Make 2
ROUND 1- Using White yarn start with a magic circle, work 6sc into the magic
circle, sl st to 1st sc (6sc)
ROUND 2- Ch1, work 2sc in each sc around, sl st to 1st sc (12sc)
ROUND 3- Ch1, * [work 1sc, 2sc in next sc] *, repeat from * to * around, sl st to
1st sc (18sc)
ROUND 4- Ch1, * [work 2sc, 2sc in next sc] *, repeat from * to * around, sl st to
1st sc (24sc)
ROUND 5- Ch1, * [work 3sc, 2sc in next sc] *, repeat from * to * around, sl st to
1st sc (30sc)
ROUND 6 – ROUND 17- ch1, work 30sc around, sl st to 1st sc
ROW 18- ch1, work 20sc leaving the remaining 10sc unworked, TURN YOUR
WORK AND CONTINUE WORKING IN ROWS
ROW 19 – ROW 28- repeat ROW 18
Turn the foot inside out, fold the 10 rows of 20sc in half and sl st across to
finish off the heel of the foot. Fasten off.
Turn the foot back the right way out.
ROUND 1- Join White yarn in the 1st missed sc of ROW 18, ch1, work the 10
missed sc, working into the end of each row around work 20sc, sl st to 1st sc
(30sc)
ROUND 2- Ch1, * [work 3sc, sc2tog] *, repeat from * to * around, sl st to 1st sc
(24sc)
ROUND 3- Ch1, * [work 2sc, sc2tog] *, repeat from * to * around, sl st to 1st sc
(18sc)
Change to Denim
ROUND 4- Ch1, * [work 1sc, sc2tog] *, repeat from * to * around, sl st to 1st sc
(12sc)
ROUND 5 – ROUND 9- ch1, work 12sc around, sl st to 1st sc
Written by Veronika Cromwell, Blue Star Crochet Company
Fasten off leaving a longer tail. Stuff with the filling and sew onto the bottom
of the body.
NOSE
ROUND 1- Using Denim yarn start with a magic circle, work 6sc into the magic
circle, sl st to 1st sc (6sc)
ROUND 2- Ch1, work 2sc in each sc around, sl st to 1st sc (12sc)
ROUND 3 – ROUND 4- ch1, work 12sc around, sl st to 1st sc
Fasten off leaving a longer tail. Stuff a little and using the tail sew onto the face
referring to the photos for placement.
ARMS
Make 2
ROUND 1- Using Denim yarn start with a magic circle, work 6sc into the magic
circle, sl st to 1st sc (6sc)
ROUND 2- Ch1, work 2sc in each sc around, sl st to 1st sc (12sc)
ROUND 3- Ch1, * [work 1sc, 2sc in next sc] *, repeat from * to * around, sl st to
1st sc (18sc)
ROUND 4- ch1, work 3sc, ch3, skip the following 3sc, work the remaining 12sc,
sl st to 1st sc (15sc + ch3 space)
ROUND 5- ch1, work 3sc, 1sc into each chain stitch of the ch3, work the
remaining 12sc, sl st to 1st sc (18sc)
ROUND 6- ch1, work 18sc around, sl st to the 1st sc (18sc)
ROUND 7- ch1, * [1sc, sc2tog] *, repeat from * to * around, sl st to 1st sc (12sc)
ROUND 8- ch1, * [1sc, sc2tog] *, repeat from * to * around, sl st to 1st sc (8sc)
ROUND 9- ch1, work 8sc around, sl st to the 1st sc (8sc)
ROUND 10- ch1, * [1sc, 2sc in next sc] *, repeat from * to * around, sl st to the
1st sc (12sc)
Written by Veronika Cromwell, Blue Star Crochet Company
ROUND 11 – ROUND 30- ch1, work 12sc around, sl st to 1st sc
Fasten off leaving a longer tail.
THUMB
ROUND 1- Join Denim yarn in the 1st missed sc of the thumb opening, ch1,
work 6sc around the opening, sl st to 1st sc (6sc)
ROUND 2 – ROUND 4- ch1, work 6sc around, sl st to 1st sc
Fasten off leaving a longer tail. Use the tail to sew up the top of the thumb and
sew in the end.
Stuff the arm and palm, using the tail end sew onto the body referring to the
photos for the placement.
Using the photos as reference embroider the mouth with needle using black
yarn.
