“Disco Dave started life as a knitted monster designed for
Tension: Let’s Knit Magazine, (can you see him lurking in the back-
20sts x 20rows = 10cm x 10cm ground?) I felt he needed a crochet buddy so I hooked up a
using 3.5mm hook and dc friend!
Abbreviation: Dave is worked using the amigurumi principle, using only
Dc2tog: insert hook in next st, yoh, double crochet and working in a continuous spiral. He is a
pull through st, rep from * once, perfect beginners amigurumi project. There are a couple of
yoh, pull through all three loops on really great video links below if you need some help getting
hook
started.
Happy hooking!” Jane
