Pattern;https://www.lovecrafts.com/en-gb/p/doll-amigurumi-crochet-pattern-by-nadinadolls;"Abbreviations:
ch – chain
sc – single crochet
dc – double crochet
sl st – slip stitch
inc – increase
dec – decrease
rnd – round
Materials and Instruments:
- crochet hook № 4;
- cotton yarn of beige or light brown colour;
- polyester yarn of white colour;
- acrylic yarn of blue, navy blue, brown and white colour;
- fiberfill for stuffing;
- eyes, buttons or beads;
- some cross-stitching threads of red and black colour and buttons.
NB: Final size of a knitted toy depends on the size of crochet hook and thread
thickness. The beginning of the round is marked by a colour thread. All details are
knitted as rounds. The glue PVA is not used if children are going to play with this
doll.
Head (beige/light brown yarn)
1 rnd – 2 ch, 6 sc in the same stitch (6)
2 rnd – 6 inc (12)
3 rnd – (1 sc, inc) around (18)
4 rnd – (2 sc, inc) around (24)
5 rnd – (3 sc, inc) around (30)
6 rnd – (4 sc, inc) around (36)
7 rnd – (5 sc, inc) around (42)
8-20 rnds – 13 rnd around (42)
21 rnd – (5 sc, dec) around (36)
22 rnd – (4 sc, dec) around (30)
23 rnd – (1 sc, dec) around (20)
24 rnd – 10 dec around(10)
25-27 rnds – 3 rnd around (10)
Stuff the detail.
Body (white cotton yarn)
28 rnd – (4 sc, inc) around (12)
29 rnd – inc, 4 sc, 2 inc, 4 sc, inc (16)
Then knit with blue yarn.
30 rnd – (1 sc, inc) around (24)
31 rnd – inc, 9 sc, inc, 1 sc, inc, 9 sc, inc, 1 sc (28)
32 rnd – inc, 13 sc, inc, 1 sc, inc, 13 sc, inc, 1 sc (32)
33 rnd – around (32)
34-35 rnds. – 7 sc, inc, 15 sc, inc, 4 sc. At the same time we begin to knit the body
and arms at the end of this rnd. The last 4 sc do not to be knitted, leave them; also
leave 3 sc at the beginning of the next rnd. As a result 7 sc are not to be knitted. Knit
the next 10 sc, then leave 7 sc, 10 sc. According to this scheme of knitting 7 stitches
are for the arms, and 20 stitches are for the body.
35 rnd – mark with any thread the beginning of the rnd and knit around in back only.
(20)
36 rnd – around (20) and cut the thread.
Arms
Join a blue thread to the beginning of the rnd.
1-10 rnds – around (7) and cut the thread at the end.
11 rnd – work with the beige yarn in back only. 1 sc, dec, 2 sc, dec (5)
12 rnd – around (5)
13 rnd – make a finger: 3 sc, 2 ch, sl st in the same sc, 2 sc (5)
14 rnd – around (5) Finish with sl st. Cut the thread and sew the hole in the detail.
The second arm should be knitted in the same way.
Arms are not to be stuffed. Stuff only the shoulders, and put into the neck any little
tube in order the head to be stable. Stuff the upper part of the body.
Body (continue working with beige yarn)
37 rnd – 9 sc, inc, 9 sc, inc (22)
38 rnd – 5 sc, inc, 10 sc, inc, 5 sc (24)
39-40 rnds – around (24)
41rnd – 11 sc, inc, 11 sc, inc (26)
42 rnd – 12 sc, inc, 12 sc, inc (28)
43-46 rnds – around (28)
47 rnd – 12 sc, dec, 12 sc, dec (26)
Stuff the body tightly.
Legs
48 rnd – right leg: 7 sc, leave 13 loops, 6 sc, and make a round (circle). Each leg has
13 loops. Left leg: join a brown thread to the beginning of the rnd and leave a long
tail. Knit sc and make a round (circle). Knit 1 rnd around. It is necessary for making
the legs the same length. (13)
49 rnd – 11 sc, dec (12)
50 rnd – around (12)
51 rnd – 9 sc, dec (11)
52 rnd – around (11)
53 rnd – 9 sc, dec (10)
54 rnd – around (10)
55 rnd – 8 sc, dec (9)
56 rnd – 7 sc, dec (8)
Stuff the leg.
57-60 rnds – knit the boots: 4 rnds around with the white yarn (put the thread into
twice in order the boots to be more thick) (8)
If you want you may have legs without the boots. Make them longer as you want
knitting the legs 2 or 3 rnd additionally. Then you may knit the heel.
61 rnd – turn round the detail: ch, 3 sc.
62 rnd – turn round the detail: ch, 3 sc, knit in 2 sc. from the sides, sl st, 4 sc, sl st, 2
sc from the sides.
63 rnd – knit around: 2 dec, sc, 1 stitch on the bend is left, sl st, 3 sc, 1 stitch is left, sl
st. (8)
64 rnd – right leg: 4 sc, dec, 2 sc. Left leg: 5 sc, dec, sc. (7)
65-66 rnds – 2 rnd around (7)
67 rnd – dec around, cut the thread.
Stuff the leg and sew up the hole of the detail.
Knit the second leg. Sew up the hole between the legs with the left thread.
Coat (the bottom part)
1 rnd – on the perimeter of the waist cast on 20 sc (blue yarn) in the stitches which
left in the 35 rnd. (20)
2 rnd – around (20)
3 rnd – (3 sc, inc) around (25)
4 rnd – around (25)
5 rnd – (4 sc, inc) around (30)
6 rnd – around (30)
7 rnd –(5 sc, inc) around (35)
8 rnd – around (35)
9 rnd –(6 sc, inc) around (40)
10 rnd – around (40)
11 rnd – (7 sc, inc) around (45)
12-14 rnds – 3 rnd around (45)
15-17 rnds – 3 rnd around (white cottony yarn) (45)
Cap
The cap is knitted with white cottony yarn as the head (1-7 rounds), crochet №4.5
8 - rnd – (6 sc, inc) around (48)
9-18 rnd – 10 rnd around (48)
19 rnd – 43 sc, turn round the detail (43)
20 rnd – ch, 38 sc, turn round the detail (38)
21 rnd – ch, 38 sc, turn round the detail (38)
22 rnd – ch, 38 sc, turn round the detail (38)
23 rnd – ch, 38 sc. Finish the knitting on this edge. Turn round the detail and begin to
knit on the neck of the cap. (38)
24 rnd – cast on from the sides 5 sc, 10 sc, cast on 5 sc in the second side. (20)
25 rnd – turn round the detail, ch, 4 sc, dec, 3 sc, dec, 3 sc, dec, 4 sc. Finish and cut
the thread. (17)
26 rnd – knit the strings: cast on 15 ch (white yarn), 17 sc, 15 ch (47)
27 rnd – turn round the detail, 18 sc, dec, 2 sc, dec, 18 sc. (44) Finish and cut the
tread.
Comb the cap.
Assembly
Make a face. Put in the eyes between the 15th and 16th rnds. Embroider the nose with
light brown yarn. Embroider the mouth with red yarn.
Cast on 16 ch (white yarn). Knit 15 sc. Cut the thread leaving the long thread for
sewing. Sew the strip on the head where a fringe will be placed. Cut 15 threads of 10
cm length and fasten these threads on the stitches.
Cut the fringe.
Put on the cap and sew by the edge. Tie the strings of the cap under the chin. Sew the
buttons on the coat. Embroider laces on the boots.
The doll is ready!
