Sweet Oddity Art;https://www.lovecrafts.com/en-gb/p/dragon-crochet-pattern-by-carolyne-brodie;"Abbreviations:
mr= magic ring- crochet single crochet stitches in to the
adjustable loop BLO= back loops only
ch= chain stitch F/O= Fasten off
sc= single crochet stitch hdc= half double crochet
sl= slip stitch FLO= front loops only bob= bobble st
dc= double crochet stitch inc3= 3 sc in the same stitch inc4= 4 sc in the same st
inc= increase- make two single crochet stitches in the same stitch
dec=decrease- crochet two stitches together using the decrease method
(4 sc, inc) x 6= repeat the pattern between parentheses 6 times
Notes:
• Do not join rounds unless stated, work in a continuous spiral
• Use a stitch marker to mark the beginning of each round
• All stitches are worked in both loops unless stated otherwise in the pattern
Sweet Oddity Art 2
Head:
Crocheted from front to back of head
With Color A:
Ch 5
1. inc in 2nd ch from hook, 2 sc, inc4, working on opposite side of chain: 2 sc, inc= 12
2. inc x 2, 3 sc, inc x 3, 3 sc, inc= 18
3. (sc, inc) x 2, 3 sc, (sc, inc) x 3, 4 sc, inc= 24
4. (2 sc, inc) x 2, 3 sc, (2 sc, inc) x 3, 5 sc, inc= 30
5. sc in each st around
6. 7 sc, bob, 4 sc, bob, 17 sc
7-8. sc in each st around
9. (3 sc, dec) x 6= 24
10. (3 sc, inc) x 6= 30
11. (4 sc, inc) x 6= 36
12. (5 sc, inc) x 6= 42
13. (6 sc, inc) x 6= 48
Place eyes between rounds 12 and 13, leaving 10 holes between them. If you want the sunken
eye look, do not place the backs of the eyes on until round 21.
TIP! You may have to adjust the eye placement depending on yarn and hook size you use.
14-18. sc in each st around
19. (6 sc, dec) x 6= 42
20. (5 sc, dec) x 6= 36
21. (4 sc, dec) x 6= 30
Now for the eyes. Stuff the head well. Cut a long piece of yarn and remove the eyes. Place the
needle in the hole where the first eye was and thread the needle into a hole next to the eye
hole. Go back and forth between each eye hole repeating the process from the first eye. Pull
slightly on the yarn after going through each hole. Do this about 3 times on each side until you
reach the look you want. Follow the pictures for help. There is also a youtube video I have for
extra help on this process.
https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9XoBnTY6k70&t=55s
To place the backs of the eyes you will need to remove most of the stuffing to place the
washers on the eyes then re stuff it
22. (3 sc, dec) x 6= 24
23. (2 sc, dec) x 6= 18
24. (sc, dec) x 6= 12
25. dec x 6= 6
F/O and sew the hole closed
Sweet Oddity Art 3
Legs and Body: Tail:
Legs(Make 2): With Color A:
Starting with Color B: 1. Make 6 sc into a magic ring= 6
1. Make 6 sc into a magic ring= 6 2. 2 sc, inc x 2, 2 sc= 8
2. Increase in each st around= 12 3. Sc in each st around
3. (sc, inc) x 6= 18 4. 3 sc, inc x 2, 3 sc= 10
Change to Color A: 5. Sc in each st around
4. BLO sc in each st around 6. 4 sc, inc x 2, 4 sc= 12
5. 6 sc, (bob, sc,) x 3, 6 sc 7. Sc in each st around
6. (sc, dec) x 6= 12 8. 5 sc, inc x 2, 5 sc= 14
7. (sc, inc) x 6= 18 9. Sc in each st around
Do not F/O the 2nd leg! Work 7 extra st on rnd 10. 6 sc, inc x 2, 6 sc= 16
7 of the 2nd leg to move the stitch marker. 11. Sc in each st around
marker. Connect legs: 12. 7 sc, inc x 2, 7 sc= 18
1. inc x 3, 28 sc, inc x 3= 40 13. Sc in each st around
2. (inc, 6 sc) x 6= 48 14. 8 sc, inc x 2, 8 sc= 20
Start stuffing the legs 15. Sc in each st around
3-9. sc in each st around 16. 9 sc, inc x 2, 9 sc= 22
10. (dec, sc) x 4, 30 sc, (dec, sc) x 2= 42 17. Sc in each st around
11. dec x 4, 30 sc, dec x 2= 36 18. 10 sc, inc x 2, 10 sc= 24
12-13. sc in each st around F/O and leave a long tail for sewing
14. (dec, 10 sc) x 3= 33
15. sc in each st around
16. (dec, 9 sc) x 3= 30
17. sc in each st around
Stuff the body as you work
18. (dec, 8 sc) x 3= 27
19. sc in each st around
20. (dec, 7 sc) x 3= 24
21. sc in each st around
22. (dec, 6 sc) x 3= 21
23. sc in each st around
24. (dec, 5 sc) x 3= 18
25-27. sc in each st around
F/O and leave a long tail for sewing
Sweet Oddity Art 4
Arms(Make 2): Horns(Make 2):
With Color A: Starting with Color B:
1. Make 6 sc into a magic ring= 6 1. Make 3 sc into a magic ring= 3
2. Increase in each st around= 12 2. Sc, inc, sc= 4
3. sc in each st around 3. 2 sc, inc, sc= 5
4. 2 sc, (bob, sc) x 3, 4 sc 4. 3 sc, inc, sc= 6
5. (sc, dec) x 4= 8 5. 4 sc, inc, sc= 7
Do not stuff the arms anymore 6. 5 sc, inc, sc= 8
6-11. sc in each st around 7. 6 sc, inc, sc= 9
Work 3 sc, fold the arms in half and sc 8. 7 sc, inc, sc= 10
the opening closed. F/O and leave a 9. 8 sc, inc, sc= 11
long tail for sewing 10. 9 sc, inc, sc= 12
Change to Color A:
11. BLO sc in each st around
12. sc in each st around
F/O and leave a long tail for sewing
Ears(Make 2 in Color A, 2 in Color B):
Starting with Color B:
1. Make 6 sc into a magic ring= 6
2. Increase in each st around= 12
3. (sc, inc) x 6= 18
Do not F/O Color A ears!
Place the back sides of Color A and Color B ears together. sc the ears together with Color A
yarn.
4. 6 sc, (ch 4, sl st in 4th ch from hook, 2 sc) x 3, sc in remaining stitches
F/O and leave a long tail for sewing
Wings(Make 2):
With Color B:
Ch 8
1. sc into 2nd chain from hook, 5 sc, sl st in last ch, ch 1= 7
2. Turn, 2 sc, inc, 4 sc, ch 4= 12
3. turn, sc in 2nd chain from hook, sc in next 2 chains, 4 sc, inc, 2 sc, sl st in last st, ch 1= 12
4. turn, 2 sc, inc, 9 sc, ch 4= 17
5. turn, sc in 2nd chain from hook, sc in next 2 chains, 9 sc, inc, 2 sc, sl st in last st, ch 1= 17
6. turn, 2 sc, inc, 14 sc= 22
7. Ch 1, turn, 9 sc, work 6 sc in the same st, 8 sc
F/O and leave a long tail for sewing
Sweet Oddity Art 5
Assembly
Head and Body:
1. Pin the head and body together.
2. Sew the head onto the body. You may need to add more stuffing as you sew.
Horns:
1. Pin the horns onto the top of the head.
2. Sew the horns onto the head.
Sweet Oddity Art 6
Ears:
1. Pinch the ears together at the bottom of the ear. Sew together about 3 stitches to
create a closed look.
2. Pin the ears next to the horns.
3. Sew the ears onto the head.
Sweet Oddity Art 7
Arms:
1. Pin the arms onto the side of the body approximately between rounds 22 and 23.
2. Sew the arms onto the body.
Tail:
1. Pin the tail onto the back of the body.
2. Sew the tail onto the body.
Sweet Oddity Art 8
Wings:
1. Pin the wings onto the back of the body.
2. Sew the wings onto the body.
You have your finished dragon! Thank you for your purchase! If you have any questions or
concerns please email me at sweetoddityart@gmail.com or etsy convo me. I will get back to
you asap. Please share your finished dragon with me as often as you want! I love seeing them!
Sweet Oddity Art 9
Helpful Tips:
Exact Colors Used:
1. Variegated: Tangled Pixie Rainbow
2. Black: I love this yarn black
The rainbow variegated can be purchased @tangled_pixie on Instagram
The eyes can be purchased at darkside crochet on instagram
You can use different eye sizes. You might have to adjust the placements if you change the
sizes.
You can use different hook sizes and weights of yarn. It will just change the size of your dragon
and you might need to adjust eye and nose placement.
How you stuff matters! The type of stuffing you use, how you stuff, all this matters on how your
dragon turns out. I prefer Polyfil stuffing but you can use other types.
Sweet Oddity Art 10
Additional Information
How to work on the opposite side of the chain:
This is an example picture!
1. Work the indicated amount of stitches across the first side of your chain
2. Turn the chain around and work the indicated amount on the opposite side of the chain
2. Turn the chain around and work the indicated amount on the opposite side of the chain
Sweet Oddity Art 11
3. Here is your finished round when you are working on the opposite side of the chain.
