in same st) st together)
Special False (faux) stitch: Cut yarn and pull through the last st. Thread the end through your needle and
stitches: insert the needle under both loops of the first st, and back again though the back loop of the last st to
create a faux st while bringing the yarn back to the back of your work.
Notes * Instructions are in standard terms, not UK.
* The stitch markers are not mentioned in the pattern, they are included for you to use if required. I
used scrap yarn to mark the beginning of rounds.
Credits: The shaping for Dunsparce’s head is based on Aphid777’s Baby Eevee pattern.
