Height: 8 cm
Easy level
4 hours approximately
Necessary Skills:
• Working in rounds (in a spiral)
• Counting/marking stitches and
rounds
• Using a stitch marker and running
stitch marker
• Basic sewing
• Invisible decrease
• Changing colours
3
Tips
All amigurumis are made with tight stitches, to avoid small holes when the
thread stretches when filling, use a smaller crochet hook.
All parts are worked in a spiral, without slip stitches or beginning chains.
Once we work in a spiral, you may miss the beginning of the round; to avoid
that, use a stitch marker.You can use a stitch marker or a piece of thread of a
contrasting color. Mark the first stitch of each row.
Fill the parts as you go. It is very difficult to fill the pieces evenly when they
are almost finished.
Always change the color of the thread in the last step of the last stitch of the
previous color.
If it is easier for you, you can glue the accessories instead of sewing.
Invisible decrease: Insert hook into the front loop of the next 2 stitches. Yarn
over and pull through both front loops. Yarn over and pull through both
loops.
sc3tog is a decrease with 3 sc passing the hook in three stitches
simultaneously and joining them. When joining the arms you will pick 3sc
from the arm and body at the same time.
All parts have been worked with single crochet X
Have FUN!
