© Copyright Hooked, stitched and glued 2022
Egg
Eggs are worked top down and in a spiral-do not join rounds, just use a stitch marker
to mark the first stitch of each round.
Make a magic ring.
Round 1 ch1, 4dc into magic ring. (4dc)
Round 2 2dc in each st. (8dc)
Round 3 (1dc, 2dc in next st) 4 times. (12dc)
Round 4 1dc, 2dc in next st (2dc, 2dc in next st) 3 times, 1dc. (16dc)
Round 5 (3dc, 2dc in next st) 4 times. (20dc)
Round 6 2dc, 2dc in next st (4dc, 2dc in next st) 3 times, 2dc. (24dc)
Round 7 (5dc, 2dc in next st) 4 times. (28dc)
Round 8 1dc in each st to end.
Round 9 3dc, 2dc in next st (6dc, 2dc in next st) 3 times, 3dc. (32dc)
Round 10 1dc in each st around.
Round 11 (7dc, 2dc in next st) 4 times. (36dc)
Rounds 12-16 1dc in each st around.
Round 17 (4dc, dc2tog) 6 times. (30dc)
Round 18 1dc in each st around.
Round 19 (3dc, dc2tog) 6 times. (24dc)
Round 20 1dc, dc2tog, (2dc, dc2tog) 5 times, 1dc. (18dc)
Stuff the egg at this point
Round 21 (1dc, dc2tog) 6 times. (12dc)
Round 22 dc2tog 6 times. (6dc)
Fasten off and gather up the stitches to close the hole.
Finishing
Close the hole using the yarn tail, and darn in the end. Use embroidery silks or yarn
scraps to embroider flowers or anything that takes your fancy!
Add a hanging loop through the top if you like.
Ta da-one eggcellent egg!
