Assembly
Connecting the Ears
-The ears are connected between rounds 15 and 17. Position the ears with a 6 stitch gap
between the ears at the top of head.
Connecting the Front Legs
-The front of the Front Legs are connected between the 4th and 5th round from the crease of
the neck, with a 3 stitch gap between the legs, centered with the head. The back of the Front
Legs are connected between the 8th and 9th round from the crease of the neck.
Connecting the Rear Legs
-The back of the Rear Legs are connected between the 4th and 5th round from the rear end,
with a 4 stitch gap between them. The front of the Rear Legs are connected between the 7th
and 8th round from the rear end.
Connecting the Tail
-The tail will be connected centered 1 round above the center of the rear. Using one strand for
the left and the other strand for the right, weave them both into the body 1 stitch off center so
that both strands come out through the center.
-Now using both strands, one at a time, send them back through the center top of the tail and
into the body (through the off centered holes we first went through) so that both strands come
out through the center again.
-Tie the strands together and hide them in the body.
-Using a pet grooming brush or fine toothed comb, fray out the 1 inch ends of the tail for hair.
Congratulations!
