Crown (Make 1)
Using gold yarn. Ch 20 and slst to join.
rnd 1 -3 20 Sc (20) (3 rounds)
The points of the crown will be created in the next round.
slst into the first stitch of round 3, 3-ch picot, slst into the next stitch of
round 3.
Repeat 9 more times into the remaining stitches of round 3 to create ten
points. Cut the yarn and fasten off invisibly.
Copyright © 2022 erinmaycrochet. All Rights Reserved.
Page 11
Assembly
Position the body so that the flat portion of the head is at the top and the
bulge of the belly is on the bottom before sewing.
Place the eyes on the top of the front of the body between rounds 13-18
with about 7-8 stitches in between. Sew in place using the long yarn tails.
Copyright © 2022 erinmaycrochet. All Rights Reserved.
Page 12
Place the arms on the sides of the body and sew in place using the long yarn
tails. The arms should be placed 2-3 rounds behind the eyes.
Place the legs on the end of the body and sew in place using the long yarn
tails.
Tip #1 – I chose to sew the legs to the body with a few stitches in between,
which will cause the legs to face outward in a ‘V’ shape. Sew the legs closer
together with no spaces if you would prefer the legs to be straighter.
Copyright © 2022 erinmaycrochet. All Rights Reserved.
Page 13
Sew the spots to the back of the body using the long yarn tails.
If you would like the crown to be attached to the body, place the crown on
the top of the head between the eyes and sew in place using gold yarn.
Copyright © 2022 erinmaycrochet. All Rights Reserved.
Page 14
Congratulations! Your Fernando the Frog Prince is complete!
