Sweet Oddity Art;https://www.lovecrafts.com/en-gb/p/fish-crochet-pattern-by-carolyne-brodie;"Abbreviations:
mr= magic ring- crochet single crochet stitches in to the
adjustable loop BLO= back loops only
ch= chain stitch inc3= 3 sc in the same stitch
sc= single crochet stitch F/O= fasten off
sl= slip stitch
dc= double crochet stitch
inc= increase- make two single crochet stitches in the same stitch
dec=decrease- crochet two stitches together using the decrease method
(4 sc, inc) x 6= repeat the pattern between parentheses 6 times
Notes:
• Do not join rounds unless stated, work in a continuous spiral
• Use a stitch marker to mark the beginning of each round
• All stitches are worked in both loops unless stated otherwise in the pattern
Sweet Oddity Art 2
Head and Body:
Lips(Make 2):
With Color C:
1. Make 6 sc into a magic ring= 6
2. Increase in each st around= 12
Do not F/O 2nd piece.
Place both pieces together to look like a figure 8.
Make 3 sc on both pieces to connect them together.
Start crocheting 9 sc on the 1st lip. Make 9 more sc around the 2nd lip = 18
3. (sc, dec) x 6= 12
Sweet Oddity Art 3
Sweet Oddity Art 4
Continuing with the body:
Change to Color A:
1. sc in each st around
2. (sc, inc) x 6= 18
3. sc in each st around
4. (2 sc, inc) x 6= 24
5. sc in each st around
6. (3 sc, inc) x 6= 30
7. sc in each st around with an additional 2 sc (you are not increasing. You are moving the stitch
marker. Work 2 extra sc and in the very next stitch start the next round)
8. (2 sc, inc) x 6, 12 sc= 36
9. (3 sc, inc) x 6, 12 sc= 42
10. (4 sc, inc) x 6, 12 sc= 48
11. (5 sc, inc) x 6, 12 sc= 54
12. (6 sc, inc) x 6, 12 sc= 60
(place a stitch marker in between stitch 4 and 5 of round 15. Place a 2nd stitch marker 32
stitches away from the 1st stitch marker. This is to mark where your eyes should go. This is an
approximate point. You may need to adjust once you start the decreasing rounds.)
13-19. sc in each st around
Change to Color B:
21-27. sc in each st around
Stuff the fish as you work. Place eyes between rounds 15 and 16, leaving 32 holes in between
them. You might have to adjust placement after row 30. Make sure you look at the eyes and
see how they look. If you want the sunken eye look, do not place the backs until round 33.
28. 18 sc, (dec, 8 sc) x 3, dec, 10 sc= 56
29. 17 sc, (dec, 7 sc) x 3, dec, 10 sc= 52
30. 16 sc, (dec, 6 sc) x 3, dec, 10 sc= 48
31. 15 sc, (dec, 5 sc) x 3, dec, 10 sc= 44
32. 14 sc, (dec, 4 sc) x 3, dec, 10 sc= 40
33. 13 sc, (dec, 3 sc) x 3, dec, 10 sc= 36
Sweet Oddity Art 5
Body Continued:
Now for the eyes. Stuff the head well. Place the eyelashes inside the eye along the edge. Cut a
long piece of yarn and remove the eyes. Place the needle in the hole where the first eye was
and thread the needle into a hole next to the eye hole. Go back and forth between each eye
hole repeating the process from the first eye. Pull slightly on the yarn after going through each
hole. Do this about 3 times on each side until you
reach the look you want. Follow the pictures for help. There is also a youtube video I have for
extra help on this process.
https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9XoBnTY6k70&t=55s
To place the backs of the eyes you will need to remove most of the stuffing to place the
washers on the eyes then re stuff it.
34. (4 sc, dec) x 6= 30
35. (3 sc, dec) x 6= 24
36-37. sc in each st around
38. (2 sc, dec) x 6= 18
39-44. sc in each st around
Change to Color A: Fold the tail in half. Sc the tail together to close the tail. = 9
Ch 1, turn, inc across= 18
Ch 1, turn, sc across= 18
Ch 1, turn, inc across= 36
Ch 1, turn, sc across= 36
Ch 1, turn, inc across= 72
Ch 1, turn, sc across= 72
F/O and weave in the ends
