Assembly Frankie Kitty
Mark the center of the body with some pins to ensure things are even and
placed symmetrically. Use neat stitches and hidden stitches where possible to
sew together the various parts.
Pin the ears, the nose (after stuffing it lightly), the paws and the bow tie to get a
preview of the kitty. The ears are placed between rounds 3 and 4 from the top
center of the head. Check that both ears are at the same distance from the eyes
and sew in place. To find the right position for the paws, put the toy on the
table, pin two paws to bottom of the body in the center so that the kitty is
balanced and stays upright. The nails are positioned vertical with respect to the
body. Pin the other two paws in the middle of the body with the nails sideways. When you are happy
with their, positions sew in place. Now sew on the nose just slightly below the eyes, the bow tie just
below the nose and the tail onto the bottom back of the body in the center.
Congratulations, you have completed Frankie Kitty the Ami!
2020 ©MarysAmiland
