5. EYEBROWS
Material: YarnArt Begonia in brown.
How to make:
-Thread the yarn (about 100cm in length) into a tapestry needle. Insert the needle from the top of
the head (leaving a 7-8cm tail) to a place where the eyebrow will start, point 1. Then insert the
needle to point 2 and push it back to point 1 (same place where the yarn comes up). You will have a
line - base for the eyebrows, pic.27-29.
Pic.27 Pic.28 Pic.29
Next, wrap the line with the yarn 3 times, then insert the needle to point 2 and push it through to
the top of the head. Repeat the same with the other eyebrow and return the needle to the top of the
head and secure the ends, pic.30-33. Don't cut the yarn end as you still have enough tail to make a
mouth.
Pic.30 Pic.31 Pic.32 Pic.33
To make the mouth:
Push the needle with brown yarn from top of the head down to the bottom of yellow face between
Rounds 6 and 7, pic.34. Take 2.0mm hook and make 1ss in each of next 8-9sts between these
rounds. Then pull the yarn out, insert it into a needle and make a small vertical line at the end.
Push the needle with the yarn to the top of the head, secure it and cut the yarn ends, pic.33, 35-39.
Pic.34 Pic.35 Pic.36
Pic.37 Pic.38 Pic.39
6. NOSE
Material: YarnArt Begonia in pink, hook size: 1.5mm;
How to make (see the chart below): 3ch, 3htr in 3rd ch from hook, 2ch, ss in same base ch. Fasten
off leaving a long tail for attaching purposes, pic.40.
Take a piece of white thread and insert the needle from back to the front of the nose, make a knot
and hide the yarn end, pic.41-43.
Pic.40 Pic.41 Pic.42 Pic.43
7. WHISKERS
Material: YarnArt Begonia in black, hook size 1.5mm;
How to make:
- take the black yarn and insert it through 4 stitches between Rounds 4 and 5 of the centre of the
face. Insert the hook to the place where the yarn end is coming up and make 14ch. Fasten off
leaving a tail about 6mm, pic.44-49. Follow the same instruction to make the whisker from the
other side.
