TO MAKE UP
On the apple insert two ⅜in/10mm toy safety eyes and
remove the stitch markers. Sew the side edges tog, stuffing
as you sew, and gather the cast on sts tog at the bottom.
Using a length of yarn D, sew up through the center core of
the apple from the gathered cast on sts at the bottom up
through the gathered bound (cast) off sts at the top, and
back down again and out at the bottom, pulling the yarn tight
to make indents at the top and bottom. Firmly double knot
the tails to secure the yarn and hide the tails inside the apple.
Sew on each cheek using a running back stitch around the
outer edge in yarn L.
Sew the side edges of the stalk tog and add a little filling
inside the top (bound (cast) off end). Sew the cast on edge
onto the top (bound (cast) off end) of the apple.
Sew the side edges of the leaf tog; this seam runs down the
back. Sew the cast on edge onto the base of the stalk.
