without eyes.
To assemble the bunch of grapes, make layers of grapes to
stack on top of each other. First take 3 grapes and with yarn
K sew through the center of each grape so that they form
a triangle shape, making sure that the cast on end of each
grape is at the top and the seamed side edge faces the
inside of the triangle. Repeat this process with another
4 grapes to form a square shape, and include the grape with
eyes in this square ensuring that the eyes face outwards.
Then take the grape attached to the stalk, and feed the end
of the stalk up through the hole in the middle of the triangle
layer, and then through the hole in the middle of the square
layer (you should have one grape leftover). Arrange the bunch
by moving the layers, and when you are happy with the
layout use yarn K to sew the grapes tog in a few places to
keep them in position. Finally sew the last grape on top of the
square layer and also onto the stalk.
Place the two vine leaves tog, wrong side facing each other,
and sew tog around the side edges. Sew the cast on edge
onto the stalk on top of the bunch of grapes.
