Goldfish Toy Amigurumi;https://www.lovecrafts.com/en-gb/p/goldfish-toy-amigurumi-crochet-pattern-by-heidi;;"Goldfish Toy Amigurumi
Crochet Pattern
By Wondertime Tots
Difficulty: Advanced Beginner
©2014 Heidi DeAlessio
February 26, 2014
Goldfish Toy Amigurumi Crochet Pattern
Wondertime Tots
Finished size about 8.5 inches
Materials List:
 H hook
 4 ounces Red Hear Super Saver in pumpkin
 Yarn needle for attaching
 Polyester fiberfill
 Stitch marker
Notes:
This pattern is worked in the round. Do not join at the end of each row; just keep working
moving your stitch marker at the end of each round. This will keep your work seamless. Keep
your stitches close together so that no filling shows through. You will do yourself a huge favor
by counting your stitches after each round. After each decrease, pull the stitch tight so it’s closer
together. Don’t overstuff, just enough so he’s plump and squishy. Squeeze around to shape a
little, flattening the bottom a little. Have fun. Each goldfish will have its own personality because
it is handmade. Don’t stress out if it’s not “perfect” or doesn’t look exactly like the picture.
Yours is an original  Enjoy! Heidi
PATTERN NOTES: All pieces will start with a sloppy slip knot since they are worked in the round. This will prevent a hole in your
work. Also, do not join rounds at the end. Continue with the next round, moving your stitch marker to mark the start of your
round. To make a sloppy slip knot: wrap the yarn around the hook, holding the bottom of the yarn at the hook and then
crochet as directed. Once the first round is completed, pull the tail tight as you hold the loop you just finished. Your loop will be
tighter and there won’t be any hole in the center.
©2014Wondertime Tots *This pattern is copyright protected. Find me on Ravelry.com and
Craftsy.com 2
Goldfish Toy Amigurumi Crochet Pattern
Wondertime Tots
 PATTERN NOTES: The body is made as one piece then the fins are attached after. There are
two smaller side fins and one larger top fin. The fins are basically circles that are folded in
half and sc together. You can add safety eyes if you wish, embroider eyes on with yarn. Yarn
eyes are safer for babies and toddlers. You may also cut out eyes from felt and glue on with
a fabric adhesive. Of course, you may even leave the fish without eyes. So you have many
options and each will create a different look.
 Add this fish to a baby blanket for a special and unique baby gift.
Starting at the head:
R1- Start with a slip knot, then chain 2 stitches, then single crochet (sc) 6 times in the 2nd chain from
the hook. This is your first round (6 sc)
R2- Sc two times in each sc. (12 sc)
R3- Sc 2 times in the first stitch then sc once in the next stitch: repeat this pattern until you reach
the end of the round. This is the first increase. You should have 18 single crochet stitches in the
round. (18sc)
R4: Sc 2 times in the first st then sc once in the next 2 st: repeat pattern to the end of the round (24
sc)
R5: Sc 2 times in the first sc then once in the next 3 stitches: repeat pattern to the end, increasing to
30 sc
R6: Sc 2 times in the first sc then once in the next 4 stitches: repeat pattern to the end, increasing to
36 sc
Rounds 7 to 17: Single crochet once in each stitch around (36 sc)
ADD EYES, STUFF TO TOP
R18: Sc2tog, sc next 4: repeat pattern until you have decreased your stitches to 30 sc
R19: Sc once in each st around (30 sc)
R20: Sc2tog, sc next 3: repeat pattern until you have decreased to 24 sc
R21: Sc2tog, sc next 2: repeat until you have 18 sc- STUFF AS YOU GO
Rounds 22 to 26: Sc once in each st around (18 sc)
R27: Sc 2 times in the first st, sc once in the next 2 st: repeat 5 more times, inc. to 24 sc
R28: Sc 2 times in the first sc, sc once in the next 3 st: repeat 5 more times, inc. to 30 sc
R29: Sc 2 times in the first sc, sc once in the next 4 st: repeat 5 more times, inc. to 36 sc
Rounds 30 to 33: Sc once in each stitch around (36 sc) FINISH STUFFING then close tail together by
shutting the tail and single crocheting across the top
Fasten off and weave in tail.
©2014Wondertime Tots *This pattern is copyright protected. Find me on Ravelry.com and
Craftsy.com 3
Goldfish Toy Amigurumi Crochet Pattern
Wondertime Tots
Side Fins – Make 2- H hook, pumpkin yarn
R1- Start with a slip knot, and then chain 2 stitches, then single crochet (sc) 6 times in the
2nd chain from the hook. This is your first round (6 sc)
R2- Sc two times in each sc. (12 sc)
R3- Sc 2 times in the first stitch then sc once in the next stitch: repeat this pattern until you
reach the end of the round. This is the first increase. You should have 18 single crochet
stitches in the round. (18sc)
R4: Sc 2 times in the first st then sc once in the next 2 st: repeat pattern to the end of the
round (24 sc)
R5: Sc 2 times in the first sc then once in the next 3 stitches: repeat pattern to the end,
increasing to 30 sc
Rounds 6 and 7: Sc once in each stitch around (30 sc)
 Then fold the circle in half. Chain 1 and sc across both stitches to make one half-
circle. Finish off with an 8 inch tail.
Fold half-circle in half again to get the
half-way point. You will be sewing through this half-way point to attach to the fish.
Thread the tail through the needle and sew onto the side of the fish. Secure by sewing twice
over the stitches and fasten off, weaving in the tail. Then sew one stitch over on each side
and fasten off the bottom and weave in the tail.
©2014Wondertime Tots *This pattern is copyright protected. Find me on Ravelry.com and
Craftsy.com 4
Goldfish Toy Amigurumi Crochet Pattern
Wondertime Tots
Attach the other fin on the other side.
Top Fin- Make 1
R1- Start with a slip knot, and then chain 2 stitches, then single crochet (sc) 6 times in the
2nd chain from the hook. This is your first round (6 sc)
R2- Sc two times in each sc. (12 sc)
R3- Sc 2 times in the first stitch then sc once in the next stitch: repeat this pattern until you
reach the end of the round. This is the first increase. You should have 18 single crochet
stitches in the round. (18sc)
R4: Sc 2 times in the first st then sc once in the next 2 st: repeat pattern to the end of the
round (24 sc)
R5: Sc 2 times in the first sc then once in the next 3 stitches: repeat pattern to the end,
increasing to 30 sc
R6: Sc 2 times in the first sc then once in the next 4 stitches: repeat pattern to the end,
increasing to 36 sc
Rounds 7 and 8: Sc once in each stitch around (36 sc)
 Fold the circle in half. Sc across both stitches to make one half-circle. Finish off with
an 8 inch tail.
 Attach to the top of the fish by lining the fin down the middle then whip stitching to
the top.
To keep the fins folded, you can block the pieces first before attaching. Another way is to
keep folding them repeatedly.
