Assembly
Head and Body:
1. Cut the shape of his mouth out with black felt. It might take a couple tries. Mine did
to get it the way I wanted it. I did not include a template because oogie’s mouth comes
in so many different shapes.
2. You can sew, hot glue or use fabric glue to put the mouth on his face. Make sure the
mouth is where you want it before you glue it or sew it on.
3. Take a long strand of black embroidery thread. Thread your needle. Insert the needle
into a hole on the side of the head. Bring the needle up to a place on his mouth and
start sewing stitches around the edges of the mouth.
