1. Cut a long strand of green yarn. Thread a needle with the yarn. Insert the needle into
a hole in between the eyes. Bring the needle to an inner corner of the eye. Insert the
needle into a hole on the top corner of the eye. Do this approximately 3 times. Repeat
for the other eye.
2. I used a mini spider party favor for oogie’s spider on his head. I took an embroidery
strand and wrapped it around the spider making a knot. Then took the other end of the
strand and threaded the needle. I inserted the needle into the tip of the head and
wrapped it around the head several times. Weave in the ends.
