The Elemental Guardians Collection;https://www.lovecrafts.com/en-gb/p/happy-fox-free-pdf-amigurumi-animal-english-pattern-crochet-pattern-by-harmonidycrochet;"Abbreviations and Skills
Difficulty:​ Intermediate
● R​: Row
● MR​: Magic ring
● RND:​ Round
● CH​: Chain
● ST(S): ​Stitch(es)
● FO​: Fasten off
● SS​: Slip Stitch
● SC​: Single Crochet
● HDC:​ Half double crochet
● DC:​ Double Crochet
● BO:​ Bobble Stitch
● BLO​: Back loop only
● INC​: single crochet increase
● DEC:​ single crochet decrease. (sc2tog in
the front loops of the stitch)
Legs: Make two
Begin with blue.
Leg 1
Rnd 1: ​8sc in the MR (8)
Rnd 2-5: ​8sc, ​Color Change to White in the last
st. ​(8) (4rounds)
Rnd 6-9:​ 8sc (8) (4rounds)
Fasten off. Leave a long tail for sewing.
Count 4 stitches from where you've fastened off.
Put a stitch marker on the 4th stitch.
Start stuffing as you go.​
Leg 2
Begin with Blue.
Rnd 1-9: ​repeat rnd 1-9 (8) (9rounds)
Rnd 10:​ 8sc, ch4, connect the ch4 to the stitch
marker of L​ eg1​ with a sc. 7sc on L​ eg1​. 4sc on
ch4.​ ​END OF ROUND​. (​ 8sc on each leg,
4chains, 4sc on ch4) (24)
Rnd 11:​ 24sc (24)
Rnd 12:​ *4sc, dec * repeat * to* 4 times. (20)
Rnd 13-15:​ 20sc (20) (3 rounds)
Rnd 16:​ *3sc,dec* repeat *to* 4 times (16)
Rnd 17: ​*2sc, dec* repeat *to* 4 times (12)
Rnd 18-20: 1​ 2sc (12) (3rounds)
Continue working your way in crocheting the
head.
HEAD
Begin with White. Stuff as you go.
Rnd 21:​ 12inc (24)
Rnd 22:​ *1sc, inc* repeat *to* 12 times. (36)
Rnd 23:​ *2sc, inc* repeat *to* 12 times.(48)
Rnd 24: ​*3sc, inc* repeat *to* 12 times.(50)
Rnd 25:​ 50sc (50)
Rnd 26:​ *3sc, dec* repeat *to* 12 times.(48)
Rnd 27-33: ​48sc (48) (8rounds)
Rnd 34:​ *4sc, dec* repeat *to* 12 times. (36)
Rnd 35:​ *3sc, dec* repeat *to* 12 times. (24)
Rnd 36:​ *2sc, dec* repeat *to* 12 times. (18)
Rnd 37: ​*7sc, dec* repeat *to* 2 times. (16)
Rnd 38:​ *6sc, dec* repeat *to* 2 times. (14)
Rnd 39:​ *5sc, dec* repeat *to* 2 times. (12)
Rnd 40: ​*1sc, dec* repeat *to* 3 times. (9)
Stuff the head firmly. It takes half an hour to
really stuff it firmly.
Fasten off. Weave on ends.
SNOUT
Begin with black.
Rnd 1: ​6sc in the MR, ​Color change to white in
the last st.​(6)
Rnd 2: ​*1sc, inc* repeat 3 times (9)
Rnd 3: ​*2sc, inc* repeat 3 times (12)
Rnd 4: *​ 3sc, inc* repeat 3 times (15)
Rnd 5: ​15sc (15) (3rounds)
Fasten off. Leave a long tail for sewing.
EARS:​ ​Make two
Begin with blue.
Rnd 1​: 6sc on MR (6)
Rnd 2​: 6sc (6)
Rnd 3​: *1sc, inc* repeat 3 times (9)
Rnd 4​: *2sc, inc* repeat 3 times (12)
Rnd 5​: *3sc, inc* repeat 3 times, c​ olor change to white in the last stitch.​ (15)
Rnd 6-7​: 15sc (15) (2rounds)
Rnd 8​: *3sc, dec* repeat 3 times (12)
Rnd 9:​ *2sc, dec* repeat 3 times (9)
Fasten off. Leave a long tail for sewing.
ARMS: Make two
Begin with blue.
Rnd 1​: 6sc on MR (6)
Rnd 2​: 6inc (12)
Rnd 3​: *1sc, inc* repeat 6 times (18)
Rnd 4​: 17sc, 1bo (18)
Rnd 5​: 18sc (18)
Rnd 6:​ *1sc, dec* repeat 6 times (12)
Rnd 7​: 12sc (12)
Rnd 8​: 12sc, C​ olor change to white in the last
stitch. (​ 12)
Rnd 9:​* 1sc, dec* repeat 4 times. (8)
Rnd 10-13:​ 8sc (8) (4rounds)
Stuff only the hands. Do not stuff the upper
part of the arms.
Fasten off. Leave a long tail for sewing.
SCARF
The chain2 counts as 1 stitch.
R1:​ Ch10, Dc on the 3rd ch from the hook. 7dc
(9)
R2-17​:Ch2, B​ LO 8dc​. (9) (16rounds)
Fasten off. Leave a long tail for sewing.
TAIL
Begin with blue.
Rnd 1​: 6sc on MR (6)
Rnd 2​: 6sc (6)
Rnd 3​: *1sc, inc* repeat 3 times (9)
Rnd 4​: *2sc, inc* repeat 3 times (12)
Rnd 5​: *3sc, inc* repeat 3 times (15)
Rnd 6:​ *4sc, inc* repeat 3 times (18)
Rnd 7-8: 1​ 8sc,C​ hange color to white in the last stitch.
(18) (2 rounds)
Rnd 9: ​18sc (18)
Rnd 10:​ *4sc, dec* repeat 3 times. (15)
Rnd 11:​ *3sc, dec* repeat 3 times. (12)
Rnd 12-16: 1​ 2sc (12) (5 rounds)
Fasten off. Leave a long tail for sewing.
ASSEMBLY
Use pins to place all the parts together before sewing. That way you can still modify
it in a way that suits your needs and taste.
● Arms- F​ latten the arms and place it on the toy’s shoulder. Make sure that the
Arms are aligned/ parallel with the toy’s Legs. The Legs will serve as your guide
on where to place the ears as well. The thumbs should be pointing towards
you.
● Scarf- S​ ew the both ends of the scarf, then
fold it lengthwise. Place it on the neck of
the doll.
● Snout- ​Stuff it with stuffing. Locate the
center of the toy’s face. Place the last stitch
of the snout on the 12th round of the head
counting from the top. Do not sew
completely yet because you will still insert
little stuffing before you will finally close it.
● Ears & Tail- ​Count 6 rounds from the top of the head. Place the Ears on the
6th round (for both left and right). Make sure that the ears are aligned to the
arms and legs. Attach the tail flatly on the butt.
● Eyes- ​See picture below. The gap of the eyes to the nose is one sc. The gap
between two eyes is 6sc.";;Lovecrafts
@ALMAPHLOX - PHLOXY CROCHET;https://www.lovecrafts.com/en-gb/p/happy-sun-crochet-pattern-by-phloxy-crochet;"ABBREVIATIONS & STITCHES YOU NEED TO KNOW
ch = chain
ss = slip stitch
sc = (US) single crochet / (UK) double crochet
inc = increase | dec = decrease
hdc = (US) half double crochet / (UK) half treble crochet
dc = (US) double crochet / (UK) treble crochet
NOTES
No sewing required!
Work in rounds.
I used Paintbox Yarns Simply DK to create this happy sun as shown in the pictures.
1
xolhpamla@
@ALMAPHLOX - PHLOXY CROCHET HAPPY SUN AMIGURUMI PATTERN
1. Start with a magic ring of 6 stitches. (6)
1
2. inc in all stitches. (12)
CORE 3. 1 sc, 1 inc - repeat 6 times. (18)
4. 2 sc, 1 inc - repeat 6 times. (24)
YELLOW YARN
5. 3 sc, 1 inc - repeat 6 times. (30)
6. 4sc, 1 inc - repeat 6 times. (36)
7. 8. 9. sc around. (36)
10. 4 sc, 1 dec - repeat 6 times. (30)
11. 3 sc, 1 dec - repeat 6 times. (24)
12. 2 sc, 1 dec - repeat 6 times. Stuff the core of the sun. (18)
13. 1 sc, 1 dec - repeat 6 times. (12)
14. 6 dec. (6)
Fasten off, cut the yarn leaving a tail.
Close the hole: weave the yarn tail through the front loop of each stitch and then pull tight.
Hide the remaining tail.
Make a slip knot with orange yarn.
2
Insert the hook in any stitch of round 8.
RAYS
Pull the slip knot through the stitch, then start the rays as follows:
ORANGE YARN 1 sc, 1 hdc in next stitch, 3 dc in same stitch, 1 hdc in next stitch - repeat until you have 11
rays.
As a final step, slip stitch into the very first sc you made over round 8.
Fasten off, cut the yarn and hide the tails.
Embroider a face, making 2 “v”s for the eyes and add a smile.
3
You can use leftover yarn or floss.
FACE
You are all done!
