Little Red Riding Hood Crochet Pattern;https://www.lovecrafts.com/en-gb/p/little-red-riding-hood-rag-dolls-crochet-pattern-by-chord-clan-designs;"Abbreviations
Dec -> invisible decrease. Insert hook into front loops only of next 2 stitches, yarn over, pull through 2
​
loops on hook, yarn over, pull through final 2 loops on hook, counts as 1 single crochet. Tutorial
​
FO -> finish off. Always leave a tail which can be useful for sewing your doll together and weave in ends
​
at the end
Sc -> single crochet, Sc x 5 -> Single stitch 5 times, Dc -> double crochet
​ ​ ​ ​ ​
Inc -> Increase, doing two Sc in a single spot. Tutorial
​ ​
Magic circle -> This is the basic stitch that starts out all circular patterns in amigurumi. Here’s my favorite
​
tutorial: https://www.allfreecrochet.com/Tutorials/How-to-Crochet-the-Magic-Circle
​
Whip Stitch -> This is the stitch used to sew together any doll. I don’t go into great detail on how to do
​
this because precision isn’t important. Each toy should come out unique, but I’ll provide enough
photographs so that you can tell where I attached each part. Tutorial: http://www.wikihow.com/Whipstitch
​
Sc around X times -> Single crochet stitch around the entire row, for X rows.
​
Rows with a repeating pattern are written like “[Sc 4, inc] around (12)”, which means to repeat the
​ ​
pattern in [ ] until the end of the row. 12 is the number of stitches you’ll have when finished. When doing
these, I place a stitch marker in the last stitch so that I only have to count the up to the length within the []
and I just keep on doing that until I hit my marker.
Little Red Riding Hood Rag Dolls Crochet Pattern
Chord Clan Designs, Jordanna Chord
