​
Using polymer clay I shaped a bunch of
different eyes to try on before choosing the
final one.
Because my doll wasn’t for a kid I just super
glued them onto to the face.
I bake them in an pan with a bed of the
polyfill, the same polyfill I used to stuff the doll
with.
Polyfill bedding for the clay pieces helps bake
tiny pieces more evenly.
If you want to do child safe eyes, they work
too, but you will need to attach them before
sewing the top close.
