Clover Leaf (Make 4)
Using green yarn.
Each clover leaf is created by combining two parts together to create the
ends of the leaf.
Begin by crocheting the two leaf ends.
Leaf Ends (Make 2)
rnd 1 6 MR (6)
rnd 2 6 INC (12)
rnd 3 (1 Sc, 1 INC) x 6 (18)
Cut the yarn and fasten off on the first leaf end. Do not cut the yarn on the
second leaf end.
Starting from the last stitch of round 3 on the second leaf.
rnd 4 9 Sc on the second leaf, 18 Sc on the (36)
first leaf, 9 Sc into the remaining stitches
on the second leaf
Page 5
The leaf tops should now be combined. Continue crocheting the remainder of
the leaf.
rnd 5 (5 Sc, 1 DEC, 5 Sc) x 3 (33)
rnd 6 33 Sc (33)
rnd 7 (9 Sc, 1 DEC) x 3 (30)
rnd 8 30 Sc (30)
rnd 9 (4 Sc, 1 DEC, 4 Sc) x 3 (27)
rnd 10 27 Sc (27)
rnd 11 (7 Sc, 1 DEC) x 3 (24)
rnd 12 24 Sc (24)
rnd 13 (3 Sc, 1 DEC, 3 Sc) x 3 (21)
rnd 14 21 Sc (21)
rnd 15 (5 Sc, 1 DEC) x 3 (18)
Cut the yarn and fasten off for the first three leaves. Do not cut the yarn on
the fourth leaf.
Copyright © 2022 erinmaycrochet. All Rights Reserved.
Page 6
Clover Top
The clover is created by attaching the four leaves together and crocheting
the top and stem of the clover. Starting from the last round of the fourth
leaf, begin to crochet the top of the clover.
Tip #1 – Add or remove a few stitches as needed on the last leaf to make
sure the round ends at the edge of the leaf when folded over. See the photo
below as an example of where the last round of the fourth leaf should end.
Copyright © 2022 erinmaycrochet. All Rights Reserved.
Page 7
rnd 1 9 Sc onto the first leaf, 9 Sc on the (36)
second leaf, 9 Sc on the third leaf,
9 Sc on the fourth leaf
rnd 2 (2 Sc, 1 DEC, 2 Sc) x 6 (30)
rnd 3 (3 Sc, 1 DEC) x 6 (24)
rnd 4 (1 Sc, 1 DEC, 1 Sc) x 6 (18)
rnd 5 (1 Sc, 1 DEC) x 6 (12)
rnd 6 6 DEC (12)
Cut the yarn and use the yarn tail to close the remaining stiches. The top of
the clover is now complete, and the four leaves should be combined.
Copyright © 2022 erinmaycrochet. All Rights Reserved.
Page 8
Clover Stem
Flip the clover over and begin to crochet the stem in the same way as the
top. Reattach the yarn to one of the remaining stitches of the leaves.
rnd 1 9 Sc onto the first leaf, 9 Sc on the (36)
second leaf, 9 Sc on the third leaf,
9 Sc on the fourth leaf
rnd 2 (2 Sc, 1 DEC, 2 Sc) x 6 (30)
