Mer-bear;https://www.lovecrafts.com/en-gb/p/mer-bear-knitting-pattern-by-cheezombie;;"Mer-bear
Materials needed:
A few oz of sport weight yarn
3 size 3.5 double pointed needles
small crochet hook
buttons/thread
fiberfill
Note: actual stitch gauge is unimportant, but it should be tight enough so the stuffing does
not poke through. The examples are approximately 8 inches high and 4 inches across,
but the finished size will vary with yarn and needle substitutions.
Stitch Glossary
K knit
Kfb knit into front and back loops of stitch
K2tog knit 2 stitches together as one
St stitch
M1 make 1 stitch
Note: for the purposes of this pattern pick up a loop from stitch in row
below working stitch, instead of the “bar” between stitches
Ssk slip 2 stitches, one at a time, from left needle to right, then insert left
needle into stitches and knit them together
Sl1 k1 psso slip 1 stitch, knit the next stitch, then pass the slipped stitch over the knit
stitch and off the needle
K1 sl1 psso knit 1 stitch, slip next stitch from left needle to right, slip both stitches
back to left needle, slip left stitch over right stitch and off needle, return
remaining stitch to right needle
Detailed directions, pictures, and video of all of these techniques can easily be found
through Google.
The bear is knit from bottom to top.
Cast on 12 stitches with tail color, six each on 2 double pointed needles.
Join and knit 2 rounds.
Round 3 m1 k6 m1 repeat 16 st
Round 4 knit
Round 5 m1 k8 m1 repeat 20 st
Round 6 knit
Round 7 m1 k10 m1 repeat 24 st
Round 8 knit
Round 9 m1 k12 m1 repeat 28 st
Round 10-16 knit
Optional: add knit rounds here for a longer tail.
On last round, place stitch marker after 7th stitch and 21st stitch.
Rearrange stitches on needles to work front to back instead of side to side with 14 stitches
on each needle.
Drop tail color and join body color on right side of 1st needle.
Round 17-20 knit
Optional: add a few knit rounds here for a longer torso
Round 21 ssk k24 k2tog 26 st
Round 22 knit
Round 23 ssk k9 k2tog repeat 22 st
Round 24 knit
Round 25 ssk k18 k2tog 20 st
Round 26 knit
Round 27 ssk k6 k2tog repeat 16 st
Round 28 knit
Round 29 ssk k12 k2tog 14 st
Round 30 knit
Round 31 kfb k5 kfb repeat 18 st
Round 32 knit
Round 33 kfb k7 kfb repeat 22 st
Round 34 knit
Round 35 kfb k9 kfb repeat 26 st
Round 36 knit
Round 37 kfb k24 kfb 28 st
Round 38-40 knit
At this point I like to stuff the lower body.
Round 41 (sl1 k1 psso) k24 (k1 sl1 psso) 26 st
Round 42 (sl1 k1 psso) k22 (k1 sl1 psso) 24 st
Round 43 (sl1 k1 psso) k8 k2tog ssk k8( k1 sl1 psso) 20 st
Round 44 knit
Round 45 ssk k6 k2tog repeat 16 st
Round 46 knit
Round 47 ssk k4 k2tog repeat 12 st
Round 48 ssk k2 k2tog repeat 8 st
Cut yarn and draw through remaining stitches loosely. Stuff bear and pull stitches tight.
Tailfin
Cast on 6 stitches
Row 1 knit
Row 2 purl
Row 3 kfb repeat 12 st
Row 4 purl
Row 5 k2 kfb repeat 16 st
Row 6 purl
Row 7 knit
Row 8 purl
Row 9 k8 and leave remaining 8 st on left needle. Put these stitches on a holder,
they will be worked later.
Next row turn and purl 8
Next row kfb k5 k2tog 8 st
Next row purl
Repeat last two rows once and bind off. More repeats can be added for longer fins.
Put leftover stitches back on a needle and attach yarn on the purl side.
Next row purl
Next row (knit side) k2tog k5 kfb
Next row purl
Repeat last 2 rows once and bind off. Sew to end of tail.
Tip: single crochet around the edges will make a stiffer fin.
Ears knit 2
Cast on 5 stitches
Knit 4 rows
Row 5 k2tog k1 k2tog 3 st
Bind off
Sew to top of head.
Tip: weave yarn in and out around outer edge of ear and pull slightly. This can help
create a curved ear shape.
Finishing Options
Paws
Make 2 with tail color and 2 with body color
Cast on 6 stitches
Row 1 knit
Row 2 purl
Row 3 kfb k4 kfb 8 st
Row 4 purl
Row 5 kfb k6 kfb 10 st
Row 6 purl
Row 7 knit
Row 8 purl
Row 9 k2tog k6 k2tog 8 st
Row 10 purl
Row 11 k2tog k4 k2tog 6st
Bind off
Sew purl sides together of opposite yarns, leaving a space to stuff. Finish stuffing and
sew to sides of body.
Fins (make 2)
Cast on 4 stitches
Row 1 knit
Row 2 kfb each st 8 st
Row 3 knit
Change color and knit 4 rows.
Bind off and sew to sides of body. For a seahorse look, knit a 3rd fin and sew to top of
the head like a mohawk.
Flower
Chain 4
Slip stitch into first chain
Chain 3
Slip stitch into first chain again
Repeat 4 times
Cut yarn and pull through. Sew next to ear.
Sew on buttons for eyes and embroider nose and mouth.
