Putting it Together:
Stuff the teeth and sew them along the bottom of the metroid so the two large ones are on opposite
ends of each other and the smaller teeth are evenly spaced between those. The teeth should overlap
both the body and mouth colors. Sew the three dots in a triangle shape pointing upward. Tie off and sew
in any lose ends that may remain into the body.
