Sweet Oddity Art;https://www.lovecrafts.com/en-gb/p/mini-ghost-crochet-pattern-by-carolyne-brodie;"Abbreviations:
mr= magic ring- crochet single crochet stitches in to the
adjustable loop BLO= back loops only
ch= chain stitch F/O= Fasten off
sc= single crochet stitch hdc= half double crochet dc-inc= double crochet increase
sl= slip stitch FLO= front loops only tr=triple crochet
dc= double crochet stitch inc3= 3 sc in the same stitch
inc= increase- make two single crochet stitches in the same stitch
dec=decrease- crochet two stitches together using the decrease method
(4 sc, inc) x 6= repeat the pattern between parentheses 6 times
Notes:
• Do not join rounds unless stated, work in a continuous spiral
• Use a stitch marker to mark the beginning of each round
• All stitches are worked in both loops unless stated otherwise in the pattern
Sweet Oddity Art 2
Head:
Crocheted from top of head to bottom
With Color A:
1. Make 6 sc into a magic ring= 6
2. Increase in each st around= 12
3. (sc, inc) x 6= 18
4. (2 sc, inc) x 6= 24
5. (3 sc, inc) x 6= 30
6. (4 sc, inc) x 6= 36
7-11. sc in each st around
Place eyes between rounds 9 and 10,
leaving 8 holes in between them.
12. (4 sc, dec) x 6= 30
Start stuffing the head
13. sc in each st around
14. (3 sc, dec) x 6= 24
15. BLO (2 sc, dec) x 6= 18
16. (sc, dec) x 6= 12
17. Dec x 6= 6
F/O and sew the hole closed
Body/Sheet:
Attach Color A yarn to round 15 of the head with a sl st
1. sc in each st around
2. (2 sc, inc) x 6= 24
3. (3 sc, inc) x 6= 30
4. sc in each st around
5. (4 sc, inc) x 6= 36
6. (5 sc, inc) x 6= 42
7. sc in each st around
8. (6 sc, inc) x 6= 48
9. (7 sc, inc) x 6= 54
10. sc in each st around
11. (8 sc, inc) x 6= 60
12. (skip a stitch, 5 dc in the same st, skip a stitch, sc) x 15= 90
F/O and weave in the tail ends
Sweet Oddity Art 3
Bow:
Starting with Color A:
Ch 12
1. sc in 2nd ch from hook and across= 11
2. Ch 1, turn, sc across
Change to Color B:
3-4. Repeat row 2
Change to Color C:
5-6. Repeat row 2
F/O and weave in the tail ends
Middle of Bow:
Starting with Color A:
Ch 5
1. sc in 2nd chain from hook and across= 4
2. Ch 1, turn, sc in each st across= 4
3-4. repeat row 2
Change to Color B:
5-8. Repeat Row 2
Change to Color C:
9-12. Repeat Row 2
You may need to adjust the amount of rows if it is too long for the bow.
F/O and use the tail to sew it around the middle of the bow.
Sweet Oddity Art 4
Assembly
1. Sew the bow onto the head.
2. Add some blush to the cheeks with pink eyeshadow or pink crayon.
3. For the extra light you can add a little battery operated tea light under her if you want.
4. Embroider a little mouth with black embroidery thread.
5. You can add some spots to the eyes with white acrylic paint if wanted.
Sweet Oddity Art 5";;Lovecrafts
