If you've made amigurumi before, you may have noticed the gap or bump that forms when you
decrease.The invisible decrease is an alternative method of decreasing which will make your
decrease stitch look much like the other stitches in the row or round. It is as good as its name
claims – it’s almost impossible to see, even if you know what you’re looking for. In this video
you can learn how to make invisible decreases (click on the link or scan QR code):
https://youtu.be/JPEBcQip3Ko
HEART Use red color yarn.
Round 1: mr, sc 6 = [6]
Round 2: (sc 1, inc) x 3 = [9]
Round 3: (sc 2, inc) x 3 = [12]
Round 4: sc 2, inc 2, sc 4, inc 2, sc 2 = [16]
Round 5: sc in each st around = [16]
Round 6: sc 3, inc 2, sc 6, inc 2, sc 3 = [20]
Round 7: sc in each st around = [20]
Round 8: sc 4, inc 2, sc 8, inc 2, sc 4 = [24]
Round 9 (See the picture below): Make sl st into the 12th stitch from the start of the round. Now we
have 2 equal parts of 12 stitches each. Continue crocheting to the left.
sc in next 11 sts, sc into the stitch with wich we joined the sides of the heard = [12]
3
Round 10: (sc 2, dec) x 3 = [9]
Round 11: (sc 1, dec) x 3= [6]
Cut off the yarn and fasten off. Stuff the heart tightly.
After you have finished crochet the first side of the heart, join
the yarn.Continue crocheting to the left.
While joining and continue crocheting there will be a gap. You
can sew it when the piece is ready.
Round 1: chain 1 (this chain 1 is the first stitch of the round), sc
in next 11 sts = [12]
Round 2: (sc 2, dec) x 3 = [9] Finish stuffing.
Round 3: (sc 1, dec) x 3= [6]
Cut off the yarn and fasten off. You can leave a long yarn tail to
make a hanging loop.
A full video tutorial on how to crochet the heart and and make the
hanging loop can be watched here (click on the link or scan QR code):
https://youtu.be/uMd87Q7bSvc
