By Isabela Tavares;https://www.lovecrafts.com/en-gb/p/mini-koala-amigurumi-crochet-pattern-crochet-pattern-by-my-new-craft-amigurumis;"ABBREVIATIONS
ch = chain dec = decrease
slst = slip stitch BLO = Back Loop Only
sc = single crochet FLO = Front Loop Only
hdc = half double MR = Magic Ring
crochet ( ) = repeat sequence
dc = double crochet [ ] = total number of
tc = treble crochet stitches
inc = increase
Isabela Tavares 04
v. 1.1
INSTRUCTIONS
Head/Body
(Grey)
1- 6 sc into the MR [6]
2- 6 inc [12]
3- (1 sc, 1 inc) x6 [18]
4- (2 sc, 1 inc) x6 [24]
5- (3 sc, 1 inc) x6 [30]
6 to 12- Sc around [30]
Attach the eyes at the front of the head and between
rows 8 and 9, with 6 stitches between them.
13- (3 sc, 1 dec) x6 [24]
14- (2 sc, 1 dec) x6 [18]
15- (1 sc, 1 dec) x6 [12]
Stuff as you weave.
16- FLO (1 sc, 1 inc) x6 [18]
17- (2 sc, 1 inc) x6 [24]
18 to 21- Sc around [24]
22- (2 sc, 1 dec) x6 [18]
23- (1 sc, 1 dec) x6 [12]
24- 6 dec [6]
Fasten off and hide the thread.
Isabela Tavares 05
v. 1.1
Muzzle
(Black)
Into the MR:
1 sc, 1 hdc, 1 dc, 1 hdc
1 sc, 1 hdc, 1 dc, 1 hdc
Close with 1 slst in the first stitch.
Fasten off and leave a long tail for sewing.
Note: you can hide the remaining thread from the
Magic Ring as you weave or, at the end, just cut it
leaving a very small leftover.
Ears
Bigger Part (Grey) - make 2:
1- 6 sc into the MR [6]
2- 6 inc [12]
Fasten off and leave a long tail for
sewing.
OBS: You can hide the remaining
thread from the Magic Ring as you weave or, at the
end, pass it forward through the central hole and cut
it.
Minor Part (Off-White) - make 2:
1- 6 sc into the MR
Close with 1 slst in the first stitch.
Fasten off and hide the thread.
Note: you can hide the remaining
thread from the Magic Ring as you
weave or, at the end, just cut it
leaving a very small leftover.
Isabela Tavares 06
v. 1.1
Arms
(Grey) - make 2:
1- 6 sc into the MR [6]
2- (1 sc, 1 inc) x3 [9]
3 to 4- Sc around [9]
Fasten off and leave a long tail
for sewing. Stuff a little.
Legs
(Grey) - make 2:
1- 6 sc into the MR [6]
2- 6 inc [12]
3 to 4- Sc around [12]
5- 6 dec [6]
Fasten off and leave a long tail
for sewing. Stuff a little.
Belly
(Off-White)
1- 6 sc into the MR [6]
2- 6 inc [12]
Fasten off and leave a long tail
for sewing.
Note: you can hide the
remaining thread from the
magic ring as you weave or, at
the end, just cut it leaving a very
small leftover.
Isabela Tavares 07
v. 1.1
Scarf
(Green)
56 chain stitches, 1 slst into the
second stitch from the hook,
54 slst.
Fasten off.
ASSEMBLY
Sew the muzzle between the eyes
(the top of the muzzle in line with
the top of the eyes).
Sew the larger parts of the ear to
the Koala's head, at the level of
the eyes, 4 stitches away from
each eye.
Glue the minor parts of the ears
over the larger parts.
Isabela Tavares 08
v. 1.1
Sew the arms to the sides of the
body (at the height of rows 16
and 17) and the legs a little
more to the center than the
arms (at the height of rows 20
and 21).
Sew the belly.
Tie the scarf around
Koala's neck and that's
it!
Thanks for
crocheting
with me!
Oh! The Mini Koala can
also be a keychain!
