ch - chain (UK - chain)
sc - single crochet (UK - double crochet)
dc - double crochet (UK - treble crochet)
tr - triple crochet (UK - double treble crochet)
inc - 2 single crochet stitches in the same stitch (UK - increase in double crochet)
dec - 2 single crochet stitches together (UK - decrease in double crochet)
(É) - repeat what is inside ( ) symbols the number of times speciÞed in pattern
[É] - total amount of stitches in the round
fo - fasten off (UK - fasten off)
2
PATTERN
BODY
Start with gray yarn.
Round 1: 6 sc in a magic ring [6]
R2: (1 inc) x 6 [12]
R3: (1 sc, 1 inc) x 6 [18]
R4: (2 sc, 1 inc) x 6 [24]
R5: (3 sc, 1 inc) x 6 [30]
R6: (4 sc, 1 inc) x 6 [36]
R7 - R16: Sc around [36] - 10 rounds
Change to pink yarn.
R17 - R23: Sc around [36] - 7 rounds
R24: (4 sc, 1 dec) x 6 [30]
Fo. Cut the yarn leaving a tail for sewing.
Stuff the body Þrmly and sew it like on the photo.
3
EYES
Use white yarn
Round 1: 6 sc in a magic ring [6]
R2: (1 inc) x 6 [12]
R3: Sc around [12]
Fo. Cut the yarn leaving a tail for sewing.
Make 2.
Pupil of the eyes
Make magic ring and 6 sc in it. Sl st in the Þrst sc. (use
black thread Yarn Art IRIs or other and the crochet
hook 1mm).
Make 2.
BEAK
Use yellow yarn.
Make a foundation chain with 3 ch.
Round 1: Starting in the 2nd chain from the hook: 2 sc
[2]
R2: turn work around, 1 dec [1]
Fo. Cut the yarn leaving a tail for sewing.
4
WINGS
Use pink yarn
Left wing
Round 1: 6 sc in a magic ring [6]
R2: (1 inc) x 2, 2 hdc in next st, 2 dc in next st, 2 tr in next st.
Fo. Cut the yarn leaving a tail for sewing.
Right wing
Round 1: 6 sc in a magic ring [6]
R2: 4 ch, 1 tr in the same loop, 2 dc in next st, 2 hdc in next st, (1 inc) x 2
Fo. Cut the yarn leaving a tail for sewing.
5
FINISHING
Sew the eyes to the body after the 8th row.
Sew the beak and wings.
Make ears.
Put the yarn into the outer loop using the hook. Put the edges of the yarn into the
formed loop and tighten it.
6
Your owl is ready!
