General instructions
• This pattern is worked in continuous round : do not join or turn unless stated otherwise.
• Mark the last stitch of the round with your stitch marker in order to check that you’ve
made the right amount of stitches in the round.
• You’ll see that the increases and decreases of the pattern are shifted every other row.
That’s to avoid the small line that shows when you keep on making your increases and
decreases at the same place.
• If you print this pattern, you can tick the ○ to help you get your bearings.
