Pattern Notes
• As with all amigurumi patterns, stitches should be worked
tightly to help ensure the finished project keeps its shape.
• Each round is worked in a spiral and does not need to be
joined unless specifically stated.
• Pattern is written in US terms
Cone (Make 1)
Starting with orange yarn.
rnd 1 6 MR (6)
rnd 2 6 INC (12)
rnd 3 (1 Sc, 1 INC) x 6 (18)
rnd 4 BLO 18 Sc (18)
rnd 5 (5 Sc, 1 INC) x 3 (21)
rnd 6 21 Sc (21)
rnd 7 (3 Sc, 1 INC, 3 Sc) x 3 (24)
rnd 8 24 Sc (24)
rnd 9 (7 Sc, 1 INC) x 3 (27)
Copyright © 2022 erinmaycrochet. All Rights Reserved.
Page 5
Switch to white yarn.
rnd 10 27 Sc (27)
rnd 11 (4 Sc, 1 INC, 4 Sc) x 3 (30)
rnd 12 30 Sc (30)
rnd 13 (9 Sc, 1 INC) x 3 (33)
Switch to orange yarn.
rnd 14 33 Sc (33)
rnd 15 (5 Sc, 1 INC, 5 Sc) x 3 (36)
rnd 16 36 Sc (36)
rnd 17 (11 Sc, 1 INC) x 3 (39)
rnd 18 39 Sc (39)
rnd 19 (6 Sc, 1 INC, 6 Sc) x 3 (42)
rnd 20 FLO 42 Sc (42)
rnd 21 (3 Sc, 1 INC, 3 Sc) x 6 (48)
rnd 22 (11 Sc, 3 Sc in same stitch) x 4 (56)
rnd 23 12 Sc, 3 Sc in same stitch, (13 Sc, (64)
3 Sc in same stitch) x 3, 1 Sc
rnd 24 13 Sc, 3 Sc in same stitch, (72)
(15 Sc, 3 Sc in same stitch) x 3,
2 Sc
Cut the yarn and fasten off invisibly.
