This is the original pattern of mini whale by Yevheniia Romanchuk.;https://www.lovecrafts.com/en-gb/p/mini-whale-or-dolphin-crochet-pattern-by-lovenikadesign;;"This is the original pattern of mini whale by Yevheniia Romanchuk.
This purchase is for personal purposes only. You may sell the finished toy you
created with the help of these instructions, but you are NOT allowed to sell the
pattern or copy, share or distribute it in digital or paper form. Thank you for your
understanding.
Finished size
Using similar yarn and 2,5 mm crochet hook, mini whale is around 6 cm (2.3”) length.
Page 1 of 7
@Yevheniia Romanchuk
Supplies
1. Yarn: This example is crocheted from YarnArt Jeans yarn (cotton 55%,
acrylic 45%, 50g = 160m), color – 33 (blue).
2. Crochet hook: 2,5 mm, or in accordance with the yarn you use.
3. A little piece of a different color yarn or stitch marker (I use first one).
4. Fiber filling.
5. А thick needle.
6. One pair of 5 mm black safety eyes.
7. Pins.
8. Scissors.
Notes
Work in continuous rounds. Don’t join or turn if not instructed in the pattern.
Use a stitch marker (or a piece of yarn). Place it at the last (or first) stitch of the
row and always move it up when working to the last (or first) stitches of the
rows.
When finishing flippers, fin and tail leave a long yarn tail (around 20 cm) which
you can use for sewing.
Don’t fill the stuffing into the flippers, fin and tail.
If you need some help, please, message me. I'll always help you.
Page 2 of 7
@Yevheniia Romanchuk
Pattern
Body:
Legend
1: 6sc in mr (6) rnd(s) – round(s)
2: 6inc (12) mr – magic ring
ch – chain
3: (sc, inc)*6 (18)
sc – single crochet
4: (2sc, inc)*6 (24)
st(s) – stitch(es)
5: 15sc, inc, 4sc, inc, 3sc (26)
ss – slip stitch
6: 17sc, inc, 2sc, inc, 5sc (28)
inc –1 increase = 2 sc in the same st
7: 19sc, 2inc, 7sc (30)
dec – 1 decrease = 2 sc together
8: 5sc, 2inc, 13sc, 2inc, 8sc (34)
sc3tog – 3sc together
9: 6sc, 2inc, 15sc, 2inc, 9sc (38)
(…) *n – repeat n times
10: sc in each st around (38)
(n) – stitch count of the row
11: 4sc, 4dec, 4sc, dec, 5sc, 4dec, 5sc,
dec (28)
If you use eyes, place them between rounds 8 and 9 leaving 9 sts between
them (7 viewable sts).
Fill the body with a fiber filler.
12: dec, sc, dec, 2sc, (dec, sc)*2, dec, 2sc, 3dec, 2sc, dec, sc (19)
13: 6dec, sc3tog, 2dec (9)
Cut the yarn, leaving yarntail. Tighten the hole with the help of needle, hide the
yarntail inside the toy.
Find video help for ultimate finishing
of amigurumi here:
https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SMkNQAZ5Si0
Page 3 of 7
@Yevheniia Romanchuk
Flippers (2 details):
1: 4sc in MR (4)
2: (sc, inc)*2 (6)
3: 5sc, inc (7)
4: 6sc, inc (8), ss to the next st.
Cut yarn leaving long yarntail for sewing.
Page 4 of 7
@Yevheniia Romanchuk
Dorsal fin:
1: 4sc in MR (4)
2: (sc, inc)*2 (6)
3: 5sc, inc (7), ss to the next st.
Cut yarn leaving long yarntail for sewing.
Tail:
1: 4sc in MR (4)
2: (sc, inc)*2 (6)
3: sc in each st around (6)
4: inc, 4sc, inc (8)
Make 2 identical details. On first crochet ss, cut
the yarn. On the second detail don’t crochet ss
and don’t cut the yarn, continue crocheting on
the first detail, starting from the ss:
5: 3sc, dec, 3sc, on the second detail: 3sc, dec, 3sc (14)
6: 2sc, sc3tog, sc, dec, sc, sc3tog, 2sc (9), ss to the next st.
Cut yarn leaving long yarntail for sewing.
Page 5 of 7
@Yevheniia Romanchuk
Sew the tail to the body over rnd 10.
Sew the flippers to the body over rnd 11.
Page 6 of 7
@Yevheniia Romanchuk
Sew the dorsal fin to the body over rnds 4-6.
