MonsterHangingToy;https://www.lovecrafts.com/en-gb/p/monster-hanging-toyfree-crochet-patternscrochet-easy-patternscrocheting-projects-for-beginners-crochet-pattern-by-kathy-leung;;"MonsterHangingToy
–FreeCrochetPattern
Looking for a funny crochet gift or a cute amigurumi pattern to make?
This free crochet pattern will guide you through creating an adorable big
eye monster hanging toy! With its bright green body, a single big blue
eye, and cute yellow horns, this little monster is perfect for decorating
bags, keychains, or even as a playful home accessory. Whether you’re a
beginner or an experienced crocheter, this easy crochet pattern is fun to
make and great for all skill levels.
Tagme@directsourceyarn
Materials Needed
• Yarn: Green, blue, white, yellow, and pink (cotton or acrylic)
• Hook: 2.5mm or 3mm crochet hook
• Stuffing: Polyester fiberfill
• Embroidery needle: For details and assembly
• Keyring or loop: If making a hanging toy
Big Eye Monster Crochet Pattern (Step-by-Step)
Head
Use green yarn.
Rnd 1: 6 SC in magic ring [6]
Rnd 2: 6 INC [12]
Rnd 3: (INC, SC) x6 [18]
Rnd 4: (2 SC, INC) x6 [24]
Rnd 5: (3 SC, INC) x6 [30]
Rnd 6: (2 SC, INC, 2 SC) x6 [36]
Rnd 7: (5 SC, INC) x6 [42]
Rnd 8-15: 42 SC [42], 8 rounds
Rnd 16: (5 SC, DEC) x6 [36]
Rnd 17: (2 SC, DEC, 23 SC) x6 [30]
Rnd 18: (3 SC, DEC) x6 [24]
Rnd 19: (2 SC, DEC) x6 [18]
Rnd 20: (DEC, SC) x6 [12]
Rnd 21: 6 DEC [6]
Stuff the head firmly.
Fasten off
Eye
Part 1: Use white yarn.
Rnd 1: 10 DC in magic ring [10]
Rnd 2: 10 DC INC [20]
Invisible fasten off and leaving a 60 cm long tail for sewing.
Part 2: Use blue yarn.
Rnd 1: 7 SC in magic ring [7]
Rnd 2: 7 INC [14]
Invisible fasten off and leaving a long tail for sewing.
Sew the blue eye to the white part.
Horn (make 2)
Use yellow yarn.
Rnd 1: 5 SC in magic ring [5]
Rnd 2: (SC, INC) x2, SC [7]
Rnd 3: (2 SC, INC) x2, SC [9]
Rnd 4: (3 SC, INC) x2, SC [11]
Rnd 5: (4 SC, INC) x2, SC [13]
Cheek (make 2)
Use pink yarn.
Rnd 1: 6 SC in magic ring [6]
Invisible fasten off and leaving a long tail for sewing.
Sew onto both sides of the face.
Mouth
Use blue yarn.
Embroider a simple curved smile below the eye
Assembly & Finishing Touches
• Attach a keyring or loop if making a hanging toy
• Secure all pieces and weave in loose ends
