Pattern Notes
Growing pumpkins is one of my
highlights of the Summer – and
harvesting them in Autumn is even
better!
These little Munchkins are such a cute
variety and are perfect for decorating
the house (before making their way to the oven).
This is a beginner-friendly pattern that’s quick as well as easy to make.
It’s worked in continuous rounds so you’ll want to place a st marker at the
beginning of each round to keeping track of your stitch count. The pumpkin is
then shaped, and the stem is crocheted separately before attaching.
You’ll also find a stitch guide included to help you with the particular stitches
used throughout this pattern, and to grow your amigurumi skills!
You could try making multiple pumpkins in a range of different autumnal
shades, or add some natural variation to the height by adding a few rounds of
xs all round.
Happy crocheting!
