Yarn & Measurements
The colours below are just suggestions and match the images in this pattern.
You can substitute your preference of colours.
I used Hobbii Yarn’s Rainbow Bamboo for my pumpkins in the following colours:
Orange: ginger (21)
Dark green: dusty pine (38)
The left-hand column is how I refer to the colours throughout this pattern; the
right-hand column gives the name and number on the Hobbii website.
You can, of course, use any other light DK weight yarn for this pattern, but I
highly recommend this lovely yarn for its softness, colour palette and sheen.
You’ll need minimal amounts of each colour so this pattern works great as a
stash buster – less than 40g (100m) in total.
When complete, your munchkin squash should measure about 7cm x 9cm,
depending on your chosen yarn and how tightly you crochet.
