Special Stitches
1. Front Loop Only (FLO)
Usually, a crochet stitch is worked through both loops (image 1).
Working in the FLO does not alter your st at all, it just requires you to ignore that
back loop and work only in the front loop instead of both.
Likewise, working through the BLO would simply
mean that you’d be working in that back loop
alone and not the front loop.
front
back
loop
loop
2. ‘X’ or Cross Stitch (xs)
These patterns make use of the ‘x’ or cross stitch
instead of the regular single crochet. This is
generally the preferred st for amigurumi because it Image 1
results in a more plump and neat looking st.
To make it, simply insert your hook into the stitch, YU (instead of YO as you
normally would), pull up a loop, YO, pull through 2 loops.
Here’s a handy video you might find helpful for comparison and to show you how
it’s done:
https://youtube.com/shorts/H3npWfRSv9A?si=Og5p-imRU0-9ND82
