‘base’ to pass off as your own design.
However, if you’re not confident using this st, feel free to use a regular single
crochet in its stead. With only a little practice though, I’m sure you will find it just
as natural to make this classic amigurumi st without even thinking about what
you’re doing.
3. Invisible Decrease (inv-dec)
This technique gives your decreases a neater and less conspicuous look. You can
use a regular decrease if you’d prefer, but you won’t find an inv-dec much more
complicated to make and the results are totally worth any effort required to learn it.
To make an inv-dec:
1. Insert hook into FLO of next st. Do not YO.
2. Insert hook into FLO of 2nd st.
3. YO, pull up a loop.
4. YO, pull through all loops on hook.
