4 a planet of my own
Round 26: * sc2tog, sc in next 3 sts. Repeat from * 5 times (24)
Remove hook, but do not break yarn.
Ring
Hold your baby planet so that round 26 is on the top (so it resembles a bowl).
Round 1: For this round, you will work through the front loops of the stitches on rnd 14 of the
planet. Join a strand of SC to the front loop of a stitch on round 14. Sc a second time in this
same st. Sc in the next 9 sts. * sc twice in next st, sc in next 9 sts. Repeat from * 4 times (66)
Round 2: * sc twice in next st, sc in next 10 sts. Repeat from * 5 times (72)
Round 3: * sc twice in next st, sc in next 11 sts. Repeat from * 5 times (78)
Round 4: * sc twice in next st, sc in next 12 sts. Repeat from * 5 times (84)
Rounds 5-6: sc in each st (84) Round 7: * sc2tog, sc in next 12 sts. Repeat from * 5 times (78)
Round 8: * sc2tog, sc in next 11 sts. Repeat from * 5 times (72)
Round 9: * sc2tog, sc in next 10 sts. Repeat from * 5 times (66)
Round 10: * sc2tog, sc in next 9 sts. Repeat from * 5 times (60)
Fasten off with a long tail.
Your planet should look approximately like the
photo at right. Stuff the ring of your planet, and
with a tapestry needle and the long tail, whipstitch
round 10 of the ring to round 16 of the planet body.
Stuff your planet!
Back to finishing the body of your planet...
Round 27: * sc2tog, sc in next 2 sts. Repeat from * 5 times (18)
Round 28: * sc2tog, sc in next st. Repeat from * 5 times (12)
Round 29: * sc2tog. Repeat from * 5 times (6)
Round 30: sc next and 4th st together. Fasten off, drawing tail to the inside.
Now, all you need to do is give your planet a name!
