Neon Horse;https://www.lovecrafts.com/en-gb/p/neon-the-horse-crochet-pattern-by-cara-engwerda;"Abbreviations:
 2.0mm hook/B-1 (US)  MR = magic ring
 4ply yarn/fingering > less than 50g in  BLO = back loops only
BEIGE, APRICOT, PURPLE and PINK  ch = chain
 8mm safety eyes  sc = single crochet
 dc = double crochet
 Scissors
 inc = single crochet increase (2 sc in
 Tapestry needle
one stitch)
 Polyester toy stuffing
 3dc = 3 dc in one stitch
 Stitch marker
 dec = decrease (sc 2 together)
 sl st = slip stitch
 (..) = repeat the space in brackets the
given number of times
 [..] = total number of stitches
Notes:
 A yarn with no stretch is best for amigurumi, I ordinarily use cotton or cotton blend.
 Amigurumi is stitched in the round (unless it says otherwise).
 For this pattern, the following yarns were used:
o BEIGE = Hobbii Cotton Kings 8/4 in colour 02
o APRICOT = Hobbii Rainbow Cotton 8/4 in colour 89
o PURPLE = Hobbii Rainbow Cotton 8/4 in colour 39
o PINK = Hobbii Rainbow Glitter Gold in colour 044
 Generally, the hook you use for amigurumi will be a smaller than for other crochet as you
want the stitches tight.
 The yarn thickness and hook size used will affect the size of the finished item. My Neon the
Horse is approximately 15m tall when seated (5 ¾ inches).
 I have used safety eyes for this pattern but you may choose to embroider. Please ensure
that there are no loose fittings.
