© Cara Engwerda trading as Cara’s Creations, 2021
25) (sc, dec) x 6 [12]
Fasten off, weave tail through final round
and pull to close. Leave a tail for sewing.
Mane (PINK):
Leave a long tail at the beginning for sewing. You will
work in rows and turn at the end of each row. Chains
do not count as a stitch.
1) ch16, sc in 2nd ch from hook, sc x 14 [15]
2) ch2 and 3dc in same stitch, 3dc x 14 [45]
3) ch2 and 3dc in same stitch, 3dc x 44
[135]
Fasten off and leave a tail for sewing.
Tail (PINK):
Leave a long tail at the beginning for sewing. You
will work in rows and turn at the end of each row.
Chains do not count as a stitch.
1) ch9, sc in 2nd ch from hook, sc x 7 [8]
2) ch2 and 3dc in same stitch, 3dc x 7 [24]
3) ch2 and 3dc in same stitch 3dc x 24 [72]
Fasten off and leave a tail for sewing.
Patch (BEIGE):
1) ch 6, sc in 2nd chain from hook, sc x 3,
3sc in the final chain, turn and work
on the other side: sc x 3, inc [12]
2) inc, sc x 3, inc, sc, inc, sc x 3, inc, sc [16]
3) sc, inc, sc x 4, inc, sc, inc, sc x 5, inc, sc [20]
Fasten off and leave a tail for sewing.
Assembly (photos over the page):
1) EYES – using APRICOT, sew over a stitch on
the inner part of each eye (As shown) and
pull a little to create an indent. Tie off yarn
tails and hide inside the head.
2) PATCH – sew to the centre of the head over
rounds 12-19.
3) HEAD – sew to the body. Go around twice to
make secure.
4) EARS – sew to either side of the head over
rounds 189-22. Approx. 3 stitches from the patch.
5) LEGS – sew to rounds 5-7 of the body pointing outwards, 3 stitches apart.
6) ARMS – sew to the body over rounds 17-22 on a diagonal so the arms point slightly forward
and rest on the legs.
7) MANE – approx. 1 round after the patch, sew down the back of the head.
5 | P age
© Cara Engwerda trading as Cara’s Creations, 2021
8) TAIL – sew to the back of the body over
rounds 6-11.
9) NOSTRILS – using APRICOT, making 2
vertical lines over rounds 3-5, approx. 5
stitches apart.
That’s it! Enjoy your Neon.
