Jordanna Chord
​
No Left Overs Amigurumi Pig Crochet Pattern
Jordanna Chord Page 1
​ ​
Shopping list
Polymer Clay
Crochet Hooks
Caron Simple Soft Yarn
Stitch Markers
Nuts and Bolts
Superglue
No Left Overs Amigurumi Pig Crochet Pattern
Jordanna Chord Page 2
​ ​
Step 1. Make eyes
Take about 1 oz of white polymer clay and a little dot of black clay for the pupil. I rolled each into
a ball and then flattened them. I used a toothpick to make the two eyes connected and provide
stability. The eyes are 1 inch tall. I attached a nut to the back for attaching to the doll (which is
optional if you choose just to superglue them on).
Indentations for the pupils was made with my Toothpicks provide a bit of stability.
crochet hook.
I attached to the back ah nut with a small Bake on top of a bit of polyfill so they can lie
snake of clay. wrapped around the base. flat. Bake per your clay’s instructions.
No Left Overs Amigurumi Pig Crochet Pattern
Jordanna Chord Page 3
​ ​
Step 2. Make the tail
Wrap yarn around a small piece of wire for
the tail.
To attach, shape the end of wire into a loop
that you can thread a knot into. I then sew
that into the doll. The tail helps to hold up
your doll, so place it at the very bottom when
you attach.
No Left Overs Amigurumi Pig Crochet Pattern
Jordanna Chord Page 4
​ ​
Step 3. Make the body
1. Magic circle with 6 stitches
2. [Inc] around (12)
3. [Sc, Inc] around (18)
4. [Sc x 2, Inc] around (24)
5. [Sc x 3, Inc] around (30)
6. [Sc x 4, Inc] around (36)
7. [Sc x 5, Inc] around (42)
8. Sc around, using the inner loop only.
This causes the bend so that you get
the flat bottom. (42)
9. Sc around (42)
10.Sc x 10, Inc, [Sc x 13, Inc] x 3, Sc 3
(46)
11.Sc around three times
12.Sc x 3, Inc, Sc x 11, Inc, Sc x 9, Inc,
Sc x 11, Inc, Sc x 8 (50)
13.Sc around three times
14.Sc x 4, Inc, Sc x 11, [Inc, Sc x 12] x 2,
Inc, Sc 9 (54)
15.Sc around three times
16.Sc x 5, Dec, [Sc x 11, Dec] x 2, Sc x
12, Dec, Sc x 7 (50)
17.Sc around three times
18.Sc x 7, Dec, [Sc x 11, Dec] x 2, Sc x
10, Dec, Sc x 3 (46)
19.Sc around once
No Left Overs Amigurumi Pig Crochet Pattern
Jordanna Chord Page 5
​ ​
20.Sc x 4, [Dec, Sc x 10] x 3, Dec, Sc 4
(42)
21.Sc x 4, [Dec, Sc x 9] x 3, Dec, Sc 4
(38)
22.Sc x 4, [Dec, Sc x 8] x 3, Dec, Sc 2
(34)
23.Sc x 4, [Dec, Sc x 7] x 3, Dec (30)
24.Sc x 4, [Dec, Sc x 6] x 3, Dec (26)
25.Sc x 4, [Dec, Sc x 5] x 3, Dec (22)
26.Sc x 4, [Dec, Sc x 4] x 3, Dec (18)
A good point to attach the eyes and tail
before you close up the body. Begin stuffing
now too.
27.Sc x 3, [Dec, Sc x 3] x 3, Dec (12)
28.Sc, Dec around. Finish stuffing and
close up.
No Left Overs Amigurumi Pig Crochet Pattern
Jordanna Chord Page 6
​ ​
Step 4. Make the Ears, Arms & Nose
Ears
Make 2
1. Chain 2.
2. [Sc x 3] in second Ch from hook, turn
(3)
3. Sc across, turn (3)
4. Sc in 1st stitch, Inc, 3 Sc in the last
stitch, turn (6)
5. Sc in 1st stitch, Inc, Inc, Sc, Dec,
Finish off.
Nose
1. Magic circle with 6 stitches.
2. Inc around (12)
3. [Sc, Inc] around (18)
4. [Sc x 2, Inc] around (24)
5. Sc around in back loop only. This is
your bend.
6. Sc around twice. Finish off. Stuff
lightly while sewing into place.
No Left Overs Amigurumi Pig Crochet Pattern
Jordanna Chord Page 7
​ ​
Legs
Make 2
1. Magic circle with 6 stitches.
2. Inc around (12)
3. [Sc x 2, Inc] (16)
4. Sc around 4 times.
Arms
Make 2
5. Magic circle with 6 stitches.
6. Inc around (12)
7. [Sc x 2, Inc] (16)
8. Sc around 2 times.
For both, stuff lightly while attaching.
No Left Overs Amigurumi Pig Crochet Pattern
Jordanna Chord Page 8
​ ​
Step 5. Make the wings
I use 18 gauge wire in the chain to give a bit more stability. This is optional, but let’s the wings
have more shape. When you chain, work around the wire by hooking the yarn underneath the
wire as pictured.
Cut the spare wire off and bend the ends over
the last and first stitch of the chain.
Make 2.
1. Chain 30 around the wire.
2. Dc x 30, turn
3. Ch 1, Sc x 20, Ch 6, turn
4. Dc x 25, turn
5. Ch 1, Sc x 15, Ch 6, turn
6. Dc x 20, turn
7. Ch 1, Sc x 10, Ch 6, turn
8. Dc x 15, turn
9. Ch 1, Sc x 5, Ch 6, turn
10.Dc x 10, Finish off.
No Left Overs Amigurumi Pig Crochet Pattern
Jordanna Chord Page 9
​ ​
Sew onto the back however you like.
No Left Overs Amigurumi Pig Crochet Pattern
Jordanna Chord Page 10
​ ​
Step 6. Make the mouth
Wrap yarn around a small piece of wire
shaped into a circle. This shapes the “oh” for
the mouth.
Attach just below the nose.
No Left Overs Amigurumi Pig Crochet Pattern
Jordanna Chord Page 11
​ ​
No Left Overs Amigurumi Pig Crochet Pattern
Jordanna Chord Page 12
