Notamouse
Notes
Tension is not critical for this project, but it may affect the yarn quantities required
Measurements: Notamouse measures 5cm tall
The pattern is worked using the amigurumi method. Work stitches continuously in a spiral
without closing off each round with a slip stitch. It may help to use a stitch marker in the first
stitch of each round, moving it up as you work.
Body
Make a magic loop
Round 1 (RS) Ch1 (does not count as a st throughout) 6dc into loop. [6 sts]
Round 2 2dc in each st around. [12 sts]
Round 3 (Dc in next 2 sts, 2dc in next st) 4 times. [16 sts]
Round 4 (Dc in next 3 sts, 2dc in next st) 4 times. [20 sts]
Round 5 - 6 Dc in each st around.
Round 7 (Dc in next 4 sts, 2dc in next st) 4 times. [24 sts]
Round 8- 14 Dc in each st around.Place safety eyes between round 6/7.
Stuff the body.
Round 15 (Dc in next 2 sts, dc2tog) 6 times. [18 sts]
Round 16 (Dc in next st, dc2tog) 6 times. [12 sts]
Add additional stuffing if required.Round 17 (Dc2tog) 6 times. [6 sts]
Fasten off and weave in ends.
Ears (make 2)
Make a magic loop
Round 1 (RS) Ch1 (does not count as a st throughout) 6dc into loop. [6 sts]
Round 2 2dc in each st around. [12 sts]
Round 3 (Dc next 3 sts, 2dc in next st) 3 times. [15 sts]
Round 4 - 6 Dc in each st around.
Fasten off leaving a long tail to stitch the ears to the body
