Sweet Oddity Art;https://www.lovecrafts.com/en-gb/p/oakley-the-monkey-crochet-pattern-by-carolyne-brodie;"Abbreviations:
mr= magic ring- crochet single crochet stitches in to the
adjustable loop BLO= back loops only
ch= chain stitch F/O= Fasten off
sc= single crochet stitch hdc= half double crochet
sl= slip stitch FLO= front loops only
dc= double crochet stitch inc3= 3 sc in the same stitch
inc= increase- make two single crochet stitches in the same stitch
dec=decrease- crochet two stitches together using the decrease method
(4 sc, inc) x 6= repeat the pattern between parentheses 6 times
Bob= bobble stitch
Notes:
• Do not join rounds unless stated, work in a continuous spiral
• Use a stitch marker to mark the beginning of each round
• All stitches are worked in both loops unless stated otherwise in the pattern
Sweet Oddity Art 2
Legs and Body:
Starting with Legs(Make 2):
With Color B:
1. Make 6 sc into a magic ring= 6
2. Increase in each st around= 12
3. (sc, inc) x 6= 18
4. (2 sc, inc) x 6= 24
5. (3 sc, inc) x 6= 30
6. sc in each st around
Change to Color A:
7-8. sc in each st around
9. dec x 6, 18 sc= 24
10. 2 sc, dec, 9 sc, dec x 2, 7 sc= 21
Start stuffing the feet
11-13. sc in each st around
Change to Color C:
14. (6 sc, inc) x 3= 24(Mark the 3rd st on the 1st leg with a stitch marker)
Do not F/O the 2nd leg!
Work 6 more sc around the top of the 2nd leg, (You are moving the starting position)
Ch 4, work a sc into the marked stitch on leg 1, work 23 more sc around the 1st leg, work 4 sc on
the back of the ch 4, work 24 more sc around the 2nd leg, work 4 sc on the front of the ch 4= 56
Sweet Oddity Art 3
Legs and Body Continued:
1. sc in each st around
2. (13 sc, inc) x 4= 60
3-6. sc in each st around
7. (8 sc, dec) x 6= 54
Stuff the body as you work
8. sc in each st around
9. (7 sc, dec) x 6= 48
10. (On stitch 30 change to Color E) sc in each st around
11. (6 sc, dec) x 6= 42
12. (On stitch 25 change to Color A) sc in each st around
13. sc in each st around
14. (5 sc, dec) x 6= 36
15. 2 sc, bobble stitch, 33 sc= 36
16-17. sc in each st around
18. (10 sc, dec) x 3= 33
19. sc in each st around
20. (9 sc, dec) x 3= 30
21. sc in each st around
22. (8 sc, dec) x 3= 27
23. sc in each st around
24. (7 sc, dec) x 3= 24
F/O and leave a long tail for sewing
Sweet Oddity Art 4
Head:
Crocheted from top to bottom
With Color B:
1. Make 6 sc into a magic ring= 6
2. Increase in each st around= 12
3. (sc, inc) x 6= 18
4. sc, inc, (2 sc, inc) x 5, sc= 24
5. (3 sc, inc) x 6= 30
6. 2 sc, inc, (4 sc, inc) x 5, 2 sc= 36
7. (5 sc, inc) x 6= 42
8. 3 sc, inc, (6 sc, inc) x 5, 3 sc= 48
9-13. sc in each st around
(Mark the 1st and last increase of round 14 with a stitch marker)
14. 10 sc, inc x 6, 10 sc, inc x 6, 16 sc= 60
15-18. sc in each st around
Place eyes between rounds 11 and 12, leaving 10 holes between them. Place the 1st eye before
the 1st increase. Count 10 holes after the first eye and place the 2nd eye. If you want the
sunken eye look, do not place the backs of the eyes on until round 23
Place nose in between rounds 14 and 15, in between the eyes.
19. 10 sc, (sc, dec) x 3, 12 sc, (sc, dec) x 3, 20 sc= 54
20. (7 sc, dec) x 6= 48
21. sc in each st around
22. (6 sc, dec) x 6= 42
23. (5 sc, dec) x 6= 36
Now for the eyes. Stuff the head well. Cut a long piece of yarn and remove the eyes. Place the
needle in the hole where the first eye was and thread the needle into a hole next to the eye
hole. Go back and forth between each eye hole repeating the process from the first eye. Pull
slightly on the yarn after going through each hole. Do this about 3 times on each side until you
reach the look you want. Follow the pictures on pg. 5-6 for help. There is also a youtube video I
have for extra help on this process.
https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9XoBnTY6k70&t=55s
To place the backs of the eyes you will need to remove most of the stuffing to place the
washers on the eyes then re stuff it.
24. sc in each st around
25. (4 sc, dec) x 6= 30
26. (3 sc, dec) x 6= 24
F/O and leave a short tail
Sweet Oddity Art 5
Sweet Oddity Art 6
Cap:
With Color A:
1. Make 6 sc into a magic ring= 6
2. Increase in each st around= 12
3. (sc, inc) x 6= 18
4. (2 sc, inc) x 6= 24
5. (3 sc, inc) x 6= 30
6. (4 sc, inc) x 6= 36
7. (5 sc, inc) x 6= 42
8. (6 sc, inc) x 6= 48
9. (7 sc, inc) x 6= 54
10. (8 sc, inc) x 6= 60
11-18. sc in each st around
19. 18 sc, 2 sl, 3 hdc, 4 dc, 3 hdc, 2 sl, 3 hdc, 4 dc, 3 hdc, 2 sl, 10 sc
F/O and leave a tail
Ears(Make 2 in Color A, 2 in Color B):
Starting with Color B:
1. Make 6 sc into a magic ring= 6
2. Increase in each st around= 12
3. (sc, inc) x 6= 18
4. (2 sc, inc) x 6= 24
Do not F/O the Color A ears! Place the back sides of Color A and Color B ears together.
You will be working around the ears to connect them together:
5. (3 sc, inc) x 6= 30
F/O and leave a long tail for sewing
Sweet Oddity Art 7
Arms(Make 2):
Starting with Color B:
1. Make 6 sc into a magic ring= 6
2. Increase in each st around= 12
3. (3 sc, inc) x 3= 15
4. sc in each st around
5. 3 dc cluster, ch 1, 14 sc= 15
6. (Do not work on the ch 1 from the previous round) (3 sc, dec) x 3= 12
7. (2 sc, dec) x 3= 9
Start stuffing the arms
Change to Color A:
No longer stuff the arms
8-19. sc in each st around
Fold the arms in half and sc the opening closed. F/O and leave a long tail for sewing
Sweet Oddity Art 8
Tail:
Starting with Color B:
1. Make 4 sc into a magic ring= 4
2. Increase in each st around= 8
3-5. sc in each st around
Change to Color A:
I did not stuff my tail, I used a pipe cleaner to stuff it instead
6-29. sc in each st around
If you are using a pipe cleaner, fold the pipe cleaner in half and twist it together. Insert it into
the tail. Fold the tail in half and sc the opening closed. F/O and leave a long tail for sewing
Sweet Oddity Art 9
Surfboard:
Starting with Color A:
1. Make 4 sc into a magic ring= 4
2-4. sc in each st around
Change to Color D:
5. Increase in each st around= 8
6. (sc, inc) x 4= 12
7. (2 sc, inc) x 4= 16
8. sc in each st around
9. (3 sc, inc) x 4= 20
Do not stuff the surfboard
10-44. sc in each st around
45. (3 sc, dec) x 4= 16
46. sc in each st around
47. (2 sc, dec) x 4= 12
Change to Color A:
48. Dec x 6= 6
F/O and sew the hole closed
Sweet Oddity Art 10
Assembly
Head and Body:
1. Put the cap around the head. Your cap will cover half of the open hole on the bottom
of the head.
2. Sew the head and body together. You may need to add more stuffing while you sew.
Sweet Oddity Art 11
Sweet Oddity Art 12
Arms:
1. Pin the arms onto the side of the body approximately between rounds 22 and 23.
2. Sew the arms onto the body.
Sweet Oddity Art 13
Ears:
1. Pin the ears onto the side of the cap. Approximately between rounds 13 and 14.
2. Sew the ears onto the head.
Sweet Oddity Art 14
Tail:
1. Pin the tail right above your waistband on the body.
2. Sew the tail onto the back of the body.
Sweet Oddity Art 15
Embellishments:
1. Embroider a smile on the side of the face.
2. Add some blush to the cheeks and inside the ears if you want.
Sweet Oddity Art 16
Necklace:
1. If you want, thread a strand of thread through a button and tie it around the neck.
Hair on top of head:
1. Attach brown yarn to the top of the head with a sl st. Ch 6, sl st in the 2nd ch from
hook and across. Sl st into the head. Repeat on top of the head 3 more times.
Weave in the tail ends.
Sweet Oddity Art 17
You now have your finished monkey! Thank you for your purchase! If you have any questions or
concerns please email me at sweetoddityart@gmail.com or etsy convo me. I will get back to
you asap. Please share your finished monkey with me as often as you want! I love seeing them!
Sweet Oddity Art 18
Helpful Tips:
Exact colors and brands of yarn used:
1. Brown: Red Heart Café Latte
2. Cream: Red Heart Aran
3. Variegated: Yes Sewing Blue
4. Yellow: Red Heart Daffodil
5. Blue: Red Heart Peacock
You can use different eye and nose sizes. You might have to adjust the placements if you
change the sizes.
You can use different hook sizes and weights of yarn. It will just change the size of your monkey
and you might need to adjust eye and nose placement.
How you stuff matters! The type of stuffing you use, how you stuff, all this matters on how your
monkey turns out. I prefer Polyfil stuffing but you can use other types.
