Using yellow yarn.
rnd 1 6 mr (6)
rnd 2 6 inc (12)
rnd 3 (1 sc, 1 inc) x 6 (18)
rnd 4 (5 sc, 1 inc) x 3 (21)
rnd 5 (6 sc, 1 inc) x 3 (24)
rnd 6-9 24 sc (24) (4 rounds)
rnd 10 (7 sc, 1 inc) x 3 (27)
rnd 11 (8 sc, 1 inc) x 3 (30)
rnd 12 (4 sc, 1 inc) x 6 (36)
rnd 13-16 36 sc (36) (4 rounds)
rnd 17 (4 sc, 1 dec) x 6 (30)
rnd 18 (3 sc, 1 dec) x 6 (24)
Add stuffing the body, adding more as you go along.
rnd 19 (2 sc, 1 dec) x 6 (18)
rnd 20 (1 sc, 1 dec) x 6 (12)
rnd 21 6 dec (6)
Cut the yarn and use the yarn tail to close the remaining stitches.
WING (MAKE 2)
Using yellow yarn. ch 4, starting in the 2nd chain from the hook and working on
both sides of the chain.
2 sc, 3 in same stitch,
row 1 (7)
2 sc, ch 1, turn
row 2 3 sc, 1 inc, 3 sc (8)
Cut the yarn and fasten off, leaving a long tail for sewing.
BEAK (MAKE 1)
Using orange yarn.
rnd 1 4 mr (4)
rnd 2 (1 sc, 1 inc) x 2 (6)
Cut the yarn and fasten off, leaving a long tail for sewing.
