Ootori-Sama;https://www.lovecrafts.com/en-gb/p/ootori-sama-ghibli-crochet-pattern-by-knitknot2know;;"Ootori-Sama
I've always wanted a bunch of Ootori-sama dolls ever since I saw them in my all time favorite
movie “Spirited Away”, so I thought, why not make it myself? And thus this pattern was born.
Please tag me @KnitKnot2Know if you upload your work on instagram, I would love to see!
THIS PATTERN IS FOR PERSONAL USE ONLY, DO NOT COPY, REPRODUCE, MODIFY,
PUBLISH, OR SHARE THIS DOCUMENT. YOU MAY SELL THE PHYSICAL ITEM BUT
PLEASE CREDIT ME (@KnitKnot2Know) AS THE DESIGNER.
@KnitKnot2Know 1
Materials
- Velvet Yarn (I use Mini Aster 100% polyester size 3) in yellow (body), green or white (leaf
or towel), orange (for beak) (1 ball of each yarn (184m) is enough to make both sizes)
- Crochet size 3mm
- Felt (for eyes)
- Stuffing materials
- Tapestry needle
- Scissor
- Sewing pin
- Stitch marker (optional)
Abbreviation
- Ch — Chain
- Mr — Magic ring
- Sc — Single crochet
- Hdc — Half double crochet
- Dc — Double crochet
- Inc — Increase
- Dec — Decrease
- Sl st — Slip Stitch
- St — Stitch
- FLO — Front Loop Only
- BLO — Back Loop Only
- (…) x n — repeat sequence in brackets n times
★The finished toy using a 3mm crochet hook is 12 cm for normal size without hat/ 14 cm with
hat, and 9 cm for mini size without towel/ 10cm with a towel.
