Little owl amigurumi;https://www.lovecrafts.com/en-gb/p/owl-amigurumi-crochet-pattern-by-pletionica;"Abbreviations:
ch - chain
sc - single crochet
Inc = Increase 2 sc into next stitch
st – stitch
Rnd – round
NOTE: -This pattern works in continuous rounds (instead of joined rounds).
-Use a stitch marker (or a piece of the other colors yarn) to mark the beginning of the row
(round).
Starting with turquoise color yarn, using a Single crochet stitch:
Make magic ring
Round 1: 6 single crochet (SC) in a magic circle (6 total)
Round 2: 2 SC in each stitch, (12 SC total)
Round 3: (1 SC, 2 SC in next st) Repeat (18 total)
Round 4: (2 SC, 2 SC in next st) Repeat (24 total)
Round 5: (3 SC, 2 SC in next st) Repeat (30 total)
Round 6 - 20: single crochet all around (30 total)
Stuff with Fiberfill stuffing
Round 21: connect the front and back of the owl with a hook (make 15 single crochet)
EYES:
-use white yarn
Round 1: 6 single crochet (SC) in a magic circle (6 total)
Round 2: 2 SC in each stitch, (12 SC total)
-make 2 circles
-in the middle of the circles sew green plastic buttons
-sew eyes on the face
WINGS:
-start with turquoise color yarn
Round 1: 6 single crochet (SC) in a magic circle (6 total)
Round 2: 2 SC in each stitch, (12 SC total)
change color to blue
Round 3: (1 SC, 2 SC in next st) Repeat (18 total)
Round 4: (2 SC, 2 SC in next st) Repeat (24 total)
-sew wings on both sides of the owl
-decorate front part of the owl with colorful beads
-sew beads with needle
Owl toy – finished size 10 cm (4 inches)
ENJOY THE PATTERN :-))
Please remember that safety eyes and tiny parts are not suitable for small
children. When making toys for younger kids, it is best to embroider on the
eyes.
