Knitting pattern for OWL;https://www.lovecrafts.com/en-gb/p/owl-knitting-pattern-knitting-pattern-by-worldcountrytoys;"Abbreviations
st, sts- stitch, stitches
R-round
k-knit
k2tog-knit two stitches together
p-purl
*-repeat
In this pattern we use US terminology.
BODY
Cast on 48 stitches.
R1-36: k48
R37:(k14, k2tog)*=45sts
R38:(k13, k2tog)*=42sts
R39-59: k42
R60:(k1, k2tog)*=28sts
R61:(k2tog)*=14sts
R62:(k2tog)*=7sts
R63:(k2tog)*k1=4sts
Bind off 4 stitches.
COWL
Cast on 90 stitches, knit in rounds, 6 rounds in total - purl all stitches.
SOCKS
Cast on 14 stitches.
R1-16: k14
R17:(k2tog, k3, k2tog)*=10sts
R18:(k2tog, k1, k2tog)*=6sts
R19р:(k3tog)*=2sts
Bind off 2 stitches.
MITTENS
Cast on 14 stitches.
R1-7: k14
R8: slip 3 stitches (for thumb) onto an additional knitting needle, cast on 3 stitches with the main knitting needle,
k11=14sts
R9-11: k14
R12:(k2tog, k3, k2tog)*=10sts
R13:(k2tog, k1, k2tog)*=6sts
R14:(k3tog)*=2sts
Bind off 2 stitches.
Thumb knitting.
Knit 3 stitches from the additional knitting needle, pick up 3 stitches across another edge=6sts
Knit 5 rounds, knit 3 stitches together*=2sts
Bind off 2 stitches.
OWL DETAILS
The owl is finished! Don’t forget to kiss her and wish her a Happy
Birthday!
