Bear peeking out of a sunflower snuggle buddy - Peek-A-Boo-Bear;https://www.lovecrafts.com/en-gb/p/peek-a-boo-bear-crochet-pattern-by-lisa-kingsley;;"Bear peeking out of a sunflower snuggle buddy - Peek-A-Boo-Bear
Peek-A-Boo-Bear measure 11' inches tall - not including the ears - and is 13 inches
round
Supplies needed:
Tweed and stripes: rainforest (40 grams)
Vanna's choice: mustard (30 grams)
Red heart premier : mocha (40 grams)
Red heart super saver : buff (small amount)
15 mm triangular safety nose
12 mm safety eyes (1 pair black)
Polyester stuffing
4 mm hook (bear)
5 mm hook (pillow)
Tapestry needle
Stitch marker
White felt - optional
Stitches used:
Sc - single crochet
Dc - double crochet
Tr - triple crochet
Hdc - half double crochet
Sl st - slip stitch
2sc - increase (2 sc in one st)
St - stitch
Sc2tog - decrease (turning 2 st into one st)
BLO - back loop only
MR - magic ring
Ch - chain
Pillow: using rainforest - working in the round - using 5 mm hook - starting at the top
1) MR - 6 sc in the loop
2) 2sc in each st (12 st)
3) *sc in the next st, 2sc in the next st* repeat *to* all around (18 st)
4) *sc in the next 2 st, 2sc in the next st* repeat *to* all around (24 st)
5) *sc in the next 3 st, 2sc in the next st* repeat *to* all around (30 st)
6) *sc in the next 4 st, 2sc in the next st* repeat *to* all around (36 st)
7) sc in the back loop only in each st around (36 st)
8 to 29) sc in each st around (36 st)
Start stuffing
30) sc in the back loop only (36 st)
31) *sc in the next 4 st, sc2tog* repeat *to* all around (30 st)
32) *sc in the next 3 st, sc2tog* repeat *to* all around (24 st)
33) *sc in the next 2 st, sc2tog* repeat *to* all around (18 st)
34) *sc in the next st, sc2tog* repeat *to* all around (12 st) finish stuffing the pillow
firmly
35) sc2tog all around (6 st)
Fasten off , sew the hole closed and weave in end
Flip pillow over and start working in the unworked front loops with Vanna's choice -
mustard - making sure the top of the pillow is facing you
1) join with a sl st to one of the unworked petal at the top of the pillow and sc in each st
around , sc in the same st as the sl st , join with a sl st to the first sc.
Start flower petals:
*Ch2, dc, tr all in the same st, ch3, tr, dc, hdc all in the next st, sl st in the next st*
repeat all around , ending with a sl st in the beginning ch2 stitch (total of 12 petals)
This is what the flower petals should look like when completed:
Bear head: using mocha yarn and a 4 mm hook
1) MR - 6 sc in the loop (6 st)
2) 2sc in each stitch (12 st)
3) *sc in the next st, 2sc in the next st* repeat *to* all around (18 st)
4) *sc in the next 2 st, 2sc in the next st* repeat *to* all around (24 st)
5) *sc in the next 3 st, 2sc in the next st* repeat *to* all around (30 st)
6) *sc in the next4 st, 2 sc in the next st* repeat *to* all around (36 st)
7) sc in each st around (36 st)
8) *sc in the next 5 st, 2sc in the next st* repeat *to* all around (42 st)
9 to 13) sc in each st around (42 st)
14) *sc in the next 5 st, sc2tog* repeat *to* all around (36 st)
15) sc in each st around (36 st)
16) *sc in the next 4 st, sc2tog* repeat *to* all around (30 st)
17 + 18) sc in each st around (30 st) now would be a good time to attach the safety
eyes between rows 10 and 11 leaving 4 stitches between them. If you are using the felt
circles , cut two small circles, just a little bit bigger than the eyes. Cut slits in the felt and
insert the eyes through them and the insert into the head. Start stuffing head firmly
19) *sc in the next 3 st, sc2tog* repeat *to* all around (24 st)
20) sc in the next 2 st, sc2tog* repeat *to* all around (18 st)
Fasten off leaving a long tail to sew to the top of the pillow (don't worry about the hole
that is left behind) don't sew it on yet, wait until you have all of the parts sewn on
Muzzle - beige yarn - 4 mm hook - working in the round
1) MR - 6 sc in the loop
2) 2sc in each st (12 st)
3) *sc in the next st, 2sc in the next st* repeat *to* all around (18 st)
4) *2sc in the next 3 st, sc in the next 6 st* repeat *to* one more time (24 st)
Fasten off leaving a long length to sew to the face , attach safety nose between rows 3
and 4. Using the mocha yarn stitch the mouth and the line between the nose and
mouth. Sew the muzzle just below the eyes. Weave in your ends
Close up view of the face, so you can see the placement of the muzzle and the mouth:
Ears - make 2 - mocha yarn - working in the round - 4 mm hook
1) MR - 6 sc in the loop
2) 2sc in each st (12 st)
3) *sc in the next st, 2sc in the next st* repeat *to* all around (18 st)
4 to 6) sc in each st around (18 st)
Fasten off
Flatten and sew to the top of the head between rows 5 and 12, leaving 7 stitches
between them
Paws - make 2 - mocha yarn - working in the round - 4 mm hook
1) MR - 6 sc in the loop
2) 2sc in each st (12 st)
3) *sc in the next st, 2sc in the next st* repeat *to* all around (18 st)
4 to 7) sc in each st around (18 st)
8) *sc in the next st, sc2tog* repeat *to* all around (12 st)
9) sc2tog all around (6 st)
Fasten off leaving a long length to sew to the top of the pillow
Using beige yarn stitch 3 little lines on the paws, between rows 3 and 4 leaving 2
stitches between the lines , (once the paws are sewn on) .
*sew the head onto the top of the pillow, right in the centre using the yarn you left earlier
(see picture below)
*sew the paws to the top of the pillow between the head and the petals (see picture
below)
*now it is time to sculpt the eyes: thread your tapestry needle with mocha yarn, insert
your needle just below the right eye , going through to just below the left eye (see
picture below) , pull yarn through (not all of the way) then re insert your needle a couple
of stitches above and going through to the other eye: (see picture below), work your
yarn through, then reinsert your needle through the same stitch as you started with ,
pull the two ends of yarn tightly,(see picture below) you should see the muzzle pop out
and the eyes come closer together. Once you are happy with the look, reinsert the
needle through to the other eye making sure to come out of another stitch , tie the ends
together and hides your ends inside the bears head.
First needle pass:
Second needle pass:
Notice the two ends of yarn on either side of the muzzle? Pull those two ends tightly:
Top view of the bears head and paws, so you can see the placement once they are
sewn on:
Side view, re: placement of head and paws:
Tada, now your little snuggle buddy should be all done. I hope you enjoyed making him
and that the recipient will love him for years to come :)
