Penguin";"Pattern
Eye Pads
E/9 - 3.5 mm Hook
White (Red Heart) 8 yds
Make 2
Working in rounds
1. Ch 2, 8sc into 2nd ch from hook (8)
2. Inc around (16)
3. (Sc, inc) around (24)
* Invisible Finish for Open Pieces
-Refer to the instructions for the invisible finish for open pieces.
Tummy Pad
E/9 - 3.5 mm Hook
White (Red Heart) 4 yds
Working in rows
1. Ch 5, sc into 2nd ch from hook, sc in next 3 (4)
2. Ch 1, turn, sc across (4)
3. Ch 1, turn, inc, sc in next 2, inc (6)
4 - 12. Ch 1, turn, sc across (6)
*Start working down the side edge
- Place 10sc along side edge
- Place 4sc along starting edge
- Place 10sc along other side edge
- Place 6sc across the last row
* Invisible Finish for Open Pieces
-Refer to the instructions for the invisible finish for open pieces.
Beak
E/9 - 3.5 mm Hook
Carrot (Red Heart) 2 yds
Working in rounds
1. Ch 3, sc into 2nd ch from hook, 3sc in last ch
On other side of starting chain: sc in first ch, 3sc in last ch (8)
2 - 3. Sc around (8)
* Finish off and leave a long tail
Feet
E/9 - 3.5 mm Hook
Carrot (Red Heart) 6 yds
Make 2
Working in rows
1. Ch 4, sc into 2nd ch from hook, sc in next 2 (3)
2. Ch 1, turn, sc across (3)
-Work round 3 to change from rows to rounds by single crocheting first through the front
loops and then through the back loops on the other side in a round.
Working in rounds
3. Sc around (6)
4 - 5. Sc around (6)
6. Inc around (12)
7. Sc around (12)
* Invisible Finish for Closed Pieces
-Refer to the instructions for the invisible finish for closed pieces.
Wings
E/9 - 3.5 mm Hook
Black (Red Heart) 33 yds
Make 2
Working in rounds
1. Ch 2, 6sc into 2nd ch from hook (6)
2. Inc around (12)
3. (Sc, inc) around (18)
4. Sc, inc, (sc in next 2, inc) 5 times, sc (24)
5 - 10. Sc around (24)
11. Sc, dec, (sc in next 2, dec) 5 times, sc (18)
12 - 16. Sc around (18)
17. (Sc, dec) around (12)
18 - 19. Sc around (12)
* Invisible Finish for Closed Pieces
-Refer to the instructions for the invisible finish for closed pieces.
-Smush the wings flat
Scarf
E/9 - 3.5 mm Hook
Blue Multi (Mainstays) 16 yds
Working in rows
1. Ch 3, sc in 2nd ch from hook, sc (2)
2 - 75. Sc across (2)
*Start working down the side edge
- Place 73sc along side edge
- Place 2sc along starting edge
- Place 73sc along other side edge
- Place 2sc across the last row
* Invisible Finish for Open Pieces
-Refer to the instructions for the invisible finish for open pieces.
Hat
E/9 - 3.5 mm Hook
Blue Multi (Mainstays) 20 yds
Working in rounds
1. Ch 2, 6sc into 2nd ch from hook (6)
2. Inc around (12)
3. (Sc, inc) around (18)
4. Inc around (36)
5 - 8. Sc around (36)
9. (Sc in next 5, inc) around (42)
10 - 11. Sc around (42)
12. Dc around (42)
13. (FPSC, BPSC) around (42) (instructions for both of these stitches are at the beginning of
this pattern)
* Invisible Finish for Open Pieces
-Refer to the instructions for the invisible finish for open pieces.
- Hot glue the white pom pom onto the hat in the center on the top.
Head and Body
E/9 - 3.5 mm Hook
Black (Red Heart) 40 yds
Working in rounds
1. Magic circle, 6sc into circle (6)
2. Inc around (12)
3. (Sc, inc) around (18)
4. Sc, inc, (sc in next 2, inc) 5 times, sc (24)
5. (Sc in next 3, inc) around (30)
6. Sc in next 2, inc, (sc in next 4, inc) 5 times, sc in next 2 (36)
7 - 12. Sc around (36)
13. Sc in next 2, dec, (sc in next 4, dec) 5 times, sc in next 2 (30)
*Attach eyes to eye pads, between round 1 and round 2. Do NOT put backs on yet.
*Attach eye pads on the opposite side of the head from the rounds beginning/end
stitches. Eye studs will go between the 9th and 10th round of the head, and will have 5
stitches between them.
14. (Sc in next 3, dec) around (24)
* At this point, I like to sew the eye pads down to the head and attach the beak. You can
wait until later if you prefer, but I find it easier to do now. Thread a dull yarn needle with
white yarn and weave back and forth, through the eye pad and head, around the posts of
the outside stitches of the eye pads. The bottom of the eye pads should run just above
round 14. The beak is then connected just below the eyes, centered.
15. Sc, dec, (sc in next 2, dec) 5 times, sc (18)
* Stuff the head firmly
16. (Sc, dec) around (12)
17. (sc, inc) around (18)
18. Inc around (36)
19. (Sc in next 5, inc) around (42)
20 - 21. Sc around (42)
22. (Sc in next 5, dec) around (36)
23 - 24. Sc around (36)
25. Sc in next 2, dec, (sc in next 4, dec) 5 times, sc in next 2 (30)
26 - 30. Sc around (30)
31. (Sc in next 3, dec) around (24)
32 - 35. Sc around (24)
* Now, we can attach the tummy pad. Again, I find it easier to do now, but you can wait
until later if you prefer. Center the pad to the head. Attach the tummy pad in the same
manner as the eye pads, weaving back and forth around the posts of the last round on
the tummy pad and into the body. The bottom of the tummy pad should be connected
just above round 35.
* Start stuffing the neck and body firmly
36. (Sc in next 4, dec) around (20)
* In round 37, there will be 8 stitches skipped to form the tail. I mark the first and last
stitch of these 8 stitches to find them easily later.
Note: The tail should be centered on his rear end. You may have
to offset where you skip your 8 stitches to ensure the tail is in the
correct spot. Whether you back up your first stitch or move it
forward for the round, skip 8 stitches for the tail.
37. Sk 8, sc in the next 12 (12)
* Stuff firmly before closing
* Invisible Finish for Closed Pieces
-Refer to the instructions for the invisible finish for closed pieces.
Now, to finish the tail. Looking at the bottom of the penguin, with the opening for the tail
at the bottom (like the picture above), the yarn will be connected in the left stitch marker.
Create a slip knot on your hook and begin with that stitch.
1 - 3. Sc around (8)
* Finish stuffing the penguin firmly
* Invisible Finish for Closed Pieces
DO NOT CUT
-Refer to the instructions for the invisible finish for closed pieces.
THE YARN AT THE END OF THIS INVISIBLE FINISH!
-There will be a small hole between the tail and body. Use the yarn from the invisible
finish and insert it through the center of the invisible finish of the tail. Bring the yarn out
through a stitch just below that hole. Stitch the hole closed with a couple of stitches
around the hole.
*Note: If you have not sewn down eye pads, beak, or tummy pad,
do so now.
Assembly
Attaching Feet
- The flat part of the foot (where we had worked in rows) will be the part sewn to the
bottom of the body. The feet should be placed, centered, on the bottom of the penguin.
Make sure to check your placement by pinning the feet to the penguin first and looking at
the penguin straight on to ensure the feet look right.
- Sew the feet to the bottom of the penguin in a circular pattern.
Attaching Wings
- Only the top part of the wings will be sewn into the body. Pin the wings on first to ensure
you like the positioning. Tuck the top of the wing right up into the neck.
- Fold the wing evenly in half. At the crease is where to begin the attachment.
Make sure to only be going through the underside layer of the wing.
- Like the feet, sew in a circular pattern to connect the wings. Only sew through
the underside layer of the wing and into the body.
Attaching Scarf
- The scarf is wrapped around the penguins neck firmly, but loosely, OVER the top of
wings. The only parts of the scarf sewn into the penguin are the two ends.
- To connect the two ends, use a needle and Mainstays Blue Multi yarn and pass through
both ends of the scarf at the same time. Like the eye pads and tummy pad, go up and
around posts just below the outside stitches of the scarf. Pass the yarn back and forth
through the body, securing 4 or 5 stitches on each end of the scarf.
No assembly for the hat required. If you’d like, you can sew it to the head
through the rim of the hat or you can leave it detachable.
Congratulations!
