Crochet pattern;https://www.lovecrafts.com/en-gb/p/phone-holder-cushion-crochet-pattern-by-luna-crochet-designs;"Abbreviations:
st(s): stitch(es)
Level of difficulty Beginner* R: Round/Row
Crochet language: US Crochet terms
ch: chain
Gauge/tension is not important for this
pattern as long as your stitches are tight and sl. st.: slip stitch
without gaps.
beg: beginning
Finished cushion is approximately 15 X 20
cms. sc: single crochet
BLO: crochet into back loops only
FLO: crochet into front loops only
*__* repeat instructions from * to *
Cushion:
Start by creating a slip knot and chain 22.
Tip: Mark your first stitch with a stitch marker.
R 1: sc 2 into the second chain from the
hook, then sc one per chain for 19 times, sc
5 into the last chain.
Turn your work and sc to the opposite side
of the chain one sc per chain for 19 times, sc
3 into the final chain (48 sts).
R 2 - 5 (4 rounds): sc around (48 sts).
R 6: Right side facing you, fold your work in
half and sc through both sides for 15
stitches, stuff firmly and keep stuffing as
you go. Continue to sc throughout the
remaining 8 stitches (23 sts).
R 7 - 10 (4 rows): ch 1, turn work, sc 23 (23
sts).
R 11: ch 1, turn work, FLO sc 22, 2 FLO sc
into the final stitch, turn to work into the
back loops, BLO sc 22, 2 BLO sc into the final
stitch (48 sts).
R 12 onwards: working in a continuous
circle sc all around until it measures about
15 cm in height. You do not need to keep
track of the first stitch of the round.
Fold sideways in half (see photo), sl. st.
through both sides for 15 sts, stuff (do not
overstuff the pillow part) then finish sl. st.
remainder of the 8 sts (23 sts).
Sew in the ends.
