Mary’s Amiland 4
Pine Cone Elf
Assembling Pine Cone Elf
The eyes are positioned between rounds 8 and 9 from the top of the head, five
stitches apart.
Embroider the eyes with black embroidery floss, I made two French knots.
Alternatively, you can make a straigth line going over it a few times.
5 sts
Sew the star to the tip of the hat
preferably between two points of the star
and the tip of the hat.
Position the hat on the head, ensuring the star faces the
front with the hat bent on the side.
Sew in place.
Sew the ears to the head, two rounds below the hat,
three stitches away from the side of eyes.
Now prepare the pine cone, if necessary take out the ends on the
top so that the head fits well upon it.
Insert the head on the pine cone and position it so that the pine
cone stays upward independently.
Next glue the head on the top of the pine cone and the base to the bottom, leave it there until it is dry.
Finally wrap the scarf around the neck.
Congratulations, you have completed Pine Cone Elf!
