Rnd 13: (11sc, inc) x6 78sts
Rnd 14: (12sc, inc) x6 84sts
Rnd 15: 84sc into back of the loop only 84sts
How to crochet through the back of the loop
pg. 3
Pumpkin Pie | ©Created by Craftychick 2024
Draw around the base of your Pie onto your felt. Cut it out to be inserted into
your pie later, this will help keep the bottom of your Base flat to help it sit
nicely. Check that it fits after a few more rows, you may need to trim it down a
little.
Once you are happy with how it fits you can leave it in the bottom as you work.
Rnd 16-22 84sc 84sts
To join the top and base together work as
follows, this part of the pattern creates the
pastry shell edge
Still Using Stone yarn.
Place the base and the top of your pie
together, make sure that your top is facing up
and that you are starting where you finished.
Working through both pieces continue as
follows. You will need to start stuffing your
pie once you are about ¾ of the way around,
continue to stuff as you go and finish
stuffing before your pie is closed.
pg. 4
Pumpkin Pie | ©Created by Craftychick 2024
Rnd 23: 1sc, (tr inc x2, 2sc) repeat bracket instructions until you get to
your last 3sts, tr inc x2, 1sc
Tie off to finish leaving enough yarn to tie in later.
Tie off any loose ends and your Pumpkin Pie is finished!
