Rancor Cat Toy;https://www.lovecrafts.com/en-gb/p/rancor-cat-toy-crochet-pattern-by-knot-important;Abbreviations: This;"pattern uses U.S. terminology.
​
SC-single crochet
DC-double crochet
SL- slip stitch
CH- chain
decr-decrease
incr-increase (two single crochets worked in same stitch)
MR-magic ring
The number of stitches in the row is in parenthesis at the end of each row.
Instructions in parenthesis are repeated the given number of times. For example (SC, inc)x2
would be the same as SC, incr, SC, incr.
This pattern is worked in continuous spirals. Do not join rows.
Body
Row 1: MR 5 (5)
Row 2: incr 5 (10)
Row 3: (SC, incr)X5 (15)
Row 4: (SC 4, incr)X3 (18)
Rows 5-12): SC 18 (18)
Row 13: (SC4, decr)X3 (15)
Stuff the body with Poly-fil. Add catnip if desired.
Row 14: (SC, decr)X5 (10)
Row 15: dec 5 (5) Finish off.
Head
Row 1: MR 5 (5) Leave a tail for sewing.
Row 2: incr 5 (10)
Row 3: (SC, incr)X5 (15)
Row 4: (SC 4, incr)X3 (18)
Row 5: SC 4, CH 10, skip 10, SC 4 (18 including chain)
The opening you just made in row 5 is the mouth.
Row 6: SC 4, SC 10 in the chain from row 5, SC 4 (18)
Row 7: (SC 4, decr)X3 (15)
Row 8: (SC, decr)X5 (10)
Row 9: decr 5 (5) Finish off.
Arms/claws (make 2)
(See process photos at the end of this pattern.)
Row 1: MR 8 (8) Leave a long tail for sewing later.
Row 2-9: SC 8 (8)
Row 10: (SC, CH 4, SC 3 in chain)X3, SC 2, SC, CH 4 SC 3 in chain SC 2 (8 not including
single crochets in the short chains that form the claws.)
Sew the opening shut.
Legs (make 2)
Row 1: MR 8 (8)
Row 2-7: SC 8 (8)
Leave a long tail for sewing.
Teeth
(See process photos at the end of this pattern.)
There will be several color changes. All slip stitches should be worked in the main color. All
other stitches should be worked in white.
Open the mouth so that it forms a 20-stitch “circle” (more like a football shape). Draw a loop of
the main color through the right corner of the mouth. This does not count as a stitch and should
not use up any of the 20 stitches.
SL 2, (SL, SC, CH 2, SC 1 in chain, SL) X2, SL 2 (You have now used up the bottom 10
stitches. You should have two teeth.)
SC, CH 2, SC 1 in chain, SL 2, SC, CH 2, SC 1 in chain, SL 3, SC, CH 2, SC 1 in chain SL 2
(You have now completed the teeth, a total of five. They are a bit crooked, but hey-- Jabba the
Hut wasn’t known for his great employee dental plan!)
Assembly
Attach legs on one end of the body using a yarn needle. Sew the head to the side of the body
(not on top) near the other end. The top end of the body will give the rancor a nice hunched
back. Sew the arms on either side of the body so that the claws point forward rather than
hanging by his sides.
Ridges
To make your rancor more reptilian, add some ridges. Force the hook through the very top of
the head and draw a loop of the main color through. You will be crocheting down the back of
the head, up and over the hump, and a little ways down the back. You will be forcing the hook
through the fabric of the doll for each stitch, so this part is a little tricky. All stitches will be
worked in the main color.
(SL, DC, SL)X7
Tail
Force the hook through the rancor’s derriere, draw a loop of the main color through, CH 6, SC 5
in chain. Finish off with a slip stitch at the base of the tail.
Weave in all loose ends. Attach safety eyes or embroider eyes in black. Behold your rancor!
Snap a photo for posterity, toss him to your cat, and let the battle begin!
Aww. He looks like he needs a hug. Maybe he’s too cute to give to the cat. Maybe you need to
make another one.
Process photos for claws
Taken after row 9. Row 10 is not yet started.
Taken after single crochet and chain 3 in row 10.
Taken after single crochet 3 in chain in row 10. This is the
first claw. The others are worked the same way. The next
stitch will be a normal single crochet in the main ring,
followed by a chain of four and then three single crochets in
the chain.
Process photos for teeth
After drawing the loop of main color through.
After three slip stitches and a color change.
After single crochet and chain two.
After one single crochet in chain and a color change.
This is the first tooth. The next stitch will be a slip
stitch.";Lovecrafts
Knitting pattern;https://www.lovecrafts.com/en-gb/p/raven-knitting-pattern-knitting-pattern-by-worldcountrytoys;"Abbreviations
st, sts - stitch, stitches
R - round
k - knit
p - purl
k2tog - knit two stitches together
*-repeat
In this pattern we use US terminology.
BODY
Cast on 48 stitches
R1-36: k48
R37:(k14, k2tog)*=45sts
R38:(k13, k2tog)*=42sts
R39-59: k42
R60:(k1, k2tog)*=28sts
R61:(k2tog)*=14sts
R62:(k2tog)*=7sts
R63:(k2tog)*k1=4sts
Bind off 4 stitches
BEAK
Cast on 18 stitches
R1-5: k18
R6: k2tog, k7, k2tog, k7=16sts
R7: k16
R8: k2tog, k6, k2tog, k6=14sts
R9: k14
R10: k2tog, k5, k2tog, k5=12sts
R11:(k2tog)*=6sts
R12:(k3tog)*=2sts
Bind off 2 stitches.
COWL
Cast on 65 stitches, knit in rounds, 22 rounds in total - k all stitches
SOCKS
Cast on 14 stitches.
R1-16: k14
R17:(k2tog, k3, k2tog)*=10sts
R18:(k2tog, k1, k2tog)*=6sts
R19:(k3tog)*=2sts
Bind off 2 stitches.
MITTENS
Cast on 14 stitches.
R1-7: k14
R8: slip 3 stitches (for the thumb) onto an additional knitting needle, cast on 3 stitches with the main knitting
needle, k11=14sts
R9-11: k14
R12:(k2tog, k3, k2tog)*=10sts
R13:(k2tog, k1, k2tog)*=6sts
R14:(k3tog)*=2sts
Bind off 2 stitches.
Thumb knitting.
Knit 3 stitches from the additional knitting needle, pick up 3 stitches across another edge=6sts
Knit 5 rounds, knit 3 stitches together*=2sts
Bind off 2 stitches.
The little white crow is finished! Don't forget to kiss him on the
nose and wish him a Happy Birthday!
