Embroider eyes and mouth:
Using black thread, embroider eyes. Bottom is at round 6 and top is at round 4.
(pic1) Sew from top to bottom hole 4 times. There are 3 holes between the
eyes. Repeat on each side of octopus. For eyelashes, separate yarn into 4
threads. Using 1 thread, embroider eyelashes. (pic2)
Add white to eyes. Fasten off and hide all tails.
4
©Crossmanknits 2021. A pattern by Crossmanknits / Gabriella Crossman. For personal use only. You may not share or publish this pattern or any part of it without the consent of the author.
Instagram: @crossmanknits
e-mail: crossmanknits@gmail.com
ravelry: crossmanknits
etsy: crossmanknits
Baby fish:
Start with the head using color blue (pink)
Round 1 4 sc into MR (4sts)
Round 2 inc (8sts)
Round 3-4 sc
Round 5 *dec 2 sc* (6sts)
Continue with the tail using color pink (blue)
Flatten piece. Now you have 6 sts. (3 in the front and 3 in the back) You will
crochet the front and back together in a row, totaling 3 holes.
Row 1 3 dc into first hole, sl into second hole, 3 dc into third hole.
Sl into the third hole. (8sts)
Embroider eyes on each side using black yarn. Fasten off and hide all tails.
Well done! Please tag your photos with @crossmanknits
Abbreviations:
sc -single crochet inc - increase (2sc into next st)
dec -decrease (sc two together) MR - magic ring
dc -double crochet st(s) – stitch(es)
tr -treble crochet ** - repeat to end of round
flo -front loop only sl - slip
