Reversible;https://www.lovecrafts.com/en-gb/p/reversible-octopus-amigurumi-crochet-pattern-by-dalai-lana;Abbreviations;"Pattern notes: Magic ring
Rnd Round/s
Everything is worked in continuous rounds.
ch Chain
At the end of every round inside the ( ) is the st Stitch
total stitches of the row.
sc Single crochet
inc Increase
You’ll need less than 40 grams. of cotton yarn
dec Decrease
per color.
Finished toy measures approximately 10 cm.
tall, depending on the yarn tension, brand and
crochet hook size.
Heads
Make two
Rnd1: In a magic ring, sc 6 (6)
Rnd2: inc in each st around (12)
Rnd3: (sc, inc) 6 times (18)
Rnd4: (sc 2, inc) 6 times (24)
Rnd5: (sc 3, inc) 6 times (30)
Rnd6: (sc 4, inc) 6 times (36)
Rnd7: (sc 5, inc) 6 times (42)
Rnd8: (sc 6, inc) 6 times (48)
Rnd9 - 16: sc in each st around (48)
Lightly stuff one of the heads, do not
fasten off.
Insert the safety eyes between rounds
11 - 12 with an interspace
of 7 stitches.
Tentacles
Make eight
Rnd1: In a magic ring, sc 6 (6)
Rnd2: Inc 3 in one of color and inc 3 in the other
color (12)
Rnd3 - 9: sc in each st, 6 in each color like the
previous round.
Leave a long tail in two of them to sew to the heads.
Stuff all the tentacles.
Sew every tentacle with the head in the
color alike, 6 stitches of every
tentacle per side.
An original pattern by @dalailanacl
Pulpo
Materiales
Reversible
•
Hilo de algodón liso a elección en dos colores.
•
Aguja de crochet/ganchillo 2,75 - 3 mm.
