Ribbon Egg;https://www.lovecrafts.com/en-gb/p/ribbon-egg-crochet-pattern-by-betsymakes;"Abbreviations:
Ch – chain, dc – double crochet, tr – treble crochet, sk st – skip stitch, ss – slip stitch
Inc: 2dc in same stitch.
Dec: Insert the hook under the front loop of the first double crochet stitch. Do not
yarn over. Insert the hook under the front loop of the second stitch and pick it up
onto the hook. Yarn over and draw through the first two loops. Yarn over and draw
through all loops.
©All text, illustration and images copyright betsymakes 2019 www.betsymakes.blogspot.co.uk
UK crochet terminology. All rounds worked in a spiral unless otherwise stated
Ch2
Rnd1: 6dc in 2nd ch from hook. (6)
Rnd2: inc x 6. (12)
Rnd3: (dc, inc) x 6. (18)
Rnd4: (2dc, inc) x 6. (24)
Rnd5: (3dc, inc) x 6. (30)
Rnd6: (4dc, inc) x 6. (36)
Rnd7-12: dc in each stitch. (36)
Rnd13: ch4, (sk st, 1tr, ch1) x 17. Sk st, ss into 3rd ch to close round.
Rnd14: ch1, dc in same stitch as ss, (1dc in ch space, 1dc in tr) x 17. (36)
Rnd15: (4dc, dec) x 6. (30)
Rnd16: dc in each st. (30) Place the polystyrene egg into your work and continue to crochet:
Rnd17: (3dc, dec) x 6. (24)
Rnd18: dc in each st. (24)
Rnd19: (2dc, dec) x 6. (18)
Rnd20: (1dc, dec) x 6. (12)
Rnd21: dc in each st. (12)
Rnd22: dec x 6. (6)
Fasten off and cut yarn. Thread the end into a darning needle and make a running st in last
round of dc and pull up to close gap. Weave in end.
Thread the darning needle with ribbon, starting at the front of the egg weave the ribbon in
and out of the ch spaces made on round 8. Tie the ribbon into a bow at the front of the egg
and cut ends of ribbon diagonally.
