Assembly Ringo Cat
Mark the center of the body with some pins to ensure
1 2
things are even and placed symmetrically.
Use pins to mark where the joints will be placed.
Position of the joints, i.e. points from where you will
join the limbs:
Arm: the body’s joint is placed between Rounds 3 and 4
from the neck of the cat, along the side of the body. The
stich on the outer side of the arm is placed between
3 4
Round 2 and 3 from the top (photos 2 and 3).
Leg: the body’s joint is placed between Rounds 3 and 4
from the Magic Ring on the bottom. The stich on the
outer side of the leg is placed between Round 2 and 3
from the top (photos 2 and 4).
To join Ringo’s limbs I have followed the thread jointing method that is explained hereafter.
Thread jointing method
1) Cut a long length of fishing line (or yarn), thread a
doubled up strand onto a yarn needle;
2) Push the needle through the body from side to side
where the limbs will be jointed, squashing the body so the
needle can go all the way through and leaving a long
thread end on the first side;
3) Make a small stitch at the outer side of the limb at the
point where the joint will be;
4) Run the needle back through the body close to the
starting end of the thread and make a small stitch at the
outer side of the second limb, at the same height as the
stitch on the first limb;
5) Repeat the process from 2) to 4) and pull tightly to
make firm joints. If you do not pull tightly enough, the
limbs will not stay in position;
6) The two thread ends should be close together. Pull
them both tightly and tie the two ends together securely.
Hide the knot between the body and limb;
7) Weave ends in.
Now pin the ears to the head, place them at round 5 from
the top center of the head. Check that both ears are at the
same distance from the eyes. When you are happy with
the position of the ears sew them in place.
