When making a toy such as this, it is not essential to work to
the exact tension. If your tension is tight, with more stitches
and rows than stated, your toy will be smaller. If your tension
is loose, with less stitches and rows than stated, your toy
will be larger. However, if your tension is too loose, the toy
filling will show through the crochet and spoil the look of the
finished item.
