Sweet Oddity Art;https://www.lovecrafts.com/en-gb/p/sea-turtle-crochet-pattern-by-carolyne-brodie;"Abbreviations:
mr= magic ring- crochet single crochet stitches in to the
adjustable loop BLO= back loops only
ch= chain stitch F/O= Fasten off
sc= single crochet stitch hdc= half double crochet
sl= slip stitch FLO= front loops only
dc= double crochet stitch inc3= 3 sc in the same stitch
inc= increase- make two single crochet stitches in the same stitch
dec=decrease- crochet two stitches together using the decrease method
(4 sc, inc) x 6= repeat the pattern between parentheses 6 times
Notes:
• Do not join rounds unless stated, work in a continuous spiral
• Use a stitch marker to mark the beginning of each round
• All stitches are worked in both loops unless stated otherwise in the pattern
Sweet Oddity Art 2
Head and Body:
Crocheted from top of head to bottom
With Color A:
1. Make 6 sc into a magic ring= 6
2. Increase in each st around= 12
3. (sc, inc) x 6= 18
4. (2 sc, inc) x 6= 24
5. (3 sc, inc) x 6= 30
6. (4 sc, inc) x 6= 36
7. (5 sc, inc) x 6= 42
8. (6 sc, inc) x 6= 48
9-11. sc in each st around
12. (7 sc, inc) x 6= 54
13-16. sc in each st around
17. (Mark the last inc of the first set of increases and the first inc of the 2nd set of increases with
stitch markers)
20 sc, inc x 6, 10 sc, inc x 6, 12 sc= 66
Place eyes between rounds 14 and 15, leaving 14 holes between them. Place the first eye
before the first stitch marker. Place your 2nd eye after the 2nd stitch marker. If you want the
sunken eye look, do not place the backs of the eyes on until round 23.
TIP! You may have to adjust the eye placement depending on yarn and hook size you use.
Sweet Oddity Art 3
18-19. sc in each st around
20. 24 sc, (dec, 2 sc) x 6, 18 sc= 60
21. (3 sc, dec) x 12= 48
22. (6 sc, dec) x 6= 42
23. (5 sc, dec) x 6= 36
Now for the eyes. Stuff the head well. Cut a long piece of yarn and remove the eyes. Place the
needle in the hole where the first eye was and insert the needle into a hole next to the eye
hole. Go back and forth between each eye hole repeating the process from the first eye. Pull
slightly on the yarn after going through each hole. Do this about 3 times on each side until you
reach the look you want. Follow the pictures on page 5 for help. There is also a youtube video I
have for extra help on this process.
https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9XoBnTY6k70&t=55s
To place the backs of the eyes you will need to remove most of the stuffing to place the
washers on the eyes then re stuff it.
24. (4 sc, dec) x 6= 30
25. (3 sc, dec) x 6= 24
26-29. sc in each st around
30. (3 sc, inc) x 6= 30
31. sc in each st around
32. (4 sc, inc) x 6= 36
33-34. sc in each st around
Stuff the body as you work
35. (5 sc, inc) x 6= 42
36-37. sc in each st around
38. (6 sc, inc) x 6= 48
39-40. sc in each st around
41. (7 sc, inc) x 6= 54
42. sc in each st around
Sweet Oddity Art 4
Sweet Oddity Art 5
Head and Body Contiuned:
43. (8 sc, inc) x 6= 60
44-49. sc in each st around
50. (8 sc, dec) x 6= 54
51. (7 sc, dec) x 6= 48
52. (6 sc, dec) x 6= 42
53. (5 sc, dec) x 6= 36
54. (4 sc, dec) x 6= 30
55. (3 sc, dec) x 6= 24
56. (2 sc, dec) x 6= 18
57. (sc, dec) x 6= 12
58. dec x 6= 6
F/O and sew the hole closed
Fins(Make 4):
With Color A:
1. Make 6 sc into a magic ring= 6
2. Increase in each st around= 12
3. (sc, inc) x 6= 18
4. (2 sc, inc) x 6= 24
5. (3 sc, inc) x 6= 30
