Sweet Oddity Art 8
Assembly
Head and Body:
1. Thread your needle with a strand of white yarn. Insert the needle into a hole in
between the eyes. Bring the needle to a lower corner of the eye. Wrap the needle
around the outside of the eye and insert the needle into a corner. Pull on the yarn a
little tightly to give a highlighted look.
2. If you want to give your turtle a little mouth. Place a pin in between the eyes
approximately in between rounds 22 and 23. Thread your needle with a long strand of
mint yarn. Insert the needle into a hole on the bottom of the head. Bring the needle up
to a hole on the left of the pinned spot. Bring the needle over to a hole on the right side
of the pinned spot. Bring the needle up to a hole in between the eyes approximately in
between rounds 16 and 17. Pull tightly. Insert the needle into a hole next to the last
one. Bring the needle down to the spots you started with. You are needle sculpting the
mouth if you want one. Repeat this process a few times until you reach the desired look
you want.
3. Pin the eyelids over the eyes. Sew the eyelids onto the head.
Sweet Oddity Art 9
Sweet Oddity Art 10
Sweet Oddity Art 11
Sweet Oddity Art 12
Belly:
1. Pin the belly onto the front of the body.
2. Sew the belly onto the body.
Nostrils:
1. Mark 4 spots on the muzzle for the nostrils. Your pins will be one hole apart from each other.
The set of pins will be approximately 3 pins apart from each other.
2. Thread your needle with a long strand of teal yarn and embroider 2 nostrils. Weave in any
tail ends.
Sweet Oddity Art 13
Shell:
1. Place the shell onto the back of the body with pins. Do not overstuff the shell at this
point. Start sewing on the shell on blo round.
2. Once you get to the last few stitches, start stuffing the shell firmly. Finish sewing
closed.
Sweet Oddity Art 14
Front Fins:
1. Bring your yarn tail to the opposite side of the fin because you want the dc
part to be at the bottom of the fin.
2. Pin the fins onto the side of the body underneath the neck. There are no
certain round placements. I just place them in a forward angle where I think they
look best.
3. Sew them onto the body. You are only sewing the top corner area of the fin to
the body.
Sweet Oddity Art 15
Back Fins:
1. Bring your yarn tail to the opposite side of the fin. Same thing as for the front fins.
2. Pin the fins onto the bottom of the body.
3. Sew them onto the body. You are only sewing the top corner of the fins to the body.
Sweet Oddity Art 16
Tail:
1. Pin the tail onto the body under the shell.
2. Sew the tail onto the body.
Blush:
1. With some actual blush or pink crayon, add some blush to the cheeks.
You now have your finished sea turtle! Thank you for your purchase! If you have any questions
or concerns please email me at sweetoddityart@gmail.com or etsy convo me. I will get back to
you asap. Please share your finished sea turtle with me as often as you want! I love seeing
