Continued.....
Join HAZELNUT
Round 24: 60dc [60 sts].
Round 25: BLO (8dc, dc2tog) x 6 [54 sts].
Round 26: (7dc, dc2tog) x 6 [48 sts].
Round 27: (6dc, dc2tog) x 6 [42 sts].
Round 28: (5dc, dc2tog) x 6 [36 sts].
Round 29: (4dc, dc2tog) x 6 [30 sts].
Round 30: (3dc, dc2tog) x 6 [24 sts].
Round 31: (2dc, dc2tog) x 6 [18 sts].
Stuff firmly here with your fibre fill.
Round 32: (1dc, dc2tog) x 6 [12 sts].
Round 33: (dc2tog) x 6 [6 sts].
To finish: Cut yarn & weave in ends.
Assembly
Now we need to sew all the leaves onto our plant pot. I started with the 3 smallest leaves and sewed them
around the centre of the soil directly over rounds 1 & 2.
I then took the next 3 leaves and sewed them onto the plant pot just behind the smaller leaves but
covering the gaps between them. Then I did the same with the last 3 leaves so they were all evenly places
around and not directly behind one another.
Please see the picture below that may help you with placement.
