Sweet Oddity Art;https://www.lovecrafts.com/en-gb/p/small-dragon-crochet-pattern-by-carolyne-brodie;"Abbreviations:
mr= magic ring- crochet single crochet stitches in to the
adjustable loop BLO= back loops only
ch= chain stitch inc3= 3 sc in the same stitch
sc= single crochet stitch F/O= Fasten off
sl= slip stitch FLO= Front Loops Only
dc= double crochet stitch bob st= bobble stitch
inc= increase- make two single crochet stitches in the same stitch
dec=decrease- crochet two stitches together using the decrease method
(4 sc, inc) x 6= repeat the pattern between parentheses 6 times
Notes:
• Do not join rounds unless stated, work in a continuous spiral
• Use a stitch marker to mark the beginning of each round
• All stitches are worked in both loops unless stated otherwise in the pattern
Sweet Oddity Art 2
Head:
Crocheted from front of nose to back of head
Starting with Color B:
1. Make 6 sc into a magic ring= 6
2. Increase in each st around= 12
3. (sc, inc) x 6= 18
4. (2 sc, inc) x 6= 24
5. (3 sc, inc) x 6= 30
6. FLO 4 sc, bob st, 8 sc, bob st, 16 sc= 30
7-9. sc in each st around
Change to Color A:
10. sc in each st around
11. (4 sc, inc) x 6= 36
12. (5 sc, inc) x 6= 42
13. (6 sc, inc) x 6= 48
Place eyes between rows 12 and 13, leaving 10 holes between them.
14-19. sc in each st around
20. (7 sc, dec) x 6= 42
(6 sc,dec
21. sc in each st around
22. (5 sc, dec) x 6= 36
Start stuffing the head
23. (4 sc, dec) x 6= 30
24. (3 sc, dec) x 6= 24
25. (2 sc, dec) x 6= 18
26. (sc, dec) x 6= 12
27. dec x 6= 6
F/O and sew the hole closed
