Materials:
Kartopu cozy wool sport yarn
20 gm of white colour N: k010
80 gm of blue colour N: k1624
Gauge: inches
19.0 to 25.0 sts = 4
Hook : 6 mm (or in accordance with the yarn you use).
Tapestry needle
Scissor
(alternative yarn: red hear super saver #4
Hook size : 5.5mm)
TERMS USED:
Ch = chain
sc = single crochet.
sl st = slip stitch
st(s) = stitch (es)
F/O: fasten off
Finished Scarf size : 110×10 cm
Important notes:
** Work in rows, ch1 and turn at the end of every rows.
** Yarn suggestions: If you cannot find the same yarn, you can buy a different
brand of yarn. . Yarn size will depend on your hook size.
**This Scarf is really simple and you can make it any size you want
just note that:
the length of the beginning ch =the desired width of the Scarf
The number of the rows=the desired length of the Scarf
**the Scarf consists of 2 white parts and 1 blue part. blue part is 3
times the length of the white part,so in a 110 cm Scarf, the white part
is 22 cm made twice and the blue part is 66 cm.
The pattern :
With white and nako kartopu yarn
Ch 11
Row 1: in the 2nd ch from the hook, 1sc in all 10 chs. (10)ch1, turn.
From row 2 to row 20: 1sc in all 10 sts, ch1, turn. (10)
Change to blue colour
From row 21 to row 80: 1sc in all 10 sts,ch1and turn. (10)
Change colour to white.
From row 81 to row 100: 1 sc in all 10 st, ch1and turn. (10)
Slst, F/O. Sew the applique to the Scarf
Alternative yarn suggestions :
If you are Using red heart super saver #4 and 5.5 mm hook:
With white, ch17
Row 1: in the 2nd ch from the hook, 1 sc in all 16 chs. (16)
From row 2 to row 35:1sc in all 16 sts. (16)
Change colour to blue
From row 36 to row 141 :1sc in all 16 sts. (16)
Change colour to white
From row 141 to row 176 : 1sc in all 16sts. (16)
Slst,F/O
Congratulations now your sonic scarf is ready. Feel free to contact me if you
have any question regarding my pattern.
