Assembly
Head and Body:
1. Pin the head to the body for extra support. You may need to add more stuffing as you
sew.
2. Sew the head to the body.
Ears:
1. Pin the ears on top of the head. Approximately between rows 36 and 37.
2. Sew the ears onto the head.
Sweet Oddity Art 10
Arms:
1. Pin the arms to the side of the body in a forward facing angle, underneath the neck.
Since these are handmade there are no row placements I use. I just judge based on how
they look. If you are using the safety eyes as bolts, place them underneath the bolts and
sew into place.
2. Sew the arms onto the body
Legs:
1. Turn the body upside down with the nose facing away from you.
2. Pin the legs onto the bottom of the body approximately between rounds 5 and 6.
3. Sew the legs onto the body
Sweet Oddity Art 11
Tail:
1. Pin the tail onto the back of the body approximately between rounds 11 and 17.
2. Sew the tail onto the body.
Back:
1. Pin the square onto the back of the body.
2. Sew the square onto the back.
3. Pin the spots onto the square and sew them on.
4. Add some black stitches with embroidery thread around the edges of the square.
Sweet Oddity Art 12
Stitches and Face:
1. Embroider stitches on different parts of the arms, legs and body, random spots to
give the frankenweenie effect. You can even add a little black shadow on the stitches for
an extra frankenweenie look.
2. Embroider some eyebrows with a strand of black yarn, not embroidery thread.
