Sweet Oddity Art 19
Assembly
Head and Body:
1. Pin the white hair pieces onto the side of the head working in an “S” shape. Sew the
hair onto the sides of the head.
2. Pin the head to the body for extra support. You may need to add more stuffing before
you close the neck.
3. Sew the head to the body.
Sweet Oddity Art 20
Ears:
1. Pin the ears onto the side of the head. Try to pin them overlapping the gray and
black of the head.
2. Sew the ears into place.
Arms:
1. Pin the arms onto the front of the body.
2. Sew the arms underneath the bulge on the front of the body. Everything will be
slightly awkward to sew on but it just takes patience.
Sweet Oddity Art 21
Legs:
1. Turn the body upside down with the nose facing away from you.
2. Pin the legs underneath the body approximately between rounds 6 and 7.
3. Sew the legs onto the body.
Tail:
1. Pin the tail onto the back of the body.
2. Sew the tail into place.
You now have your finished Persephone! If you have any questions or concerns please
email me at sweetoddityart@gmail.com or etsy convo me. I will get back to you asap.
Please share your finished Persephone with me as often as you want! I love seeing
them!
Sweet Oddity Art 22
Helpful Tips:
Exact Colors and Brand of Yarn Used:
1. Black: I love this yarn Black
2. White: I love this yarn White
3. Gray: I love this yarn light gray
You can use different eye and nose sizes. You might have to adjust the placements if you
change the sizes.
You can use different hook sizes and weights of yarn. It will just change the size of your dog and
you might need to adjust eye and nose placement.
How you stuff matters! The type of stuffing you use, how you stuff, all this matters on how your
dog turns out. I prefer Polyfil stuffing but you can use other types.
