Spring Bunny Amigurumi;https://www.lovecrafts.com/en-gb/p/spring-bunny-amigurumi-crochet-pattern-by-heidi;"Abbreviations and Stitches Used:
Ch=chain
FO=fasten off
Sc=single crochet
r= round
Sl st=slip stitch
St = stitch (es)
sc2tog = sc 2 stitches together as one
How-To Decrease: sc2tog (sc decrease) Insert hook into st and draw up a loop. Insert hook into next st and
draw up a loop. Yarn over, draw through all 3 loops on hook. One decrease made.
 Pattern Directions: This pattern is made in the round. Do not join at the end of each row;
just keep working moving your stitch marker at the end of each round. Keep your stitches
close together so that no filling shows through. You will do yourself a huge favor by
counting your stitches after each round.
 After each decrease stitch, pull the stitch tight so it’s closer together. Use the stitch marker
at the beginning of each round to keep your place.
 For all pieces that will be stuffed, you need to push your work inside out so your tail is
inside after the first couple of rounds– pull tail tight as needed, keeping your tail out of the
way while you work. This will keep your piece with the right side out.
Gauge Notes
This pattern doesn’t specify a gauge. For stuffed animals / parts, you don’t need to be too picky about exact
sizing. The most important thing is that you use a hook size that creates a nice looking fabric for your yarn. If
you use the recommended hook size, and your fabric looks very loose (so that stuffing would show through or
there are big holes in your work), then you will want to use a smaller hook. Don’t overstuff, just enough so
your toy is plump and squishy. Squeeze to shape a little, pushing all around so the stuffing is even. Other than
that, no measuring required!
Remember that each project will have its own look because each is handmade. Don’t stress out if it’s not
“perfect” or doesn’t look exactly like the picture. Yours is an original creation.  Hope you enjoy! Heidi
