Assembling Stick
Pin the various items to the head/body to gather a pre-view of your ami.
This first phase aims to find the right position of each
item, it does not have to be perfect. You will adjust the
items as you sew them on.
More instructions where to place each item are
provided below.
The eyes are placed with the pupils towards the top, at round 9 from the top head, 3 stitches apart.
When you are happy with the position of the eyes, sew them in place with invisible stitches (find
instructions in Basic Stitches in the appendix). Fill them with fibrefill before completely sewing the eyes.
2016 ©MarysAmiland
Mary’s Amiland 6
Stick The Ami
Next find the right position of the nose. Place it
slightly below the eyes in the centre.
When you are happy with the position of the
nose sew it in place.
Now place the arms with the thumb along the body on the inner side, 16 rounds from the top of the
head. When you are happy with the position of arms sew them in place.
Note: ensure that the arms are placed at the
same level.
Place the ears on the top of the head, close to the centre, a few stitches apart.
Check that both ears are at the
same distance from the eyes.
When you are happy with the
position of the ears, sew them in
place.
Tip: put “v” stitches on the back where the colour changes are so to disguise them a bit.
Congratulations, you have completed Stick The Ami!
2016 ©MarysAmiland
