Super Simple Santa Stuffy crochet pattern
Toy stuffing
What you need to get started ... Stitch marker and pins
Sewing needle
This super simple santa stuffy is just that: a cute and jolly
santa amigurumi that’s fun and fast to make. Sit him on For optional alternative version:
your desk, hang him from your tree, or give him to a
friend! Follow the alternative instructions to create an 10mm white button
opening at the bottom to turn your ornament into a gift Small organza or plastic bag to hold filling
bag for candies or other treats which are “stuffed” inside
santa’s tummy!
The pattern is made using mostly double crochet stitches,
worked in the round in the amigurumi method (in Terminology, special stitches
continuous spirals without joining the end of each round
and notes
with a ss), with simple colour changes, and finished with
an embroidered face. It uses small amounts of yarn only,
This pattern uses UK terms
so it’s ideal for using up your yarn stash.
