DDDDeeeessssccccrrrriiiippppttttiiiioooonnnn::::
This pattern makes a cute little angel about 12.5 cm high with a potpourri tummy to bring lovely smells and smiles to
wherever she sits. The potpourri is added through an opening created at the bottom of the angel which is closed with a
small button (the filling can be changed and refreshed at any time). Alternatively, the angel can be filled with toy
stuffing, like a traditional amigurumi, or other fillings like sweets, for a gift. The wings are hand sewn from cotton fabric.
Tenshi-chan’s hair style, embellishments, colour schemes and filling can be customised in many ways, to discover her
individual personality!
MMMMaaaatttteeeerrrriiiiaaaallllssss::::
• 3.25 mm and 3.5 mm crochet hooks • Stocking or small organza draw string bag (10 x
• Stitch markers 8 cm) for the potpourri
• Blunt end needle for weaving in ends • Small quantity (about 5g) of potpourri
• Pair 9 mm black safety eyes • Small piece ribbon for embellishing the hair
• 20 x 25 cm piece of cotton fabric for wings • 10 mm button
• 20 x 25 cm piece lightweight iron on interfacing • White cotton sewing thread and hand sewing
• Small amount of pink felt for cheeks (and clear needle
drying fabric craft glue for attaching)
• Small amount polyester toy stuffing • <50g Cotton 4 ply/DK yarn in cream (head)
• <50g Cotton 4ply/DK yarn in white (body)
• <50g Acrylic DK/sport yarn in brown (hair)
