THE EGG;https://www.lovecrafts.com/en-gb/p/the-egg-crochet-pattern-by-christin-kimsey;;"THE EGG
Size Approximate size in DK/3 mm hook (worsted/3.5 mm hook)
XS 4 cm/1.6 inch (5.5 cm/2.2 inch)
S 5.5 cm/2.1 inch (7 cm/2.8 inch)
M 7 cm/2.8 inch (8.5 cm/3.3 inch)
L 8 cm/3.3 inch (9.5 cm/3.7 inch)
Abbreviation (American crochet terms): sc = single crochet, inc = increase, dec = decrease, sts = stitches
For invisible decreases insert hook into front loops of two stitches, yarn over and pull through both loops.
Now you have two loops on the hook. Yarn over and pull through both loops on the hook. Fill the egg with
toy stuffing. To close the egg, cut the yarn after second last round and draw through the loop on the hook
and thread yarn on darning needle. Insert needle in front loop of next stitch from outside to inside and draw
yarn through, repeat for all stitches (6 in total) and draw yarn tight to close hole. Insert needle into the center
of the ring coming out on the side of the egg and pull through. Now sew in the yarn and cut off the end.
UNI
Uni colored eggs are worked in spirals. They can be decorated with cross stitch pattern.
