THE PIG | CATNAP CROCHET
This pattern uses US terminology.
All decreases in this pattern use the invisible decrease method, which I’d highly
recommend using. Some pieces are worked with TWO strands of yarn together. You
can do this by taking the strand on the outside of the skein and the one which comes
from the inside of the skein together. Crochet with two strands the same way you
would crochet if you had only one. This will yield a bigger plush faster and with less
effort than crocheting with only one strand. Unless stated otherwise, everything is
crocheted in continuous rounds, in a spiral. No need to close each row with a slip
stitch. Crochet with tight stitches, using a smaller hook to avoid holes.
This pattern is property of @catnapcrochet. You may not alter, copy, sell, or redistribute this
pattern or any part of it.
If you decide to post any photos of your creations made with this pattern, I would love for
you to tag me (@catnapcrochet) on TikTok/Instagram/YouTube) so I can see and share!
DISCLAIMER: If you find any mistakes, or have any questions, please feel free to reach out to
me via email or dm (crochetcatnap@gmail.com). I am happy to help with whatever
questions you may have, and I will be updating this pattern as necessary if I find any
corrections need to be made! Thank you for your patience.
TIP: If you find any of the directions unclear, try copy & pasting them into Chat GPT and it
can help explain the instructions more in depth. Otherwise feel free to reach out to me.
THE PIG | CATNAP CROCHET
MAKE 2
using 2 strands of yarn, 3.5mm hook
R1: MC 6sc using black yarn (6)
R2: 6inc (12)
R3: (1sc, 1inc) x 6 (18)
R4-5: 18sc around (18)
R6-7: Color change to navy, 18sc around (18)
R8: (2sc, 1dec) x 4, 2sc (14)
R9: (5sc, 1dec) x 2 (12)
R10: (1sc, 1dec) x 4 (8)
R11-12: fill with some stuffing, 8sc (8)
R13: Close with 4sc
Make sure to cut off enough yarn for sewing later
MAKE 2
using 2 strands of yarn, 3.5mm hook
R1: MC 5sc using peach yarn (5)
R2: 5inc (10)
R3-4: 10sc (10)
R5-9: Color change to maroon, continue 10sc (10)
R10: Close with 5sc
Make sure to cut off enough yarn for sewing later
THE PIG | CATNAP CROCHET
using 1 strand of peach yarn, 3mm hook
R1: ch5, sc in 2nd chain from hook, 2sc, 3sc in next stitch
to go around, 2sc, 1inc (10)
R2: 1inc, 2sc, (inc x 3), 2sc, (inc x 2) (16)
R3: sc around BLO (16) and ss in next stitch & fasten off
using 1 strand of black yarn, 3mm hook
R1: ch10, start in 2nd from hook, (8sc, 1 triple inc), repeat
(8sc, 1 triple inc) around the other side of the chain (22)
R2: 1ss in the next stitch BLO, (ch25, start in 2nd from hook,
1sc, 23 hdc, 1ss BLO to next stitch)
R3: (ch30, start in 2nd from hook, 1sc, 28hdc, end with 1ss
BLO in next stitch) x18 strands.
R4: For the last strand repeat R2 with a ch25, ending with a ss. Add more
strands if you find the hair doesn’t fit around the entire head, this may
depend on the yarn you’re using
MAKE 2
using 1 strand of yarn, 3mm hook
R1: MC 6sc (6)
R2: (1sc, 1inc) x3 (9)
R3: (2sc, 1inc) x3 (12)
R4: (3sc, 1 inc) x3 (15)
R5: sc around (15)
R6: (3sc, 1dec) x3 (12)
R7: (2sc, 1dec) x3 (9)
R8: sc around (9), ss in the next stitch, leave long yarn for sewing later
