THE PIG | CATNAP CROCHET
using 1 strand of maroon yarn, 3mm hook
The jacket is crocheted as a vest and simply put onto the pig
after the arms have been sewed in.
R1: ch27, start in 2nd from hook, 26 HDC, ch1 and turn
R2-R3: 26 HDC, ch1 and turn
R4: 4 HDC, ch 9, ss into 9th stitch away from where you initially started the
chain, 21 HDC, ch1 and turn (this creates the arm hole)
R5-9: 26 HDC, ch1 and turn
R10: Repeat R4 to create the other arm hole, making sure this fits around the
size of your pig’s torso (otherwise add more/less rows, this may depend on
the size of the wool you are using)
R11-13: 26 HDC, ch1 and turn
Finally neaten it up by simply sc all around and ss to end
& Extras
Leg/Arm Cuffs: (optional) simply chain some leg and arm cuffs and stitch to
arms and legs (this is optional) for more dimension
Knife: I sewed the optional knife to the hand
Nose: Embroider 2 lines with black yarn to resemble the nostrils
Sewing the body parts: I sewed the body parts as I went along:
- I sewed the legs on the bottom near to the center
- I sewed the arms just under where the neck starts, one on either side.
- I sewed the ears on top of the head between some of the front hair strands
- I sewed the hair to the head, leaving a strand or two in front of the ears and
not sewing the end of the strands and instead leaving them hanging off
