Abbrevation
Ch : chain
Sc : single crochet
Inc: increase
Hdc : half double crochet
Dec: decrease
St: stitch
Head :
R1 : Magic ring 6 (6)
R2 : Inc in each st , repeat 6 times (12)
R3 : (1sc, inc) repeat 6 times (18)
R4 : (2sc, inc) repeat 6 times (24)
R5 : (3sc, inc) repeat 6 times (30)
R6 : (5sc , inc) repeat 5 times (35)
R7- 10 : sc in each st (35)
R11 : (4 sc, dec) repeat 5 times , 5 sc in next st (30)
R12 : (3sc , dec) repeat 6 times (24)
R13 : (2 sc , dec) repeat 6 times . Fasten off and cut the yarn
Snout
R1 : Magic ring 6
R2 : Inc in each st (12)
R3 : sc in each st (12). Fasten off leave tail for sewing.
Body
R1 : Magic ring 6 (6)
R2 : inc in each st (12)
R3 : (sc , inc) repeat 6 times (18)
R4 : (2 sc , inc) repeat 6 times (24)
R5- 8 : sc in each st (24)
R9 : orange 11sc |cream 2sc | orange 11sc (24)
R10 : orange 10sc | cream 4sc | orange 10sc (24)
R11 : orange 3sc , dec, 4 sc| cream sc ,2 dec ,sc | orange 4sc, dec,3 sc (20)
R12 : (2 sc, dec) repeat 5 times (15). Fasten off, leave tail for sewing.
Hand (make 2)
R1 : magic ring 6 (6)
R2-7 : sc in each st (6). Fasten off and leave tail for sewing.
Legs (make 2)
R1 : Magic ring 6 (6)
R2 : (inc , sc ) repeat 3 times (9)
Tail
R1 : Magic ring 4 (4)
R2 -12 : sc in each st (4). Fasten off and leave tail for sewing .
Ear (make 2)
Row 1 : ch 5
Row 2 : (start from the second ch from hook) sc 4, then ch 1
Row 3 : sc, dec, sc , then ch 1
Row 4 : sc , dec , then ch 1
Row 5 : dec . Then fasten off.";Lovecrafts
1 Llama Lou Crochet;https://www.lovecrafts.com/en-gb/p/tiniest-astronaut-crochet-pattern-by-llama-lou-crochet;"Abbreviations
This pattern is written in US crochet terminology
• sl st = slip stitch
• sc = single crochet
• hdc = half double crochet
• inc = increase by making 2 sts in the same stitch
• dec = decrease by crocheting 2 sts together
• FLO = crochet through the front loop only
• BLO = crochet thought the back loop only
I’d love to see what you’ve made!
Find me at:
Email: llamaloucrochet@hotmail.com
Ravelry: www.ravelry.com/designers/alyssa-voznak
Etsy: www.etsy.com/shop/LlamaLouCrochet
Instagram: www.instagram.com/llamaloucrochet/
©Alyssa Voznak, 2024. Pattern may not be resold or redistributed without permission. Items made from
this pattern may be sold in small quantities, with credit given to me as the designer
4 Llama Lou Crochet
How To Fasten Off Invisibly
1. Cut the yarn and pull the end out of the final stitch.
2. Skip one stitch to the left, and use a needle to pull the tail from front to back through both loops
of the next stitch.
3. Thread the tail back down through the top of the final stitch (between the front and back loops).
4. Adjust the newly created loop so it matches the tops of the stitches to either side of it. Secure
the remaining end on the inside of the piece (unless instructed otherwise).
Helmet
Round 1: with Color 1, sc 6 in a Magic Ring– 6 sts
Round 2: inc 6 times– 12 sts
Round 3: (sc in next st, inc) 6 times– 18 sts
Round 4: (sc in next st, inc, sc in next st) 6 times– 24 sts
Round 5: (sc in next 3 sts, inc) 6 times– 30 sts
Round 6-11: sc in each st– 6 rounds
Round 12: (sc in next 3 sts, dec) 6 times– 24 sts
Begin stuffing the Helmet.
Round 13: (sc in next st, dec) 8 times– 16 sts
Round 14: in the BLO, (dec) 8 times– 8 sts
Cut yarn and draw the end through the front loops of Round 14. Pull tight and knot to close.
Weave in the end.
©Alyssa Voznak, 2024. Pattern may not be resold or redistributed without permission. Items made from
this pattern may be sold in small quantities, with credit given to me as the designer
5 Llama Lou Crochet
Visor
With Color 2, ch 6
Round 1: sc in next 4 sts, sc 3 in next st.
Rotate and work in the bottom of the
foundation chain: sc in next 3 sts, inc in next
st– 12 sts
Round 2: inc in next st, sc in next 3 sts, inc in
next 3 sts, sc in next 3 sts, inc in next st, sc in
next st– 17 sts
Fasten off using the invisible
method, leaving a long tail for
seaming.
Legs
(make 2)
Round 1: with Color 2, sc 6 in a Magic Ring– 6 sts
Round 2: (sc in next st, inc, sc in next st) 2 times– 8 sts
Round 3: sc in each st
Switch to Color 3
Round 4: (sc in next 3 sts, inc) 2 times– 10 sts
Round 5-6: sc in each st– 2 rounds
For the first leg, fasten off. Do not fasten off the second leg; instead, sc in next 2 sts (this will
help hide the colors changes) then continue on to the Body:
Body
Round 1: sc in next 10 sts of the First
Leg, sc in next 10 sts of the Second Leg–
20 sts
Place a stitch marker in the first
stitch made in the First Leg. This
is now the first stitch of the round.
Round 2-5: sc in each st– 4 rounds
Round 6: (sc in next 4 sts, dec, sc in next
4 sts) 2 times– 18 sts
Round 7: sc in each st
Round 8: (sc in next 7 sts, dec) 2 times– 16 sts
Round 9: sc in each st
Fasten off using the invisible method, leaving a long tail for seaming.
©Alyssa Voznak, 2024. Pattern may not be resold or redistributed without permission. Items made from
this pattern may be sold in small quantities, with credit given to me as the designer
6 Llama Lou Crochet
Arms
(make 2)
Round 1: with Color 2, sc 6 in a Magic Ring– 6 sts
Round 2: sc in each st
Switch to Color 3
Round 3-5: sc in each st– 3 rounds
Flatten the opening so that the
stitches on both sides line up.
Round 6: sc 3 through both layers.
Fasten off with a long tail for seaming.
Finishing
With the fastened-off tail of the legs to close up the gap
between them. Stuff the legs and the body.
Attach the helmet to the opening of the body, using the front
loops of Round 13 as a guide (I prefer to go around the post
of the stitch rather than use the front loop itself). If necessary,
add more stuffing to the neck before closing
Attach the arms to either side of the body at Round 8.
Attach the visor to the helmet between Round 7-11, centered
above the arms.
With a scrap of Color 2, embroider a zipper by making two
long stitches down the front of body and two buttons using
cross stitches beside it.
Congratulations on your
finished astronaut!
