Tiny magic frog
Materials Size Difficulty
> Cotton DK yarn in 4 cm / 1.5"" tall if made using the
Dark green suggested materials
* It’s a Bonus Free Pattern to
Light green
stretch your fingers and oil your
Light yellow Construction
crochet wand before the official
Lilac Worked in one piece starting from
start of Amigurumi School of
> 2.5 to 3 mm crochet hook the top of the head, with arms
Magic 5!
> black embroidery thread or and legs made as you go.
small safety eyes or black beads
> toy stuffing
> tapestry needle
Instructions
Make in dark green or your preferred colour.
Rnd 1: start 6sc in a magic ring [6]
Rnd 2: inc 6 times [12] 1 2 3
Rnd 3: (3sc, 5dc in next st) repeat 2 times, 4sc
[20] {img 1-2}
Rnd 4: 1sc, inc, 15sc, inc, 2sc [22]
Rnd 5: sc in all 22 st [22]
Rnd 6: 5sc, inc, 10sc, inc, 5sc [24]
4 5 6
Next round adds the arms.
Rnd 7: 7sc, ch5 {img 3}, slst in second ch from
hook {img 4}, (ch1, slst in same ch) 3 times {img 5},
3slst along the ch {img 6}, 11sc, ch5, slst in second
ch from hook, (ch1, slst in same ch) 3 times, 3slst
along the ch, 6sc [24 + 2 arms] {img 7}
Rnd 8: sc in all 24 st, folding the arms to the front 7 8 9
of the work [24] {img 8}
Next round adds the legs.
Rnd 9: 4sc, ch8 {img 9}, slst in second ch from
hook, (ch1, slip in same ch) 3 times {img 10}, 3slst
along the ch, 3sc along the chain {img 11}, 1sc in 10 11 12
same st as last sc along the main round, 18sc, ch8,
slst in second ch from hook, (ch1, slip in same ch)
3 times, 3slst along the ch, 3sc along the chain, 1sc
in same st as last sc along the main round, 2sc
[26 + 2 legs] {img 12}
