Rnd 10: 4sc, fold the leg to the front of the work, 13 14 15
ch1 behind the leg, 19sc, fold the next leg to the
front of the work, ch1 behind the leg, 3sc [28] {img
13-14}
Rnd 11: 4sc, 1sc into the chain, 19sc, 1sc into the
chain, 3sc [28]
Note: If you want to use small safety eyes instead of
16 17 18
beads or embroidery add them now.
Rnd 12: (inv dec, 2sc) repeat 7 times [21]
Rnd 13: (1sc, inv dec) repeat 7 times [14]
Poke up the eye stitches (the 5dc on round 3) and
add toy stuffing {img 15}.
Rnd 14: inv dec 7 times [7]
19 20 21
Fasten off, pick up all the front loops with a tapestry
needle and pull tight to close {img 16-17}.
Use the same yarn tail to sew down the feet, folding
the longer legs and sewing down the toes, and
securing the arms on an angle towards the tummy
{img 18}. 22 23 24
Use a tail of light yellow to embroider the eyes
making horizontal stitches over the dc stitches
of round 3 to create an oval shape {img 19-20}.
Then use the black embroidery thread to make an
horizontal stitch in the middle {img 21}. With the
same yarn tail to add a little mouth too.
Note: you can embroider the eyes in a different way
or use black beads. Make the mouth pointing upward,
downward or asymmetrical. Pick the style that fits
your Tiny Frog mood!
Use a tail of lilac to embroider two little cheeks
below the eyes to complete the work {img 122-23}.
optional: Add some speckles on the back
making short straight stitches and/or french knots
using light yellow and light green yarn {img
24}.
