Sweet Oddity Art 7
Assembly
Head and Body:
1. Sew the head to the body. You may need to add more stuffing as you sew.
2. Take a long strand of white yarn and thread your needle. Insert the needle into a hole
in between the eyes. Bring the needle to the lower corner of the eye. Wrap the needle
around the outside of the eye. Insert the needle into a hole on the top of the eye.
Pull a little tightly to create a highlight for the eye. Repeat for the 2nd eye.
Sweet Oddity Art 8
Muzzle:
1. Pin the muzzle onto the face between the eyes. Yes, you stuff the muzzle. The muzzle
will start approximately between rounds 8 and 9.
2. Sew the muzzle onto the face.
Arms:
1. Pin the arms onto the body approximately between rounds 14 and 15.
2. Sew the arms onto the body.
Sweet Oddity Art 9
Ears and Horn:
1. Pin the ears on top of the head.
2. Sew the ears onto the head.
3. Pin the horn onto the head in front of the ears.
4. Sew the horn onto the head.
Sweet Oddity Art 10
Hair:
1. Pin a piece of the mane behind the horn going down the back of the head.
2. Sew the piece onto the head. Pin the 2nd piece underneath the 1st. Sew onto the head.
3. Wrap the tail into a circle and sew the top shut. Pin the tail onto the back of the body.
Sew the tail onto the body.
Sweet Oddity Art 11
Sweet Oddity Art 12
Extras:
1. Add some blush to the cheeks if you want with actual blush or pink crayon.
You have your finished Unicorn! Thank you for your purchase! If you have any questions or
concerns please email me at sweetoddityart@gmail.com or etsy convo me. I will get back to
you asap. Please share your finished unicorn with me as often as you want! I love seeing them!
