-The end will be an invisible finish used for CLOSED pieces. The steps are broken down
in steps a through c.
Invisible Finish - Closed
(this method is for CLOSED pieces)
Step a: Cut the yarn and pull up on the hook, drawing your yarn out from your last stitch.
Step b: Thread the yarn onto a dull yarn needle and insert the needle through the next 2
FRONT LOOPS ONLY. Pull yarn through. Repeat to complete the round. Pull the yarn tight to
close.
Step c: Weave through the last round to secure the end and pull tight again. Hide the loose end
through the middle of the invisible finish and inside of your finished piece.
Completing Other Leg
E/9-3.5mmHook
CherryRed(RedHeart)
* While holding the body upside down, look at the side of the body, with the unworked leg
opening facing you. The stitch marker on the left will be the first stitch of round 1.
Create a slip knot on your hook and insert into the stitch. Make sure you are working
from the outside with the hook. Your hook should be facing into the leg hole (making the
other stitch marker your next stitch). Try to keep your stitch tight when going to the other
marker. It’s a tight squeeze and there still may be a gap.
1 - 6. Sc around (18)
7. (Sc, dec) around (12)
8. Sc around (12)
* Stuff leg and finish off with an invisible finish for CLOSED pieces. Refer to the
instructions for the invisible finish of the first leg for the steps and visual reference.
* If there is a gap, you can use a scrap piece of Cherry Red yarn and loop a couple of
stitches together around the gap. Pull tight to close, tie off yarn and hide end through
the body.
Completing Arms
E/9-3.5mmHook
CherryRed(RedHeart)
* Both arms are worked the same way. Working the arms begin very similarly to the
second leg. While holding the body upside down, look at the side of the body, with the
chosen unworked arm opening facing you. The stitch marker on the left will be the first
stitch of round 1. Create a slip knot on your hook and insert into the stitch. Make sure
you are working from the outside with the hook. Your hook should be facing into the arm
hole (making the other stitch marker your next stitch). Try to keep your stitch tight when
going to the other marker. It’s a tight squeeze again, but you can fix any gap in the same
way as the leg gap.
1 - 2. Sc around (12)
3. (Sc, inc) around (18)
4. Sc around (18)
5. (Sc, dec) around (12)
* Stuff arm and finish off with an invisible finish for CLOSED pieces. Refer to the
instructions for the invisible finish of the first leg for the steps and visual reference.
Assembly of the Devil
Connecting the Eyes
- Pin the buttons first onto the head, with the bottom of the eyes lined up with each other.
The top of the bigger button will be between rounds 8 and 9 of the head. 3 stitches
separate the 2 buttons from each other.
- Using a scrap piece of Cherry Red yarn, insert hook through top of head and through a
button hole to begin. Sew eye on in an x pattern, leaving the beginning tail of the yarn
hanging out from the top of the head still.
- When you get to the last button hole, insert hook through the button hole, through the
head, and back out through the top of the head. Both ends of the scrap piece of yarn
should be coming out of the same hole. Tie together two ends tightly. Using a needle,
send both ends back through the body through that same little hole the ends are coming
from. Exit needle somewhere else on the head, pull the ends tightly to pull the knot
inside the head. Cut ends and eye is done. Repeat the steps for the other eye as well.
Connecting the Horns
- The horns are placed on top of the head. Looking at the side of the body and head,
horns should be even with the arms. Looking at the top of the head, each horn will be
about 3 rows from the top center of the head. Both of the long ends should be coming
out from the right side of the horns, when looking at the face. Sew the horns into place.
Connecting the Heart
- The heart is connected centered on the chest, just below the neck crease. Using a
scrap piece of Black yarn on a needle, insert the needle through the back of the body
and through the center of the heart. Leave the beginning tail hanging out the back of the
body. Sew around the posts of the stitches, all around the heart. On the last stitch, exit
the needle out the same hole that the beginning tail is hanging from. Tie off the two
ends together. Thread both ends of a needle and pass the needle back through the
same hole the ends are coming from. Exit the needle elsewhere on the body, pull the
ends to pull the knot inside the body. Cut ends.
Connecting the Tail
- The tail is connected on the rear end, just above the leg gap. The long connecting tail
should be coming from the underside of the tail.
The Valentine Devil is done!! Congratulations!
