all you have to do is look into the pages of Wishweaver.
About
Julianne Hildebrand Winter (pen name, J.H. Winter) is an author/illustrator based out of the Pacific Northwest.
She is a member of SCBWI, writing fantasy books for children, from picture books all the way to illustrated
chapter books and middle grade.
Set for release in September 2020, comes J.H. Winter’s debut chapter book series, Tales of Whimsy, about an orb
spider named Whimsy who, in her first adventure, goes in search of answers as to what happened to the
Wishweaver. Wishweaver is heavily-illustrated and will see art adorning nearly every spread!
When Julianne isn’t writing or illustrating, she is crafting up original crocheted amigurumi (plush toys) and C2C
graphgans to share as free patterns on her blog, Ink & Stitches. She currently teaches how to crochet amigurumi
through her many how-to videos on her Ink & Stitches YouTube Channel, and enjoys any opportunity to help
others learn the craft.
